uy who tortured my character has to be in the agme so i could get to him and kkill himfor instance,a character has to have someone present to take his revenge in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:57:19-07:00","id":608418,"title":"","content":"Probably for the same reason that a Promethean game without redemption would feel incomplete? It would lack some kind of ending I suppose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:17:40-07:00","id":608427,"title":"","content":"I didn't know how badly I wanted David Cronenberg: The Role-Playing Game. <i>Thank you</i>, Onyx Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:39:50-07:00","id":608446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608417#post608417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it'd be incomplete like if i create character who wants to find the guy who hurt him and take his revenge,the guy who tortured my character has to be in the agme so i could get to him and kkill himfor instance,a character has to have someone present to take his revenge in</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says that it <i>must</i> be achievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:44:01-07:00","id":608450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608418#post608418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably for the same reason that a Promethean game without redemption would feel incomplete? It would lack some kind of ending I suppose</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it <i>must</i> have an ending. IMO, hardwiring such a thing into the rules would reduce the chronicle options that are open to storytellers and troupes. These are RPGs, that there is some kind of &quot;victory condition&quot; should be a preference of the group playing the game and not something mandated in the rules (option to have = good, necessity to have = bad).<br /> <br /> Good RPGs lend themselves to multiple kinds of storytelling. It gives them good replayability. Note that I'm not saying that it shouldn't have it, only that it shouldn't <b><i>only</i></b> have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:55:59-07:00","id":608460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608418#post608418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably for the same reason that a Promethean game without redemption would feel incomplete? It would lack some kind of ending I suppose</div> </div> </div> </div>I worry it's a Reclamation issue, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:00:13-07:00","id":608467,"title":"","content":"You know, my immediate reaction was a raised eyebrow and then a sigh. But then I looked at that trailer for &quot;Tetsuo: The Iron Man&quot; and something clicked for me. Something horrible in a way that other NWOD games have not managed to do until now. While rather cheesy in editing, that trailer contained images which were full of such dark meanings to me that I physically moved backwards and considered closing the tab. But my curiosity was stronger. And I started wondering.<br /> <br /> This might be a mini game line focused on a contemporary yet timeless fear. A very real one. Fear of Other Humans.<br /> <br /> What they did to you cannot be properly described, not even with the sum vocabulary and imagery of all horror fiction. Their cruelty was so without limits that it changed you in a way that lacks the undertones of grandiose pledges in Changeling, and the romantic desire for a better tomorrow in Promethean. They didn't Hurt you to survive or prosper, no matter what they say. They did it because they wanted to. That's it.<br /> <br /> Right now, in the real world, there are lives being snuffed out or ruined to fuel the purposeless existence of a Big Fucking Nothing: banks, corporations, government. It's either carry their bloodstained, golden palaces on your shoulders, or be thrown out into the Streets And Alleys, where Deviants are made. The threat of unemployment and banishment is no longer a cautionary tale about the intrinsic rewards of being a good person, only about avoiding yet more agony. You drag yourself, day after day after GODDAMN DAY, with only more of the same awaiting you before the real reward: the numb embrace of worms. You are lucky to go out before the rest, but there are still untold masses suffering as slaves, in one way or another.<br /> <br /> The supreme deity of the cosmos is simply Pain. There is no escaping it, now or ever.<br /> <br /> You were doomed to this billions of years ago, as will those Deviants that come after you.<br /> <br /> The best you can hope for is the Little Death that follows the rapturous sharing of your Pain, and pray that It will avert its gaze for longer the next era.<br /> <br /> Deviant: The Roaring. A storytelling game of Broken Laws and Fading Hope.<br /> <br /> (Important Disclaimer Below)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I am sorry if I freaked anyone out with my feverish synopsis. I was probably caught up in my imagination and psychological hang ups and used the resulting inspiration to write a description of an NWOD game that would be scary for <b>me</b>. I do realize that a game where it is said 9 out of 10 times in the manual that you can't make the tiniest difference would become comically edgy without a careful touch indeed. Comparisons to Wraith: The Oblivion would be extremely hard to overcome. However, in the off chance that I managed to run or participate in a Deviant chronicle that does it <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>just</i></span> right, it would be cathartic beyond description.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,