e.<br /> <br /> I'll throw in Raven of the Teen Titans as another thing it makes me think of. I overlooked the obvious Wolverine, though perhaps because he's less linked to horror despite his actions. Everyone else from Project X though, they got some awful stories.<br /> <br /> DV8 probably sticks closest to the new World of Darkness themes, though.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://d1466nnw0ex81e.cloudfront.net/n_iv/600/997957.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am thrilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-30-2015, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T20:20:33-07:00","id":608811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608793#post608793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think assuming any given reference to fire refers to the Divine Fire is sloppy thinking that results in people attributing qualities to the Principle that it does not possess and shorts an entire axis of imagery out in multiple gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense! Hell, I've heard the term &quot;A hunger like fire&quot; to describe the Kindred condition and I'm <i>sure </i>that the Blood's transmutative traits can be directly linked to the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Now with that mystery solved, I am going to attempt to hammer in this weird looking nail (I mean come on. Who designs a nail with these weird things on the side?) into a wooden frame. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T20:46:34-07:00","id":608827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608811#post608811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nonsense! Hell, I've heard the term &quot;A hunger like fire&quot; to describe the Kindred condition and I'm <i>sure </i>that the Blood's transmutative traits can be directly linked to the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Now with that mystery solved, I am going to attempt to hammer in this weird looking nail (I mean come on. Who designs a nail with these weird things on the side?) into a wooden frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay i was probably wrong about the divine fire,but if by any chance i am right about it i would like you to pick up that Phone<br /> <i>Because i totally called it. </i>y'know.. jsut in case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T23:56:24-07:00","id":609003,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that the 'splat' that defines the type of group or organization that met them is somewhat vague by nature, but then gives you examples from existing gamelines as to potential sources if you want to draw from them, like the cheiron group, ordo dracul, demonic agencies, and other countless, more obscure examples in the books. However, it should also give the info needed to not use any of those at all and to build from scratch.<br /> <br /> Granted, depending on the mechanics of how this creation works, it may or may not be outside the capabilities of existing splats to do, dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:36:26-07:00","id":609021,"title":"","content":"The name isn't doing it for me. I am holding off on forming any strong opinion yet as Beast did not entice me either. It feels more like an aspect of the NWoD better covered by an extended set of supplements than a line but I'm going to wait and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:41:38-07:00","id":609043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609021#post609021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name isn't doing it for me. I am holding off on forming any strong opinion yet as Beast did not entice me either. It feels more like an aspect of the NWoD better covered by an extended set of supplements than a line but I'm going to wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Name is Making me think of just calling them &quot;The Artists&quot; Because DeviantArt is forever linked too that name for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:43:16-07:00","id":609052,"title":"","content":"So. In regards to fire burning within you, here's an idea that I had.<br /> <br /> <i>Condition:</i> <b>Fire of Retribution</b><br /> <i>Type:</i> persistent<br /> <br /> <i>Effects:</i> Vengeance burns within you. Ever since you found yourself in this mess, it has never been far from your mind but now that you've taken your first steps it's more than just a thought. It's an urge. You go to sleep with it, you wake up to it, you eat, drink and breathe it. It gives you strength and resolve to see it through and makes it very difficult to focus on doing anything but exacting retribution.<br /> <br /> While you are pursuing vengeance in the most direct way possible, gain +1 to all dice pools and have one less wound penalty (applies only in combat). For example, the dice pool bonus would apply to all combat rolls while trying to put down your target, but also more subtle actions such as preparing explosives for an assault on the corporate headquarters, finding out where exactly your target within the build is located, or even analyzing floor plans to figure out how to get to the target once the chaos starts. However, it wouldn't apply to seducing his colleague to dig up dirt on him, tailing him for days to see his daily routine or making him confess once you get to him.<br /> <br /> Additionally, you need to pass a Resolve + Composure roll in order to focus on extended actions that make you stray from following leads towards the target of your vengeance. Having a non-vengeful breakfast or fixing your car is fine. Helping a friend renovate his house might fall into this category, depending on the circumstances and time spent (might be fine for an afternoon if you don't know where your target is, but certainly would require a roll if you know your target's address, you've already seen him home alone and you'd need to spend days working on the house). Stepping away from the target when you have him in your sights would always require this roll. Every subsequent roll is made with a cumulative -1 penalty if no steps towards following your vengeance have been made in between. In more abstract circumstance, the roll needs to be made once a day. Directly confronted with the target, roll is made once per round: you might want to immediately leave your target's presence if you don't want to attack him.<br /> <br /> <i>Resolution:</i> Once the vengeance is exacted, the condition is resolved. Other than that, significant efforts would need to be made by the character in order to resolve it peacefully which would best be left to ST and player to agree on for each individual case. Joining a Buddhist monastery for a couple of years might be one way. Having yourself committed to a mental institution for a while would be another. Increasing Integrity should probably be a component here.<br /> <br /> Beat: The fire inside you burns so bright and hot, it might be starting to consume you. While exacting vengeance in whatever way, each time your actions cause a Breaking Point, gain a beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T01:07:39-07:00","id":609084,"title":"","content":"You know, its interesting that people keep using the term &quot;limited line&quot; in regard to new lines. I thought part of the Onyx Path practice was that all lines are effectively open (a la the &quot;Big 3&quot;), and so will grow with time, but at a slower rate given their new scale. The full potential of Deviant, or any lines present and future, effectively takes years to unfold deliberately, or else risk running into the errors other products have had like 1. The line has little definition or appeal without more fleshing out (Promethean), 2. Popularity demands more releases for a property, reducing resources allocated elsewhere (Changeling), or 3. Trying to make the venture self-contained, where the premise is engaging but is left to exist in a relative conceptual vacuum (Geist). Allowing the material to be returned to at any time leaves for sporadic but continuing growth, which is a stronger base for a new edition of a game universe than many have a shot for.<br /> <br /> That said, I was not expecting Deviant to be our new perspective into the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It seems familiar in theme (at first glance, albeit) to several games which might already exist (in nWoD or not), but I think the most analogous example is found in a fansplat. RPG.net had a number of threads pertaining to fansplats over the years, one of which underwent an in-depth attempt and an abbreviated revival attempt some years ago. I believe these were known as Soldier: the Betrayed and Soldier: the Perfected, respectively. Here are the links: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?698948-Brainstorming-Soldier-The-Betrayed\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...r-The-Betrayed</a> ; <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?717255-(NWOD-Fan-Splat)-Soldier-the-Perfected\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...-the-Perfected</a> . I'm not stating I believe these ideas are the same, but that the fan creations have themes that closest match what Deviant might try to convey. I hope someone more informed or involved might weigh in on that matter.<br /> <br /> But analogous or no, thinking of Deviant from that perspective gives me some idea for what the game involves. These aren't mummies and prometheans, purpose built to pursue dead values of a deathless empire with life unending, or captured activation in a shell of old lives, seeking to define a more complete existence in their most immediate means. Perhaps the Deviants can be marked in death or can be dead, to a degree, but that doesn't define them. Perhaps they have drives and imperatives to accomplish, old code-words and conditioning that one day drive a grandmother to leave the children for hours so she can sift through dirt in the old woods until she finds wooden carvings of indeterminate make and great value. Or perhaps, so caught up in espionage and subterfuge for years, a change in the flow of the squamous gel where his stomach used to be sends a man out of observation for the first time, scattered and wary as he tries to determine the threat potential of people using library computers. But these shouldn't define what a Deviant must do. Likewise, these aren't changelings or demons, beings stolen and warped by unbound forces that only regain their agency by forcing their aberrance into some mold resembling their old selves, or ethereal occult programs divorced from their designer by building enough inborn contradiction to change their nature as concept machinations to something with comparable agency and grounded, variable capability. It's possible the child dreaming of basketball was abducted, and spent so many years being filled with wire and conductors he can't remember what it was like to have aspirations until he tore the cables out and broke into an old repair shop, crafting some mess out of what used to be fans and circuit boards to keep himself even. And it's possible there's some poor brat born of feeding tubes and fabricators, following endless trails in lights reflected from the mirror mazes that blend with its skin, until one day it finds a path too worn to be reflective and tunnels through the walls behind the mirrors, lurking in old sewers until it gets its bearings enough to finally see itself clearly for the first time through an old, shadowed puddle. Maybe those can define them, but it doesn't define a Deviant's struggle.<br /> <br /> .It's possible that what a Deviant is can best be seen in their utilization of their circumstances. These people, bent on finding their makers and halting their works are agents not because of their making or by their makers, but of their making. A mage dreams-lives an imprinting of the cosmos-symbolized into their souls and attains enlightenment, and a beast recoils from entrenched, matchless fear until their essence is the fear embodied, but Deviants are forged by a group that wants easy revelation by engineering or by forces less enigmatic than the truest terror and the rawest understanding. A sin-eater allows the spirit-ghost-incarnation the bond that binds them indistinguishably to create a living receptacle of all things death and life inseparable, as much the true lack of either for both hosts, and hunters elect to wade in the dark and find all things banal and necessary beyond the rest of his world but within it, but Deviants can only really choose when they've rent their control or at least, when the bargains not so sweet anymore.<br /> <br /> Vampires are made with agency and some even volunteer to become life ended but not forfeit, wresting others from and pooling in their very source of power and waking. Maybe the same decisions can be said of the Deviant or their makers, but they aren't bound to their old humanity and succor like these creatures are the vein, and their curses might well be more &quot;tangible&quot;. Werewolves are often born, and even when they aren't all erupt into avatars of union and change, the wolf/moon/human-spiritual avatars of urges-sanctified and boundaries-wielded. Maybe the Deviant is born with the proclivity for their creation or have this foisted upon them unheralded through horrid lottery, but the creation imparts no law for their kind, and they are beholden to no sire of theirs.<br /> <br /> To be deviant isn't a becoming or realization, nor is it the reconciling of the lot given to them. It is mastery: the reclaiming of the self to include what they took - what they earned - when others decided to inflict it upon them. Perhaps they didn't result in the purpose they were forged for, or perhaps they are promising beyond reckoning. But that no longer matters. That power's in the hands of the made, now.<br /> <br /> And the Deviant one will use that for their own ends to play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3708-amateur-hour","name":"Amateur Hour","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:48:09-07:00","id":609191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608793#post608793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think assuming any given reference to fire refers to the Divine Fire is sloppy thinking that results in people attributing qualities to the Principle that it does not possess and shorts an entire axis of imagery out in multiple gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=608811#post608811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense! Hell, I've heard the term &amp;quot;A hunger like fire&amp;quot; to describe the Kindred condition and I'm <i>sure </i>that the Blood's transmutative traits can be directly linked to the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Now with that mystery solved, I am going to attempt to hammer in this weird looking nail (I mean come on. Who designs a nail with these weird things on the side?) into a wooden frame. </div> </div> </div> </div>however, with the references to slabs and potential body horror? Mad science has netted us two games with a strong fire theme in each (Promethean and Demon). Coupled with the Promethean-esk body replacement immortal idea potentially being included, assuming that GM or DF is involved isn't a huge stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:00:08-07:00","id":609220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amateur Hour</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609084#post609084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, its interesting that people keep using the term &amp;quot;limited line&amp;quot; in regard to new lines. I thought part of the Onyx Path practice was that all lines are effectively open (a la the &amp;quot;Big 3&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and so will grow with time, but at a slower rate given their new scale.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the original model was that each line past the big three would be a limited, one year thing, then dropped. Changeling proved popular enough to break the mold, and then Hunter with Mortal Remains updates. <br /> <br /> Now, with 2e and new company, who knows? Either way, though? That is why we call new it a limited line, and we don't expect years to be involved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:06:14-07:00","id":609228,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm currently hoping the X-splat is going to be 'augmentation' (how you were changed) and the Y-splat will be your 'purpose' (what you were created to do). Although I can see purpose as the X-splat or only splat and the 'how' being flavour.<br /> <br /> I would love for the powers to all have a physical component. As long as something supernatural is going on I can see a cyber-augmented Deviant tinkering with his implants and adding new ones by instinct while a bio-augmented Deviant growing entirely new appendages and organs.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if it'll be called Deviant: the Evolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:10:59-07:00","id":609231,"title":"","content":"I don't think the focus is on what you are created for. You wake up abandoned somewhere, whatever your purpose may have been, it was either fulfilled or discarded in the prelude. So I feel the Y-splat would be more along the lines of how do you get your vengeance. Violence, discrediting, financial ruin, that sort of thing. Even that seems a bit thin, but I've got no other ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: although, now thinking about it, I'm completely wrong. It doesn't make much sense that you'd pick your violence as means of revenge if you weren't augmented to be capable of violence... so, yeah, I think I'd get behind purpose as a better idea to define who you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2050,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","user":"Dawngreeter","date":". 07-31-2015, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:22:17-07:00","id":609274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609191#post609191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">however, with the references to slabs and potential body horror? Mad science has netted us two games with a strong fire theme in each (Promethean and Demon). Coupled with the Promethean-esk body replacement immortal idea potentially being included, assuming that GM or DF is involved isn't a huge stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean and Demon aren't all mad science all the time; neither will Deviant be. I imagine there might be a sidebar about tying their torments into one of the other lines, but the odds of it being a central feature are only marginally above nil. <br /> <br /> Actually, I wonder if it have a default mechanism at all (by which I mean no analogue to Divine Fire or the Curse of Vampirism to be the default thing that powers the supernature of Deviants). A splat which is defined only by formative experiences, not by their quasibiology is something we've not had before, even in Hunter.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:52:52-07:00","id":609294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609274#post609274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean and Demon aren't all mad science all the time; neither will Deviant be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the former are. The alchemical underpinings of Promethean and quantum techgnosis of Demon flavor broad swipes of their entire games. Now, if we assume that Deviant uses a third variation of mad science for its mystical mechanism, its not a stretch to assume the luminous beings are related somehow. <br /> <br /> Don't know enough about Deviant to assume mad science yet, but if we did, the Divine Fire wouldn't be a stretch; that's all I'm saying. Deviant could include people transformed by spirit powers, ala the Purified in Immortals, for all I know, and in that case, I totally would agree that the DF would be bad. Actually, I'm pretty much betting that we're looking at The Cherion Group: the Game, so I'm expecting more transpants and grafting than I'm expecting anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:15:49-07:00","id":609309,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call it Chieron Group The Game if only because the main characters are the victims and targets of tampering, not the tamperers or those with agency over the changes.<br /> <br /> I'm personally not expecting much of transplants and grafting per se because those two things are very... external for the impression I'm from the blurb. It seems likely that the changes the Deviant have gone through will be more fundamental, even if they come from the same direction, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-31-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:07:29-07:00","id":609361,"title":"","content":"All I can really think of when I look at this is that episode of the X Files with the flashback to the Red Scare xenotransplantation story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:15:41-07:00","id":609365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609294#post609294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, the former are. The alchemical underpinings of Promethean and quantum techgnosis of Demon flavor broad swipes of their entire games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy and Gnosticism aren't all mad science all the time either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:20:36-07:00","id":609371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609309#post609309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call it Chieron Group The Game if only because the main characters are the victims and targets of tampering, not the tamperers or those with agency over the changes.<br /> <br /> I'm personally not expecting much of transplants and grafting per se because those two things are very... external for the impression I'm from the blurb. It seems likely that the changes the Deviant have gone through will be more fundamental, even if they come from the same direction, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, when I read the blurb about Deviant, I immediately thought of the Invisible Man, both the movie and the television series. In the latter case, the entire invisibility thing was done through a gland grafted onto the experimenter's brain, which caused physiological changes to the man in question. Secreting a quicksilver-like substance that made him bend light, causing him to slowly go insane with rage issues, working to track down the scientist who created the gland... <br /> <br /> All the fun body horror stuff that TCG is renowned for. I mean, obviously, there are going to be differences, since this won't be a game about hunters; it'll be a different focus, absolutely. But there's still a lot of similarity here. And who ever said that the TCG agents had full agency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:42:00-07:00","id":609429,"title":"","content":"I read the title Deviant, but thought of a totally different view of this. <br /> <br /> Deviant:The Ruination - You have slumbered for eons, now you awaken call upon by someone who dared to disturb the division of the natural and supernatural worlds. You are the entity someone has summoned and charged with a command that you must follow, but what they don't know is that you will not go back to sleep. Deviant is game of planing, manipulation, and escape. Are you smarter then those who enslaved you or will you be cast back into the endless slumber. <br /> <br /> Deviants come form the cosmology of the WOD, each one with their own traits and abilities, unleashed on the mortal world you the creature now has flesh and blood. Each player must work to completed the goal given to them in their own way but also must figure out how to escape the bonds before put back to sleep. Once free the Deviant can explore this new world, they can choose to walk among those of this world as one of them or as some monster. Beware those who know your truth for you are bound by commands of your true name, but that is not the only fear the Deviant has to worry about. The entities that they slumbered among some times seek them out to return to serve them instead of returning to slumber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:44:55-07:00","id":609431,"title":"","content":"@MCN: Fair enough! There is definitely some overlap, but the focus looks to be very different. Didn't mean to imply all altered Chieron agents and subjects who might star in Hunter have agency over whatever the company does to them. Only making a generalization in the context of comparison with Deviant (or what we know so far, anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-31-2015, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:46:19-07:00","id":609432,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure Deviant has a very low power level. Rich commented something to that effect a while back on the Monday Meeting blog, when some comments were made about the last two games having an increased power level. I expect it'll be just people with some mojo, Hunter-style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:50:40-07:00","id":609444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609228#post609228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm currently hoping the X-splat is going to be 'augmentation' (how you were changed) and the Y-splat will be your 'purpose' (what you were created to do). Although I can see purpose as the X-splat or only splat and the 'how' being flavour.<br /> <br /> I would love for the powers to all have a physical component. As long as something supernatural is going on I can see a cyber-augmented Deviant tinkering with his implants and adding new ones by instinct while a bio-augmented Deviant growing entirely new appendages and organs.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if it'll be called Deviant: the Evolved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ditto. I'm hoping I finally have the tools to run a Creature from the Black Lagoon game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:55:30-07:00","id":609447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609429#post609429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the title Deviant, but thought of a totally different view of this.<br /> <br /> Deviant:The Ruination - You have slumbered for eons, now you awaken call upon by someone who dared to disturb the division of the natural and supernatural worlds. You are the entity someone has summoned and charged with a command that you must follow, but what they don't know is that you will not go back to sleep. Deviant is game of planing, manipulation, and escape. Are you smarter then those who enslaved you or will you be cast back into the endless slumber.<br /> <br /> Deviants come form the cosmology of the WOD, each one with their own traits and abilities, unleashed on the mortal world you the creature now has flesh and blood. Each player must work to completed the goal given to them in their own way but also must figure out how to escape the bonds before put back to sleep. Once free the Deviant can explore this new world, they can choose to walk among those of this world as one of them or as some monster. Beware those who know your truth for you are bound by commands of your true name, but that is not the only fear the Deviant has to worry about. The entities that they slumbered among some times seek them out to return to serve them instead of returning to slumber.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This idea would overlap a lot with Geist. Not that, that's a bad thing necessarily. Geist might be better if it focused more generally on claimed and less specifically on the ghost-claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:00:17-07:00","id":609448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609444#post609444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ditto. I'm hoping I finally have the tools to run a Creature from the Black Lagoon game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did Beast not get you that? I literally made a character whose whole concept was &quot;bog-dwelling fish monster&quot; during the initial draft.<br /> <br /> Regarding Deviant though, I'm hoping for a dearth of cyberware. I don't want this to become World of Darkness: Shadowrun 2016.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:17:38-07:00","id":609465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609447#post609447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This idea would overlap a lot with Geist. Not that, that's a bad thing necessarily. Geist might be better if it focused more generally on claimed and less specifically on the ghost-claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, I prefer Geist as the &quot;ghost game&quot; the same way Werewolf is the &quot;Spirit game&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:20:25-07:00","id":609553,"title":"","content":"For the record, I have no problem with adding more cyberpunk to the World of Darkness, and in fact eagerly embrace it. The fact I haven't run a Bleeding Edge game yet astounds me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:03:31-07:00","id":609656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609448#post609448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Deviant though, I'm hoping for a dearth of cyberware. I don't want this to become World of Darkness: Shadowrun 2016.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't mind a cyberwear-heavy book, but I basically agree with the point here. I'd like to see cybered characters as an option, but Deviant really feels to be more 'the gameline of Doctor Morreau' from the blurb, although we don't really know, and I'll be upset if bioaugmentation is secondary to cyberwear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:54:31-07:00","id":609803,"title":"","content":"My mind immediately jumped to X-Files. Genetic mutants, hybrids and freaks running wild, often hunting down the people behind the shady conspiracies responsible for their existence (as well as hurting innocents and causing headaches for the authorities). Yes please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3771-damoqles","name":"damoqles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:59:19-07:00","id":609806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609448#post609448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Beast not get you that? I literally made a character whose whole concept was &quot;bog-dwelling fish monster&quot; during the initial draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the wait and see camp. IMO, it's a little too Astral based for a true Black Lagoon Monster to be made but, the primordial aspect could work with the &quot;antideluvian&quot; aspect of the monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609448#post609448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Deviant though, I'm hoping for a dearth of cyberware. I don't want this to become World of Darkness: Shadowrun 2016.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto, My &quot;Monster from the Black Lagoon&quot; was a bit of a mis-remember on my part. I'm looking for something makes The Alligator People, The Fly, and The Wasp Woman quite possible. Seems like Deviant might fit the bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:02:22-07:00","id":609807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609465#post609465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eh, I prefer Geist as the &quot;ghost game&quot; the same way Werewolf is the &quot;Spirit game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, but I wish they'd change the name to something more descriptive of the splat, like Revenant, Wight, Zombie, anything but Ghost (or the German equivalent) because you don't actually play ghosts, you play claimed made from ghosts and dead people (which sounds more like a revenant to me...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:52:53-07:00","id":609851,"title":"","content":"Not really sure what else the over arching splat other than maybe &quot;Abomination: The Experiment&quot; that fits the types of things that would fall in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:27:15-07:00","id":610178,"title":"","content":"Dave B just said this about deviant on 4chan<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like. said at the panel, Deviant makes me wish &quot;Cronenburg&quot; was a verb.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's about people who have been violated and turned into generally-low-with-potential-for-explosivly-high powered body-horror supernatural beings fighting the Conspiracies that created them. A rich vein of stories we haven't really tapped yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#364041\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you were disappointed by Beast being hugh powered and not visibly monstrous to bystanders, Deviant is the exact opposite.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So,we have Lots of body horror and they are created beings,i'm having a ahard time seeing this game being a unique game,too much like promethean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 07-31-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:15:12-07:00","id":610214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610178#post610178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are created beings</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;people who have been [\u2026] turned into [\u2026] supernatural beings&quot; suggests you need to read the post again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:27:20-07:00","id":610231,"title":"","content":"I'm incredibly excited for fucked-up street-level supers with a dash of X-Files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:51:36-07:00","id":610245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610231#post610231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm incredibly excited for fucked-up street-level supers with a dash of X-Files.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back ally surgery has never been this fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:00:45-07:00","id":610249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610214#post610214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;people who have been [\u2026] turned into [\u2026] supernatural beings&quot; suggests you need to read the post again.</div> </div> </div> </div> They were created by conspirancies,so a lot more like promethean than anything else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:06:51-07:00","id":610251,"title":"","content":"Prometheans tend to be created by other Prometheans. They also don't all have bodies with which to have body horror with, some being made entirely of metal or other non-flesh.<br /> <br /> Also Promethean is about learning what it is to be human, something Deviants already know but has likely been taken from them forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:17:53-07:00","id":610256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610249#post610249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were created by conspirancies,so a lot more like promethean than anything else</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean other than the fact that there is no such thing as a conspiracy of prometheans? Prometheans are made from individuals, or not made at all, since some arise spontaneously.<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering how crossover friendly Deviant is going to be, it seems, from the description, that it would be pretty organic to include deviants in another game line by altering who did the experimentation- Ordo dracul for vampire, seer for mage, alchemists for promethean, cheiron for hunter, sorcerers for mummy, or god-machine for demon. <br /> <br /> If the deviant was made as a supersoldier, then a deviant dogs of war story would make sense. If the deviant was made as a byproduct of immortality research, well that suggests a natural connection to an immortal type or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 07-31-2015, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:31:02-07:00","id":610262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610251#post610251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans tend to be created by other Prometheans. They also don't all have bodies with which to have body horror with, some being made entirely of metal or other non-flesh.<br /> <br /> Also Promethean is about learning what it is to be human, something Deviants already know but has likely been taken from them forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean was filled with body horror,each Splat of promethean had a disfigurement that was hideous and terrifying, centimanus and pandorans are full of disfigurements as well,the first 20 pages of the corebook went out of their way to explain how much body horror promethean has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:33:41-07:00","id":610266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610262#post610262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Promethean was filled with body horror,each Splat of promethean had a disfigurement that was hideous and terrifying, centimanus and pandorans are full of disfigurements as well,the first 20 pages of the corebook went out of their way to explain how much body horror promethean has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the fact it isn't a focus at all; Centimani <i>choose </i>to look like that, and the Disfigurements are a sign of an incomplete soul that can be cured through intellectual and spiritual pursuits.<br /> <br /> And let us reiterate: <i>Prometheans were never human, and may become so.</i> That's a pretty huge difference right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:35:55-07:00","id":610268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610256#post610256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You mean other than the fact that there is no such thing as a conspiracy of prometheans? Prometheans are made from individuals, or not made at all, since some arise spontaneously.<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering how crossover friendly Deviant is going to be, it seems, from the description, that it would be pretty organic to include deviants in another game line by altering who did the experimentation- Ordo dracul for vampire, seer for mage, alchemists for promethean, cheiron for hunter, sorcerers for mummy, or god-machine for demon.<br /> <br /> If the deviant was made as a supersoldier, then a deviant dogs of war story would make sense. If the deviant was made as a byproduct of immortality research, well that suggests a natural connection to an immortal type or two.</div> </div> </div> </div>[QUOTE=StSword;n610256]<br /> <br /> i wonder if the corebook will introduce new organizations/conspiracies/enterpryses/governement agencies etc...,to be the creators of the deviants,or if they will use organizations that already were introduced in the WOD by other lines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 07-31-2015, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:56:55-07:00","id":610290,"title":"","content":"One thing worth noting: Prometheans want to be human, while Deviants (if we're calling them that???) used to be normal folks. The similarity is closer to Changeling than anything else, but even that is flimsy since it seems like we're dealing with human malice/intent, not the mad whims of insane alien gods. Deviant feels much more personal.<br /> <br /> Demon is also a game with serious body horror things (where you also play as non-human created beings!), but I feel like it certainly has a distinct identity from Promethean. And nobody pitches a fit about Mage, Changeling, and Mummy all interacting with Fate.<br /> <br /> tl;dr calm down, naysayers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:17:56-07:00","id":610307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=609806#post609806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the wait and see camp. IMO, it's a little too Astral based for a true Black Lagoon Monster to be made but, the primordial aspect could work with the &quot;antideluvian&quot; aspect of the monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Astral bog monster Beast reached her Inheritance, and is now an embodied real bog monster in the real world. Bam. Done.<br /> <br /> Ask your ST if you can play a Beast after their Inheritance. It may be difficult since you're literally just a monster, but you said you wanna do that, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:01:32-07:00","id":610389,"title":"","content":"huh,i think y'all might right on saying deviant it's not tha clsoe with promethean. slight changing subject then,android 17 and 18 from dragon ball,i think they could be deviants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:21:29-07:00","id":610421,"title":"","content":"Were they people turned into androids? Or more created from scratch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:47:05-07:00","id":610432,"title":"","content":"Deviants are people turned into cyborgs (cyborgs are part man part machine, androids are human looking robots &gt;.&gt;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:51:53-07:00","id":610433,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Androids&quot; of Dragon Ball are collectively a mix of cyborgs and androids; 17 and 18 were humans made into cyborgs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:01:12-07:00","id":610437,"title":"","content":"That I did not know, but I was going by the actual definitions.<br /> <br /> android: <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(in science fiction) a robot with a human appearance.<br /> cyborg: (in science fiction) a living being whose powers are enhanced by computer implants or mechanical body parts.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:07:49-07:00","id":610445,"title":"","content":"Everyone's latched onto the scientific/medical side of things and completely missed the &quot;altar&quot; bit, which has me more excited than anything else. Being the unwilling creation of a dark cult (Arisen or otherwise) of some sort? Sign me up for twelve copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:16:53-07:00","id":610475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=610445#post610445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone's latched onto the scientific/medical side of things and completely missed the &amp;quot;altar&amp;quot; bit, which has me more excited than anything else. Being the unwilling creation of a dark cult (Arisen or otherwise) of some sort? Sign me up for twelve copies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Instant Mummy crossover. Instant Vampire crossover. Hell, you can probably cross that hook with any gameline. Even Werewolf would work if they were trying to make you a part of their pack and something went horribly, horribly wrong (or alternatively horribly, horribly right). I'm stoked for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2