"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T23:51:58-07:00","id":614650,"title":"","content":"Ooooo I'd say kinda kin... like Mages or Psychics.<br /> Then again, we don't know How transformed they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T23:56:39-07:00","id":614653,"title":"","content":"I saw someone else mention <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=76-bWPMUHkU\" target=\"_blank\">The Secret World of Alex Mack</a> in response to this game.<br /> <br /> And I'm like, sold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T00:36:11-07:00","id":614698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=614653#post614653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw someone else mention <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=76-bWPMUHkU\" target=\"_blank\">The Secret World of Alex Mack</a> in response to this game.<br /> <br /> And I'm like, sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, man, I loved that show! It was so '90s.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if you could build Captain America as a Deviant? Though he's probably too Shining Beacon of Hope for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I also have this image of a man strapped to an altar, robed figures carving strange marks into his flesh with heated knives, and a dark transformation coming over him, his skin hardening, one hand become clawlike, pupils turning catlike, an overall horrid transformation that leaves him physically stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T00:47:33-07:00","id":614700,"title":"","content":"Being mostly Street Level it feels like Deviant will profit the most from Hurt Locker of all the full templates, just by how close to &quot;human&quot; the violence will be.<br /> It's probably too early in Deviant's development to do a compatibility pass on Hurt Locker, but having a second look at for example the minor templates in HL might be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T01:41:50-07:00","id":614716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=614698#post614698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, man, I loved that show! It was so '90s.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if you could build Captain America as a Deviant? Though he's probably too Shining Beacon of Hope for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I also have this image of a man strapped to an altar, robed figures carving strange marks into his flesh with heated knives, and a dark transformation coming over him, his skin hardening, one hand become clawlike, pupils turning catlike, an overall horrid transformation that leaves him physically stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could, rules wise, pretty much all you need for cap is physicals at 5, wits and 5, and a lot of merits, including quick healer.<br /> <br /> Thematically though, I feel deviant is aiming more for Deadpool or Winter Soldier. Both have taken up the captain america mantle though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh I had another thought on a hunter/deviant connection.<br /> <br /> Dr Wintergreen, the scientist that came up with the chemical cocktail that makes the pseudo-psychics of Vanguard, vanished. Perhaps she's started on more powerful, dangerous neurochemical experiments.....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-04-2015, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:22:34-07:00","id":615042,"title":"","content":"This game is making me picture WitchCraft's Disciplines of the Flesh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:56:51-07:00","id":615416,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think what a good Dark Era for Deviant might be. Victorian/Gilded Age, with attendant eugenic, alienist, and spiritualist experimentation would be the easiest option, but I'm wondering if there isn't something more surprising as a cool fit I'm not thinking of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-04-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:14:11-07:00","id":615623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615416#post615416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think what a good Dark Era for Deviant might be. Victorian/Gilded Age, with attendant eugenic, alienist, and spiritualist experimentation would be the easiest option, but I'm wondering if there isn't something more surprising as a cool fit I'm not thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be stepping on Promethean's toes a little bit, but my first thought would be Europe, circa 1350. Black Death is in full swing, so alchemists and other &quot;scholars&quot; go to extraordinary lengths to find the philosopher's stone/elixir of life or to produce individuals who are &quot;refined&quot; enough to be immune. People are dying all the time, so who would miss a few common folk who go missing in the name of enlightenment?<br /> <br /> Of course, that's pretty knee-jerk based on the limited information we have now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4732,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","user":"Drazosh","date":". 08-04-2015, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:43:42-07:00","id":615637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615416#post615416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think what a good Dark Era for Deviant might be. Victorian/Gilded Age, with attendant eugenic, alienist, and spiritualist experimentation would be the easiest option, but I'm wondering if there isn't something more surprising as a cool fit I'm not thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edwardian Era. See the evolution of medicine away from the Sawbones and Barbers-Surgeon of the previous 500 years into the clinical and academically rigorous field it has become today. Watch the rise of drug culture and snake-oil, as well as the birth of modern psychiatrics. (the Knick is one of my favorite shows, and a lot of the things talked about here makes me think that a story from a patient's perspective would be compelling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:50:21-07:00","id":615831,"title":"","content":"Set it during the Mauryan Empire, the time when the Vish Kanya where used as human weapons of war agianst they're enemies. The Vish Kanya where poisonous to other humans beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:16:44-07:00","id":615871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615831#post615831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set it during the Mauryan Empire, the time when the Vish Kanya where used as human weapons of war agianst they're enemies. The Vish Kanya where poisonous to other humans beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell fucking yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:42:16-07:00","id":615884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615831#post615831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set it during the Mauryan Empire, the time when the Vish Kanya where used as human weapons of war agianst they're enemies. The Vish Kanya where poisonous to other humans beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>An option contemporary to that that I keep coming back to (even though I like it more for Vampire) is the Qin Dynasty - with the idea of the Emperor having alchemical experiments carried out in his quest for immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-04-2015, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:53:43-07:00","id":615893,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I wonder if there's any underlying definition for Deviants beyond &quot;weird supernatural/mad-science abilities granted by some form of mortal experimentation/procedure&quot;? If a Cheiron Agent with Thaumatech, or a VASCU agent with Teleinformation, etc etc go rogue - would they be Deviants? Or is there some other fundamental definition I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:05:38-07:00","id":615939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615893#post615893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is there some other fundamental definition I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I think there's some sort of other factor, some influence that could separate Hunter and Deviant. Not sure what, since it isn't unwillingness, considering Mr. Dave's comments on self-experimentation mentioned earlier on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T21:52:21-07:00","id":615997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=615416#post615416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think what a good Dark Era for Deviant might be. Victorian/Gilded Age, with attendant eugenic, alienist, and spiritualist experimentation would be the easiest option, but I'm wondering if there isn't something more surprising as a cool fit I'm not thinking of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it really depends on what you want to emphasize, since Deviant seems rather broad in scope.<br /> <br /> Going to medical horror, well there's plenty of medical horror in history- Nazi experiments are a little over played one can argue, but how about the Japanese Unit 731?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:49:15-07:00","id":616020,"title":"","content":"You should be able to find some human experimentation during WW2 any place you care to look. Some seriously sick bastards were running around until starting after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:05:33-07:00","id":616039,"title":"","content":"True, but despite how much the soviet monkeyman thing caught on as a meme (and already exist in nwod anyway, as of skinchangers), from what I could look up it looks like horrific soviet experiments were more about finding new ways to kill people, which shouldn't lend itself to making a lot of deviants unless soviet mad scientists are rather incompetent at killing people.<br /> <br /> One could make a Prison break inspired Deviant game based on the San Quentin experiments- You're a convict experimented on, funded by Uncle Sam. Use your sweet new lovecraftian superpowers with your criminal talents to go all Michael Scofield and get the hell out of dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:19:21-07:00","id":616045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616020#post616020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be able to find some human experimentation during WW2 any place you care to look. Some seriously sick bastards were running around until starting after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that was a natural outcome of the whole eugenic movement, I would say it be worth looking at how belief systems had evolved from the start to the end point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:48:42-07:00","id":616068,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone was doing anything that might reasonably create Deviants, although I don't know exactly how they are created. The point is you could fudge any country with the funds for the experimentation and the people with the know how to create Deviants, however that ends up being, to create a setting. Generally, everyone was good about keeping what they were doing a secret at the time or killing their victims, so there is another slight loss of realism. It took decades before it came to an end and started decades earlier, and I think an era is supposed to be shorter than that if it is in the modern era. Around WW2 is probably the turning point of the movement. You could shift 30 years either way without much of an issue. Eugenics, and similar thinking, was indeed the lead in, IMO, so you could easily come up with something when we actually know about Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T02:02:32-07:00","id":616094,"title":"","content":"I doubt if Deviant will care overmuch about how someone is altered- different conspiracies would logically have different secrets and techniques, so I suspect how one is altered will be mostly fluff- cyborgs made from corpses like universal soldier, a guy possessed by intelligent mold found in the cthonic depths of the earth, someone infected by a moreauvian virus, someone who had their skulls opened up and their brains surgically rewired for psychic powers, someone with their blood system alchemically altered, someone who gets a bone marrow transplant from the dead to flood their system with ectoplasm, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:26:15-07:00","id":616572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=614653#post614653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw someone else mention <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=76-bWPMUHkU\" target=\"_blank\">The Secret World of Alex Mack</a> in response to this game.<br /> <br /> And I'm like, sold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap, yes please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:01:50-07:00","id":616621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616094#post616094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I doubt if Deviant will care overmuch about how someone is altered- different conspiracies would logically have different secrets and techniques, so I suspect how one is altered will be mostly fluff- cyborgs made from corpses like universal soldier, a guy possessed by intelligent mold found in the cthonic depths of the earth, someone infected by a moreauvian virus, someone who had their skulls opened up and their brains surgically rewired for psychic powers, someone with their blood system alchemically altered, someone who gets a bone marrow transplant from the dead to flood their system with ectoplasm, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope I can build the narco-bodhisattva that is Lucy without an eminent threat of turning to dust. At least, not permanently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:34:26-07:00","id":616662,"title":"","content":"I just hope at some point in the book there's a quote about using more than 10% of your brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:45:48-07:00","id":616664,"title":"","content":"My goodness I hope not. Humans use all of their brains, much like they actually use their appendix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:13:56-07:00","id":616683,"title":"","content":"I'd throw it into a fiction as a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:15:06-07:00","id":616685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616662#post616662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope at some point in the book there's a quote about using more than 10% of your brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most of my kind only make use of 10% of the brain, but I found that with some fava beans and a nice Chianti I can make use of much more of it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:33:24-07:00","id":616748,"title":"","content":"You could do much older eras but a lot of the stuff I want to do with Deviant has to do with big modern societies and intrusive demands on the bodies of subjects/citizens/patients/employees (maybe a bit of Foucault biopower stuff is in the back of my mind here).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to separate it too much from that, and since it's the age of MKULTRA and Manchurian Candidates as well as suspicion of the establishment, medical and scientific advancement, and a bunch of really fun aesthetics - the sixties in America, all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 08-06-2015, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T20:19:33-07:00","id":617101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616748#post616748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do much older eras but a lot of the stuff I want to do with Deviant has to do with big modern societies and intrusive demands on the bodies of subjects/citizens/patients/employees (maybe a bit of Foucault biopower stuff is in the back of my mind here).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to separate it too much from that, and since it's the age of MKULTRA and Manchurian Candidates as well as suspicopn of the establishment, medical and scientific advancement, and a bunch of really fun aesthetics - the sixties in America, all the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a foucult biopower stuuf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T21:54:51-07:00","id":617138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616621#post616621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just hope I can build the narco-bodhisattva that is Lucy without an eminent threat of turning to dust. At least, not permanently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, not to be a wet blanket, but if you want to play Lucy in nwod, why wait for a gameline that may or may not do what you want it to do, when you could just use the psychic hack from the mage chroniclers guide and play Lucy today?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617101#post617101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is a foucult biopower stuuf?</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biopower#Foucault_and_the_concept_of_biopower\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biopow...pt_of_biopower</a> for the long version, short version is an institution's power over life and death of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-06-2015, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T07:35:42-07:00","id":617750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=616662#post616662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope at some point in the book there's a quote about using more than 10% of your brain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They could reference it in a realistic sense: We use all our brains but not all at the same time - different parts are used as we do different things and think different thoughts. 100% of the brain being equally &quot;on&quot; at the same time would just cause a seizure. Being able to flip that switch in someone's head would be a good way to quickly debilitate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T08:34:00-07:00","id":617789,"title":"","content":"IMO, in the WoD the 100% of your brain = superpowers should be true.<br /> <br /> Possibly exploiting the same weirdness that makes Embeds work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:35:51-07:00","id":617823,"title":"","content":"There is a logical fault. If 100% of the brain was working at the same time then it must be significantly damaged. A person would feel pain to maximum intensity which usually causes the brain to shutdown certain portions, frequently switching the body to sleep mode. At the same time, the person would feel other emotions, so without a doubt would go insane. The massive amount of information being processed would result in paralysis. Imagine a computer working at 100% of resources. You can hear the *grrrrrr*. Best to avoid exact percentages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:42:16-07:00","id":617826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617789#post617789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, in the WoD the 100% of your brain = superpowers should be true..</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> I mean I recognize it's a world based on legends, folklore, etc - but some things are so stupid and commonly believed that it's just irresponsible for any publisher to reinforce them.<br /> <br /> IF it got used it should explicitly say &quot;the demon exploits the erroneous belief about the brain as a weak point to alter reality&quot;. Even then, I see no reason for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:48:19-07:00","id":617831,"title":"","content":"The only using 10% of the brain thing feels really tacky, and is one of those super commonly denounced quacky psuedo-science myth that I feel like it would detract from the seriousness of the publication if it made it in as anything other than a joke in a sidebar, maybe to illustrate how people (Deviants) might often operate with a misunderstanding of their own capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 08-06-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T11:43:31-07:00","id":617899,"title":"","content":"It's not a science factoid is a quacky psuedo-science myth, otherwise +1 to your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:03:02-07:00","id":617908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617899#post617899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a science factoid is a quacky psuedo-science myth</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Factoid\" target=\"_blank\">That's what a factoid <i>is.</i></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:35:00-07:00","id":617930,"title":"","content":"I think it would be more accurate to say that we are <i>aware </i>of 10% of our neurological functions at any given moment, due in part to our pain management, sensory processing, and autonomic nervous systems. I think its more useful to compare fictional characters that have used awareness expanding drugs to jail-breaking a smartphone; you have a lot more direct control over what the phone does, but you have no real safety-net if you screw something up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:44:12-07:00","id":617934,"title":"","content":"Are you trying to make an analogy for taking adderall? I'd be in for rules on (essentially) overclocking what you've got. Just don't say that it improves performance by 900%. Even performance enhancing drugs like adderall (and caffein and nicotein and...etc.) have very tiny effects on your cognitive abilities.<br /> <br /> Basically, talking to some neuroscientists I know, you use all of your brain most of the time. A lot of what it does is not stuff that you would not want to consciously think about even if you wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:47:54-07:00","id":617937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617101#post617101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is a foucult biopower stuuf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophy Bro explains succinctly-but-at-some-length <a href=\"http://www.philosophybro.com/post/55737445991/biopower-and-you-a-general-summary-according-to\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. To summarize very briefly as most closely relates to my thoughts about Deviant and modern times; in ye olden days kings didn't really care about the inner lives and bodily function of their subjects, just that they didn't rock the boat and they kicked out the right outputs (food, taxes). Then in most recent times powerful people and institutions realized that it was more useful to make everyone healthier, happier, more productive, and got all up in people's business about health, labor, sex, social life, and basically everything, because they want everyone to be as useful as possible, and if your idea of what you want to do is too out of line with what's expected of you - too<i> deviant</i> - it's treated as a threat to the health, labor, sex, social life, and basically everything of everyone else.<br /> <br /> Though Deviant puts a twist on it in the main text in that you're not someone who wants to live their non-traditional life in peace so much as someone whose power and usefulness to the collective was specifically maximized with surgery/ritual/what have you, and now is the time for red rampages of revenge, so<br /> <br /> I just keep getting more excited for this the more I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:13:17-07:00","id":618069,"title":"","content":"Mmmmm, V <i>is</i> for Vendetta... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:56:10-07:00","id":618256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617934#post617934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to make an analogy for taking adderall? I'd be in for rules on (essentially) overclocking what you've got. Just don't say that it improves performance by 900%. Even performance enhancing drugs like adderall (and caffein and nicotein and...etc.) have very tiny effects on your cognitive abilities.<br /> <br /> Basically, talking to some neuroscientists I know, you use all of your brain most of the time. A lot of what it does is not stuff that you would not want to consciously think about even if you wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>At Power Stat 10, I'd make that leap; on the road to that, I'd lean more toward Jason Bourne, Aaron Cross level enhancements. I would lean even more toward a tiered system where you go from being aware of those processes to being able to manipulate them at will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T18:00:12-07:00","id":618257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=617138#post617138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhm, not to be a wet blanket, but if you want to play Lucy in nwod, why wait for a gameline that may or may not do what you want it to do, when you could just use the psychic hack from the mage chroniclers guide and play Lucy today?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biopower#Foucault_and_the_concept_of_biopower\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biopow...pt_of_biopower</a> for the long version, short version is an institution's power over life and death of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too keen on hand-waving an ill-fitting origin story when this new game, as near as I can tell, has the necessary bones to build the same character out of the box.<br /> <br /> Also: whoa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T18:21:52-07:00","id":618271,"title":"","content":"Has anyone thought about making a already made supernatural like someone deciedes to make a man made vampire or werewolf or maybe a cyborg vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T23:42:56-07:00","id":618594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=618257#post618257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not too keen on hand-waving an ill-fitting origin story when this new game, as near as I can tell, has the necessary bones to build the same character out of the box.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Ill fitting?&quot; The psychic hack for mage already includes the option for psychic powers to be the result of mutation, alien heritage, or technological empowerment. A psychic power inducing drug fits right in.<br /> <br /> The description of deviant power level we were given was &quot;low powered with akira/doc manhatten style blowouts possible.&quot; Blowout as in something that isn't safe or maintained long, low powered except for brief bouts of excess power is absolutely nothing like Lucy.<br /> <br /> Can you play a Lucy inspired Deviant when the game comes out, sure, but instead of a Lucy who fights with guns until she evolves past the need, you'd be playing a Lucy who fights with guns the majority of the time except when things get desperate and she turns the dial up to 11.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=618271#post618271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone thought about making a already made supernatural like someone deciedes to make a man made vampire or werewolf or maybe a cyborg vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. Zoonotic viruses were included in Skinchangers, zombie viruses were mentioned in Antagonists, vampire and werewolf diseases were mentioned in hunter, and infectious shapeshifters were mentioned in war against the pure.<br /> <br /> Which means someone taking one of those diseases and experimenting with them is a natural idea for a Deviant origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-07-2015, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T00:20:57-07:00","id":618616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=618069#post618069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmm, V <i>is</i> for Vendetta... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T07:45:30-07:00","id":618863,"title":"","content":"I'd probably argue that Lucy and Tetsuo have fairly similar power arcs. Neither one has generally low levels of power with occasional spikes. They both start low and just get stronger and stronger over the course of the film before self-destructing/ascending at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:19:32-07:00","id":618919,"title":"","content":"But I don't want to play Lucy as a Mage, hacks or no. The thought exercise was to come up with a possible character archetype for Deviant, based on what we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:32:40-07:00","id":619020,"title":"","content":"Dave posted this on the comments section of the mid-week Meeting Notes:<br /> <br /> &quot;Deviant is about people turned into supernatural beings by human actors \u2013 their transformation is \u201cmessy\u201d compared to other beings, and they don\u2019t end up with an entirely stable \u201ctemplate\u201d. Most are the result of human conspiracies, cults, mad science, and other groups. Even those whose change was self-inflicted are sought as assets. PC Deviants are the ones who\u2019ve escaped the clutches of their conspiracy \u2013 for now \u2013 and have a thirst for revenge.<br /> Deviant is Sense8, Orphan Black, Fringe, The Fly, Hulk, Guyver, Tetsuo The Iron Man, Akira, Hollow Man, Jekyll, V for Vendetta, Videodrome, Existenz, Scanners, Dark Angel, several versions of Beauty and the Beast, John Doe, Kyle XY\u2026 One thing I quickly realized after Rose and Rich handed me the blurb you\u2019ve seen in the catalog and asked me to make a game out of it is how much inspirational media there is for it, which we\u2019ve not tapped so far.<br /> Many (but, crucially, not all) powers will be physically obvious.<br /> Counter to the trend to increase \u201cpower level\u201d over recent games, because the bulk of their foes are normal (albeit organized) people, they will trend to being the street level. The potential for Akira or Dr Manhatten-style blowouts will be there, but most Deviants will be the lowest-powered full game protagonists bar Hunters.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Ok this was posted again, feel free to ignore it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 08-07-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T15:24:22-07:00","id":619509,"title":"","content":"Well that ends all hope for <i>Standard: The Normal, the suburban commute chronicles</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T22:30:51-07:00","id":619801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=619509#post619509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that ends all hope for <i>Standard: The Normal, the suburban commute chronicles</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm more of a <i>fight:the clubbing </i>kind of guy but that would also be amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T01:29:48-07:00","id":619872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=619509#post619509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that ends all hope for <i>Standard: The Normal, the suburban commute chronicles</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Work: the Job</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T01:34:23-07:00","id":619874,"title":"","content":"Kate: The Accountant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T02:30:52-07:00","id":619887,"title":"","content":"<b>Roy: The Life</b> - RPG based on True Story shown in real TV series <i>Rick and Morty, </i>real life record of Acanthus Time and Space Master and his Sleepwalker grandson in journey across the Time and Space. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here is the prequel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/szzVlQ653as?t=11s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/szzVlQ653as?t=11s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/szzVlQ653as?t=11s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/szzVlQ653as?t=11s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T03:44:11-07:00","id":619909,"title":"","content":"So while we don't know how versatile deviants are going to be, the fact that Cheiron might get thrown in as one of the usual suspects when it comes to deviant creation, it stands to reason that badass transplants are a valid origin story for deviants.<br /> <br /> Presumably that means stuffing so much supernatural organs into someone they don't count as human anymore, something one could call the claymore method for anime fans out there.<br /> <br /> Anyone give any thoughts on what the results would look like hypothetically?<br /> <br /> Vampires- I could see several abilities carrying over, but I imagine anemia unless the deviant starts a, how shall we put it, high iron diet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Werewolf- some of the innate abilities I could see carrying over, although the parts transforming when the rest of the deviant doesn't sounds...painful. Deviant who really needs to heal quickly may have to resort to cannibalism, but that might not be that unusual in this gameline.<br /> <br /> Mages: pretty useless, unless the mage was part of a legacy with physical alterations, not that impressive I would think.<br /> <br /> Changelings- only likely to give the deviant a kith blessing like power, again not that impressive.<br /> <br /> Sineaters- Actually one of the more interesting options, since sin-eaters do have plasm in their blood stream.<br /> <br /> Mummy- I'm not sure what effects having organs made out of solid sekhem would have.<br /> <br /> Demon- A fun option, demon form options six million dollar style.<br /> <br /> Beast- Not much use, unless the beast merged with their horror to become a flesh and blood monster, then you too can be a dracoborg!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=619801#post619801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more of a <i>fight:the clubbing </i>kind of guy but that would also be amazing</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make the incredible hulk Tyler Durden for Deviant, but that might just be me.<br /> <br /> Well really more Mr Hyde as Tyler Durden, since I wasn't actually picturing Tyler Durden throwing cars at people, not that there's anything wrong with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-08-2015, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:18:10-07:00","id":620129,"title":"","content":"I still want to know if deformity is mandatory or optional, or if it has to be all the time or just some times.<br /> <br /> Because I really wanna try a Prototype-esque thing, 90-99% normal looking <i>most </i>of the time, until they sprout a carapace or a set of half foot talons... It cold even be used to justify the gameplay and story segregation in the games. most of the time, the Viral Deviant is just a little better than a peak human. He's mostly fighting normal, if well trained and armed humans, and monsters that can be put down by sufficiently armed and trained humans.<br /> <br /> But, when he goes all out, he can be at ground zero of a nuke and only <i>almost </i>die, or take out an entire city's worth of infected monsters in one go.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing Beasts being good for anything, Cheiron wise, except maybe beast blood from a compatible donor maybe acting as a stabilizing agent. The &quot;Absorb your soul and warp your body&quot; Inheritance and the &quot;incarnate&quot; inheritance could both provide parts, I think, ether for normal Cheiron soldiers or for Cheiron made deviants, but, well... Good look capturing an Incarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T13:31:19-07:00","id":620450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=620129#post620129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want to know if deformity is mandatory or optional, or if it has to be all the time or just some times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dave had said earlier that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many (but, crucially, not all) powers will be physically obvious. </div> </div> </div>As for Beasts not being good for much for Cheiron, I would mention the writeup on Heroes that mentions them collecting Trophies. If Cheiron knew about the existence of Lairs, and that things could be harvested from them, I could see that being <i>very much</i> worth someone's paycheck. If Cheiron knew about the existence and exploitable uses of Skeleton Keys, I think they'd be all over it.<br /> <br /> Now I want to make an NPC Beast who works for Cheiron, who sniffs out and targets pre-Devoured Beasts on behalf of the Company. Perhaps a Deviant could be created when the broken/suppressed/dissected Horror manifests its' spiritual mutilation in twisted flesh rather than in Soul, broken and cut off from the Primordial Dream, but at least able to take its' revenge. A Soul that should be free, but is now forever bound to the mortal form it longs to escape.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T13:56:05-07:00","id":620469,"title":"","content":"You wouldn't think mages are harvestable targets, but Cheiron scoffs at your disbelief.<br /> <br /> Cheiron cuts out souls and dreams and memes all the time. Cheiron looks at beasts and fill the room with hypodermic needle-crowded smiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:03:55-07:00","id":620587,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Cheiron Group isn't <i>just</i> the most successful pharmaceutical company in history, and it's not <i>just</i> a great place to work. It's also a place where everywhere you turn, you find that these are the sort of people you could call <b><i>Family</i></b>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T16:26:39-07:00","id":620703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=620450#post620450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dave had said earlier that:</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Physically obvious&quot; is not the same as &quot;deformed,&quot; so... that doesn't actually answer my question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T18:22:15-07:00","id":620764,"title":"","content":"I was more referring to the &quot;crucially, not all&quot; part of the statement. That, coupled with a large number of listed inspirations, makes it sound like psychics would be as easy to make as tentacle monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:39:34-07:00","id":620927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=620764#post620764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more referring to the &quot;crucially, not all&quot; part of the statement. That, coupled with a large number of listed inspirations, makes it sound like psychics would be as easy to make as tentacle monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I suspect some deviants are normal to &quot;Can I have your number?&quot; looking, and some are normal looking until they start using their powers.<br /> <br /> Although I suspect that the psychics can use body horror as much as the next deviant, deviants whose heads bulge as their brains expand and their skulls give way......<br /> <br /> Playing an atomic powered disembodied brain with psychic powers and tentacles might be over the top for ones Storyteller though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=620469#post620469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wouldn't think mages are harvestable targets, but Cheiron scoffs at your disbelief.<br /> <br /> Cheiron cuts out souls and dreams and memes all the time. Cheiron looks at beasts and fill the room with hypodermic needle-crowded smiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're getting that from what? Every single piece of thaumatech is either a body part or a physical object (like a hand of glory or geist deathmask) that I can recall, and since thaumatech is removed and implanted with a medicine roll, I don't recall medicine being the right skill for dreams, souls, or memes in the game system.<br /> <br /> Okay let me rephrase that, memes might be under medicine, although that wouldn't be my first choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-09-2015, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:49:11-07:00","id":621252,"title":"","content":"I get that from the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T22:29:25-07:00","id":621895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=621252#post621252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that from the books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then giving a single example shouldn't be hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T03:00:02-07:00","id":621994,"title":"","content":"ok- it goes like this.<br /> <br /> Cheiron harvest organs. They are a medicine company which specialize at organs transplants, so it just makes sense for them to use actual parts of monsters into the bodies of their agents. Now, as far as any sane monster would tell you, those things shouldn't work. Transplanting the eye of a demon shouldn't actually allow you to see better, there are no glands who produce ectoplasm and the vocal cords of a penanggalan shouldn't allow you steal their voice. Why? because those are supernatural powers. Biology can't understand how magical powers works. Science can't explain how the complicated truths of the World of Darkness twist the laws of physics...<br /> <br /> But Cheiron manage to do so. Why?<br /> <br /> Simply? It's also magic.<br /> <br /> The organ transplant thing is more or less a &quot;suspension of disbelief&quot; made for the agents of the company. It is easier for them to see their Endowments as something scientific- it makes sense that if you take something's eyes, you gain some of its &quot;eye mojo&quot;. I mean, look at Naruto! If they can steal eyes why can't Cheiron do? Only that Naruto is fiction even inside WoD, but never mind that. It just makes sense.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Everyone are so focused around the second part of their Endowment's name that they forget the first. Yes, this is technology- but it is also thaumaturgy. The organs are just junk, physical embodiment meant to symbolize the power that the Conspiracy tries to steal for themselves. Even other supernatural beings who would try to put the organs of other monsters into themselves wouldn't be able to get the same results. The reason? magic. Everything is magic. That's the whole point of the Cheiron Group- they hide the fact that they do impossible things under the guise of &quot;science&quot; and &quot;logic&quot;- but it does not work that way.<br /> <br /> In sort, my point is that Cheiron does harvest &quot;the hearts and souls&quot; of their enemies, they just do so by harvesting a corresponding organs. The way they do is? magic, disguised as science. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T03:05:37-07:00","id":621997,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call the organs they use &quot;junk&quot; per se. They're a focus. Something the magic acts upon and empowers. You destroy the eye or hand or whatever it will stop working because the organ is the glue binding the power to the wrong physical body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T04:19:41-07:00","id":622046,"title":"","content":"It's called &quot;Thaumutech&quot; right?<br /> <br /> As in Thaumaturgy?(I'm probably spelling this wrong and my spellchecker is being a dick right now)<br /> <br /> Literal definition being &quot;The Miracles preformed by a saint or a magician.&quot; with several modern works of fiction using it to refer to all kinds of ritual magic.<br /> <br /> So, t basically means &quot;Technology that is also ritual magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, grafting a magical item into someone is part of a ritual to let them use theme's power innately. Putting a monsters organs in you to gain monster powers-the organ is the sympathetic Focus in a ritual to steal/imitate some of that monster's power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:23:28-07:00","id":622231,"title":"","content":"Miracle or marvelous technology if you want to be literal. Although, if it was meant to be an abbreviation of thaumaturge technology then that would closer. Supernatural technology is probably more appropriate. The means of the magic isn't important. Magic usually is a result of ritual, so it likely amounts to the same thing. A surgical operation could be considered a ritual, except few people consider medicine magic these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:23:29-07:00","id":622458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=621895#post621895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then giving a single example shouldn't be hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are when everything I am doing right now is focused on other things. Any spare thoughts RPG wise I have for Hunter are predominantly aimed at the Ascending Ones*.<br /> <br /> *Okay, and the Edo Jidai Organizations for today. But in terms of what I'm currently focusing on, Beast and Changeling are the ones that have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:18:28-07:00","id":622599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=621994#post621994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok- it goes like this.<br /> <br /> -snip-<br /> <br /> In sort, my point is that Cheiron does harvest \u201cthe hearts and souls\u201d of their enemies, they just do so by harvesting a corresponding organs. The way they do is? magic, disguised as science. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. For instance, it would be perfectly appropriate for Cheiron to harvest a mage's eyes in order to give one of its agents a \u201cmage sight\u201d-like Endowment. Really though, discussions of what Thaumatechnology can or can\u2019t do really belong on the Hunter forum.<br /> <br /> Getting back to Deviant: I'm hoping that it will be possible to build a Cheiron-built Deviant who can't be distinguished from one of Cheiron\u2019s hunters (in game; obviously, the character sheets are unlikely to look the same), save for the fact that the Deviant is fighting Cheiron rather than working for them. Infiltration of the organization that made you should be a viable tactic for at least some Deviants. <br /> <br /> I'm also curious as to what was meant when we were told that the Deviant template is \u201cunstable\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T16:54:42-07:00","id":622830,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if it means that instead of a set number of X-Splats that every body is a member of one of, it's more of a &quot;here's a list of common base alterations, a list of the kind of powers you have an affinity for, and a list of potential weaknesses. Pick three of the first, two of the second, and one of the third. Also, feel free to use the first and third groups as guidelines to make your own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Dave posted a thing on the Giantitp General WoD thread. It's mostly stuff that's already known here, but it sparked a conversation, that culminated in this<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[COLOR=#CC9966</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/member.php?43935-Cirrylius\" target=\"_blank\">Cirrylius</a> on Giantip</span>[/COLOR]]<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Aaand just like that Rick is now my first Deviant antagonist. You did that.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaurOps on Giatntip</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Oh, wh-why's he chasing after us, Rick? Why's he so angry?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">&quot;I kind of sort of kidnapped him and C-urp-Cronenburged him up, Morty. I turned him into a Cronenburg, Morty. you understand?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">&quot;W-whhy did you do that?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">&quot;Listen, this place was just so weird, with all th-urp-the werewolves, witches, and vampires. It was all a bunch of superstitious nonsense, Morty. It needed someone to step in and instill order. So that's what I did.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Anybody else like how they think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T05:07:02-07:00","id":623220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622046#post622046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called &quot;Thaumutech&quot; right?<br /> <br /> As in Thaumaturgy?(I'm probably spelling this wrong and my spellchecker is being a dick right now)<br /> <br /> Literal definition being &quot;The Miracles preformed by a saint or a magician.&quot; with several modern works of fiction using it to refer to all kinds of ritual magic.<br /> <br /> So, t basically means &quot;Technology that is also ritual magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, grafting a magical item into someone is part of a ritual to let them use theme's power innately. Putting a monsters organs in you to gain monster powers-the organ is the sympathetic Focus in a ritual to steal/imitate some of that monster's power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually we know for a fact that thaumatech surgery requires absolutely no magical or ritual trappings at all.<br /> <br /> How do we know this? Because the core hunter book provides rules for hunters removing and grafting thaumatech implants themselves. Regular medical equipment, regular medicine roll (although there's a penalty if the surgeon doesn't have a specialty in thaumatech), no magic whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Of course, Cheiron is big pharma. Three words- anti rejection drugs. Cheiron agents never reject their implants, don't have a compromised immune system, and since there's no mention of cheiron agents requiring a constant course of anti rejection drugs they would seem to have permanent effect. After all, if cheiron agents suffered a slow agonizing death without their drug regimen the game would have mentioned it.<br /> <br /> Now that's magic, or science so advanced it might as well be magic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, anyone thought about the fact that Deviant is basically the video game protagonist splat? Bloodborne hunter, JC Denton, Delta, Mercer, Shepard, Warden, Cole Mcgrath, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622830#post622830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if it means that instead of a set number of X-Splats that every body is a member of one of, it's more of a &quot;here's a list of common base alterations, a list of the kind of powers you have an affinity for, and a list of potential weaknesses. Pick three of the first, two of the second, and one of the third. Also, feel free to use the first and third groups as guidelines to make your own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Dave posted a thing on the Giantitp General WoD thread. It's mostly stuff that's already known here, but it sparked a conversation, that culminated in this<br /> <br /> <br /> Anybody else like how they think?</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt deviants will need innate weaknesses. The splats that have weaknesses have them because their innate defenses are too high otherwise, but deviants, barring the occasional &quot;blowout&quot; are a low power splat. <br /> <br /> Deviants with defenses might have to include weaknesses, but to the average deviant, I suspect their weakness list will be &quot;old age, disease, poison, asphyxiation, and violence in general.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-11-2015, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T06:14:12-07:00","id":623241,"title":"","content":"Would Opress Savage qualify as a Deviant? &quot;Changed&quot; by witches with a magic ritual, sold to Dooku as apprendice aka living weapon, mistreated and betrayed by the Sith Lord, escaping... and finally deciding to claim his own piece of the Galaxy with his brother\u00b4s help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T06:15:16-07:00","id":623242,"title":"","content":"Okay, just some thoughts about Deviant: The \u201cquestion mark\u201d from me.<br /> <br /> First of all: Mad Science, yahoo!<br /> <br /> Okay, to be serious now:<br /> <br /> I think we have some games about people who become monstrous, especially on the emotional level (the Beast lurks in their soul, in one way or the other), but stay rather human like.<br /> And we have games about Monsters, who look like people, but are deviant in the way they see the world. That is all because the nWoD is a world with a lot of strange things, which you actually can't see, because they prefer to keep their privacy.<br /> <br /> I believe the unique selling point of Deviant will be, that you are a person, a human, with a rather human like mindset, but a pretty obvious, strange and twisted body (yes, even if you are invisible, could you appear more different to a human then by not appearing at all?). I think this changes will be pretty custom-made.<br /> <br /> I do not know how the splats will look like, but I think, the method which makes you different will be a thing. Are you cursed? Are you a human guinea pig? Is magic working here, ore science? (This could be a good hook for crossovers games as well.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand is the question: do or how do you keep your deviation secret? This could be the y-splat, Deviant maybe have different convictions, if they are horrible abominations or the next step in trans-human evolution.<br /> <br /> What I just missing is the social part, the subculture of Deviants. Are there a kind of supernatural self-help groups? Superhuman Anonymous? Are there paramilitary units who swear revenge to the same target? Are there a kind of underground gothic-rave events, where Deviant meet, just to see, I am not alone? How are Deviants more than just a bunch of misfits? How dose they become a bunch after all? And are \u201crave\u201d and \u201cbunch\u201d maybe actual game terms for deviant-meetings and deviant-groups?<br /> <br /> Last but not least, the most important question: Which color will the gameline get? My guess, a kind of neon Orange/Yellow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T07:28:46-07:00","id":623282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=623242#post623242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I just missing is the social part, the subculture of Deviants. Are there a kind of supernatural self-help groups? Superhuman Anonymous? Are there paramilitary units who swear revenge to the same target? Are there a kind of underground gothic-rave events, where Deviant meet, just to see, I am not alone? How are Deviants more than just a bunch of misfits? How dose they become a bunch after all? And are \u201crave\u201d and \u201cbunch\u201d maybe actual game terms for deviant-meetings and deviant-groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that there isn't a Deviant &quot;culture&quot;, much like there isn't a Beast, Promethean, or Sin-Eater culture.<br /> <br /> I'm not going by anything that I've heard or read, they just seem like the sort of splat that doesn't have a lot of numbers. Maybe I'm totally wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T08:07:12-07:00","id":623317,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters have a culture, in fact it's worth noting that they have a <i>cult</i>ure. But more on point, they connect krewes and events and ideas-they participate with each other more than,say, Beasts or Prommies-but that their culture is defined by the conglomeration of those krewes rather than an overarching society. And even depending on the city level, that may or may not be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T10:29:40-07:00","id":623480,"title":"","content":"Gene from God Hand. If the system has a Celerity analogue, it just might work as an example of a cult built Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T14:06:36-07:00","id":623650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=623220#post623220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually we know for a fact that thaumatech surgery requires absolutely no magical or ritual trappings at all.<br /> <br /> How do we know this? Because the core hunter book provides rules for hunters removing and grafting thaumatech implants themselves. Regular medical equipment, regular medicine roll (although there's a penalty if the surgeon doesn't have a specialty in thaumatech), no magic whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it doen'st have the trappings of magic doesn't mean it is not magic, and just because one doen'st know that it's magic or how it works done'st necessarily mean it can't be done.(The Thaumatech Specialty might well just be &quot;You know how the magic works.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I'm reasonably certain that making potions and the like in the modern day looks an awful lot more like making soup or cooking up some kind of drug than it does a witch sitting over a cauldron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 08-11-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T16:53:31-07:00","id":623756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=623650#post623650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably certain that making potions and the like in the modern day looks an awful lot more like making soup or cooking up some kind of drug than it does a witch sitting over a cauldron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now have an image of a traditional looking witch (warts and all), in a suburban setting slaving over a hot stove. And a soon to be Deviant chained to a table in the basement.<br /> <br /> The Monolithic structure to be taken down? Suburbia! And all the witches that use illusion spells to hide there! That probably won't work as anything other then a one off game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:07:35-07:00","id":623857,"title":"","content":"<br /> So, we know that they are going to be &quot;Lower powered than any main splat other than Hunters&quot; but that doesn't necessarily mean they are going to be vanilla mortal grade squishy. I assume they will have a suite of defensive powers and at least some sort of specific weaknesses. Possibly, since each deviant's creation is unique they may have a system for creating unique weaknesses, similar to Spirit Banes. <br /> <br /> Basically, the point I want to make though, is that just because they are, Quote &quot;The lowest powered main Splat&quot;, well, in exalted 1st/2nd ed that appellation belongs to Dragon Blooded, and while yes it takes dozens of them to stand up to a Solar, a single DB could easily take an army of mortals. So just because a Deviant would be no match for say a Werewolf in Garuru or a Vampire with combat heavy disciplines, does not mean we should just assume your standard Deviant can be taken down by a security guard with a taser, or even a 9mm. After all, the current stub we have for the game is that a group of 3-5 deviants should be able to, over the coarse of a campaign, TAKE DOWN CHIERON GROUP OR EVEN THE US GOVERNMENT (well, at least a sub-shadow conspiracy black ops NSA off shoot funded by the US Government).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:21:52-07:00","id":623878,"title":"","content":"Prototype: You can mow through soldiers with ease, but they can still kill you dead with a well placed shot, and anything super impressive requires tremendous effort.<br /> <br /> I can totally see Mercer or Heller, ability wise, as being *Power stat* 5+ deviants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:38:42-07:00","id":623884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=623650#post623650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because it doen'st have the trappings of magic doesn't mean it is not magic, and just because one doen'st know that it's magic or how it works done'st necessarily mean it can't be done.(The Thaumatech Specialty might well just be &quot;You know how the magic works.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I'm reasonably certain that making potions and the like in the modern day looks an awful lot more like making soup or cooking up some kind of drug than it does a witch sitting over a cauldron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except as I already pointed out, specialty thaumatech isn't necessary. Proto- thaumatech implants can be extracted and implanted using the exact same techniques that every single surgeon learned in medical school and residency.<br /> <br /> And in Urban Legends, inventing a supernatural drug requires occult knowledge, thaumatech does not. Obviously because one requires occult knowledge, and the other doesn't. <br /> <br /> Claiming that it's magic but cheiron agents are ignorant of it doesn't fly because Cheiron agents can invent their own thaumatech, according to the hunter core book the proper roll is either medicine, science, or crafts.<br /> <br /> So there are cheiron agents with enough practical knowledge to extract and implant thaumatech, there are cheiron agents with enough theoretical knowledge to invent new thaumatech, some of those agents are the same people.<br /> <br /> No occult knowledge necessary, no occult items necessary, no occult rituals necessary, on the practical or theoretical level. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622599#post622599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. For instance, it would be perfectly appropriate for Cheiron to harvest a mage's eyes in order to give one of its agents a \u201cmage sight\u201d-like Endowment. Really though, discussions of what Thaumatechnology can or can\u2019t do really belong on the Hunter forum.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually it wouldn't be, because witches, barring those who changed themselves with magic, are 100% biologically normal according to witchfinders. No biological differences, no thaumatech, which is why there isn't any thaumatech taken from mages in any hunter book. And since Cheiron is probably going to be one of the usual suspects for Deviant creation, I'd say it is appropriate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622599#post622599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm also curious as to what was meant when we were told that the Deviant template is \u201cunstable\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well it might be more than that but there is the &quot;blowout&quot; function when a deviant needs to turn the dial to 11. Blowout as in tire blowout (which can cause a car wreck or being stranded), as in well blowout (which causes ecological disaster or a fire), it probably is hardly safe for the deviant or anyone around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-11-2015, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T22:48:39-07:00","id":623940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=623884#post623884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except as I already pointed out, specialty thaumatech isn't necessary. Proto- thaumatech implants can be extracted and implanted using the exact same techniques that every single surgeon learned in medical school and residency.<br /> <br /> And in Urban Legends, inventing a supernatural drug requires occult knowledge, thaumatech does not. Obviously because one requires occult knowledge, and the other doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the magic ritual looks almost exactly like a normal surgery, and the fact that someone without a thaumatech specialization takes a penalty means that you need said specialty in order to know the itntricate occult knowledge to do the surgery/ritual just right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:37:38-07:00","id":624549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=619020#post619020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave posted this on the comments section of the mid-week Meeting Notes:<br /> <br /> &quot;Deviant is about people turned into supernatural beings by human actors \u2013 their transformation is \u201cmessy\u201d compared to other beings, and they don\u2019t end up with an entirely stable \u201ctemplate\u201d. Most are the result of human conspiracies, cults, mad science, and other groups. Even those whose change was self-inflicted are sought as assets. PC Deviants are the ones who\u2019ve escaped the clutches of their conspiracy \u2013 for now \u2013 and have a thirst for revenge.<br /> Deviant is Sense8, Orphan Black, Fringe, The Fly, Hulk, Guyver, Tetsuo The Iron Man, Akira, Hollow Man, Jekyll, V for Vendetta, Videodrome, Existenz, Scanners, Dark Angel, several versions of Beauty and the Beast, John Doe, Kyle XY\u2026 One thing I quickly realized after Rose and Rich handed me the blurb you\u2019ve seen in the catalog and asked me to make a game out of it is how much inspirational media there is for it, which we\u2019ve not tapped so far.<br /> Many (but, crucially, not all) powers will be physically obvious.<br /> Counter to the trend to increase \u201cpower level\u201d over recent games, because the bulk of their foes are normal (albeit organized) people, they will trend to being the street level. The potential for Akira or Dr Manhatten-style blowouts will be there, but most Deviants will be the lowest-powered full game protagonists bar Hunters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I WANT THIS GAME<br /> <br /> SO MUCH<br /> <br /> ...as long as I can play Cameron Vale, I'll be a happy gamer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Long, <i>long</i> ago, I wrote a fan supplement for the fan oWoD game &quot;Scanners: the Madness.&quot; In my defense, I didn't have a life at the time.) I particularly like that the &quot;up to eleven&quot; option will be there along with the largely street-level stuff. IMO, gonzo building explosions from overclocked pyrokinesis are as much in genre as hiding from the PMC-of-the-day in back alleys.<br /> <br /> Ooo, speaking of PMCs, would Metal Gear Rising be a valid near-future Deviant adventure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T07:26:21-07:00","id":625474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622599#post622599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really though, discussions of what Thaumatechnology can or can\u2019t do really belong on the Hunter forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also curious as to what was meant when we were told that the Deviant template is \u201cunstable\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Does DaveB ever say &quot;unstable,&quot; or just &quot;not stable.&quot; Because those have slightly different connotations (the former is more likely to indicate a single Deviant varying over time, the latter more likely just to indicate variation between them).<br /> <br /> It's one reason why I wonder if they won't have a consistent supernatural mechanism ala the Divine Fire for Prometheans or half-flesh/half-spirit for werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'm also wondering if they closest thing they'll have to an X-splat is <i>why</i> they were modified, as opposed to either sense of how (by which I mean in what way and by what method).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=622830#post622830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if it means that instead of a set number of X-Splats that every body is a member of one of, it's more of a &quot;here's a list of common base alterations, a list of the kind of powers you have an affinity for, and a list of potential weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm expecting something like Endowments, although maybe not entirely purchased out of Merits. But nature, powers, and weaknesses being determined by not necessarily similar subsystems chosen according to your backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:17:08-07:00","id":625978,"title":"","content":"If I had to guess, I would say Deviant characters will be built in a manner similar to Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:53:54-07:00","id":626052,"title":"","content":"So, I figure there isn't much we can do with what little info we have. So, I figure there's little we could do with just a blurb. So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be. What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:47:13-07:00","id":626134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626052#post626052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I figure there isn't much we can do with what little info we have. So, I figure there's little we could do with just a blurb. So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hasn't stopped anybody so far as I can tell.</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out? </div> </div> </div>See Troma Entertainment. For a more serious answer, I've been thinking of Man-Thing and Swamp Thing after reading the blurb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-13-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T21:21:21-07:00","id":626292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626052#post626052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I figure there isn't much we can do with what little info we have. So, I figure there's little we could do with just a blurb. So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be. What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal guy who has his sanity shattered by a painful introduction to the world of alphabet soup conspiracies dating back to the Cold War.<br /> <br /> Victim of an Arisen cult, scraping together an intuitive grasp of ancient magic in order to strike back at the unkillable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T04:43:52-07:00","id":626485,"title":"","content":"And in the April Fools Day supplement, Deadpool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T04:56:31-07:00","id":626486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626052#post626052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be. What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Helena Hyde (as in Orphan Black's Helena, and Edward Hyde).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:27:14-07:00","id":626731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626052#post626052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I figure there isn't much we can do with what little info we have. So, I figure there's little we could do with just a blurb. So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be. What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been interests in doing a Prototype style game for a while I'm WoD, but not from the perspective of a Mercer/Heller type (at least not at first, but from some poor sucker who caught paths virus and is no slowly changing. Deviant has the potential to do that, and to do other games as well, which makes it a far more potentent and imagitative thing that what I had in mind. It's literally the game I didn't know I needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:50:52-07:00","id":626739,"title":"","content":"I read &quot;unstable&quot; as &quot;failing implants&quot;. Going with the body horror idea, what if your &quot;improvements&quot; require . . . &quot;upkeep&quot;. For example, your &quot;improved&quot; heart starts to fail, and you need a &quot;new&quot; one . . . Or if you want to boost your powers. Are you prepared to cut into your own body, and start taking pieces out?<br /> <br /> This also strikes me as the kind of game that needs a &quot;Sanity&quot; stat, to really make it pop. Slashed across the arm, the Deviant gets a good look at the insides. . . and there's nothing human left, just tubes and wires. Shot, the bullet is pushed out of the wound, along with what looks like a bunch of insect larvae, wriggling and writhing on the floor. You throw up, and wormlike <i>things</i> crawl out of the mess, and back into your mouth, even as the remaining vomit eats through the floor . . .<br /> <br /> Or going back to the idea of needing a new heart. Sure, you can live without one for several hours (thanks to another &quot;improvement&quot;) . . . but what of your sanity? Sawing open your chest, and stitching a new one in place would be an incredibly grisly prospect . . .<br /> <br /> Just how much can you take, before you go completely batshit insane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  Conceptually, the wormlike things were overlapping a bit with the insect larvae 08-14-2015, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:50:33-07:00","id":626832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626739#post626739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read &quot;unstable&quot; as &quot;failing implants&quot;. Going with the body horror idea, what if your &quot;improvements&quot; require . . . &quot;upkeep&quot;. For example, your &quot;improved&quot; heart starts to fail, and you need a &quot;new&quot; one . . . Or if you want to boost your powers. Are you prepared to cut into your own body, and start taking pieces out?<br /> <br /> This also strikes me as the kind of game that needs a &quot;Sanity&quot; stat, to really make it pop. Slashed across the arm, the Deviant gets a good look at the insides. . . and there's nothing human left, just tubes and wires. Shot, the bullet is pushed out of the wound, along with what looks like a bunch of insect larvae, wriggling and writhing on the floor. You throw up, and wormlike <i>things</i> crawl out of the mess, and back into your mouth, even as the remaining vomit eats through the floor . . .<br /> <br /> Or going back to the idea of needing a new heart. Sure, you can live without one for several hours (thanks to another &quot;improvement&quot;) . . . but what of your sanity? Sawing open your chest, and stitching a new one in place would be an incredibly grisly prospect . . .<br /> <br /> Just how much can you take, before you go completely batshit insane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of the opening fluff for a certain CWoD splat book.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:59:03-07:00","id":626845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626052#post626052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I figure there isn't much we can do with what little info we have. So, I figure there's little we could do with just a blurb. So I figure I might start a conversation based on what might be. What sort of characters do you hope to play when the game's out?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, powerful, slightly-to-seriously disturbed psionics, like the Scanners and victims of Project Akira. A shapeshifter who's combination of Mystique with a Hulk/Guyver hybrid -- the perfect infiltrator, until someone messes them up and the biotech turns the Deviant into a barely-human killing machine. Invisible Agents stalking the shadows, from those who want their molecules back to the conspirators plotting to <i>Take Over the World!</i> because the change left them freakin' nuts. Low-grade supermen and women who are stronger, faster and smarter than baselines, waging a secret war to decide whether they rejoin humanity or replace it. A faux-angel hiding from the monstrous sorcerous conspiracy that made the perfect escape artist, then didn't expect an escape (and the techno-Demons who think said angel is hunting <i>them)</i>. A faux-devil created to be the ultimate horror, but who decides to be a fierce hero instead. Groups of Deviants protecting a world that hates and fears them, from a darker world that thinks they're hilarious -- or just <i>delicious.</i><br /> <br /> Have I mentioned that I <i>really </i>want this game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:16:07-07:00","id":626965,"title":"","content":"I bet there's loyal deviants who work for the corp or cult or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:03:45-07:00","id":627006,"title":"","content":"I think they're called Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:25:01-07:00","id":627095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=627006#post627006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're called Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which does bring up an interesting point: What defines a &quot;Deviant&quot;? What makes one person under Cherion's knife a regular(if Endowed) Hunter and the other a Deviant? Is rebelion nessasary for the template, or is it something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T17:30:13-07:00","id":627132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=627095#post627095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which does bring up an interesting point: What defines a &quot;Deviant&quot;? What makes one person under Cherion's knife a regular(if Endowed) Hunter and the other a Deviant? Is rebelion nessasary for the template, or is it something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, a Deviant is what happens, in the case of a Cheiron made one, when the Thaumatech-surgeons screw up a major modification.<br /> <br /> Or when the subject takes <i>too</i> well to the graft.<br /> <br /> And presumably the subject is someone they abducted to test the procedure on before trying it on one of their valuable field aquisition squad members","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T17:58:53-07:00","id":627137,"title":"","content":"Sanity seems a little obvious. They might want to try to do something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T22:25:54-07:00","id":627272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=627132#post627132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, a Deviant is what happens, in the case of a Cheiron made one, when the Thaumatech-surgeons screw up a major modification.<br /> <br /> Or when the subject takes <i>too</i> well to the graft.<br /> <br /> And presumably the subject is someone they abducted to test the procedure on before trying it on one of their valuable field aquisition squad members</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually Cheiron considers plenty of their agents completely expendable, whether it's for experimentation or as canon fodder. <br /> <br /> So my assumption is that deviants would be the result of Cheiron allowing their scientists to try out the &quot;let's just do something random and see what happens&quot; sort of experiments. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T00:20:53-07:00","id":627349,"title":"","content":"There's &quot;expendable&quot; and there's &quot;worthless.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bullets are expendable, but you don't want to waste even one if you're in a situation where you might need them.<br /> <br /> Cheiron agents might be expendable, but you aren't gonna waste them on a procedure that hasn't been tested yet or that hasn't been perfected to the point that people live through it.<br /> <br /> That's what hobos and runaway kids are for.<br /> <br /> And that's my first Deviant Character. I'mma make a homeless war veteran who got fast talked into a procedure because they said he'd get a free meals and a place to sleep while he was in their care.<br /> <br /> 5 years of poking, prodding, and physical deformity later, and he has escaped, and he's<b> <i>pissed.</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T01:11:57-07:00","id":627365,"title":"","content":"This game actually rings to me. Im not really a fan of the general WoD, only Mage (and maybe a bit of Hunter). Not that i dislike the other lines, they're cool but they don't give me the awesome feeling. But Deviant intrigues me and I hope i won't get disappointed.<br /> <br /> So good luck with the game, Deviant authors/developers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T05:39:13-07:00","id":629820,"title":"","content":"So this is the game where we play Final Fantasy VII, right?<br /> <br /> My character has been spliced with demon-alien genes and is hunted by super-soldiers and his 'siblings' who budded off of him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T15:11:06-07:00","id":630297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=629820#post629820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is the game where we play Final Fantasy VII, right?<br /> <br /> My character has been spliced with demon-alien genes and is hunted by super-soldiers and his 'siblings' who budded off of him</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...I would totally play in that Deviant game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T15:35:19-07:00","id":630304,"title":"","content":"If I were to say that this game has the potential to be the most superhero-ish out of the rest of the World of Darkness games, would I be wrong?<br /> <br /> By the way, if I'm right, I'm SOOOOOOOOOOO that much more excited about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T16:08:14-07:00","id":630373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=630304#post630304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to say that this game has the potential to be the most superhero-ish out of the rest of the World of Darkness games, would I be wrong?<br /> <br /> By the way, if I'm right, I'm SOOOOOOOOOOO that much more excited about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you mean it's about otherwise human characters with weird abilities, then yes I think you're right. But I don't think it's narratively &quot;superhero stories&quot; in the sense of &quot;fighting supercriminals to protect law and order&quot; which is kind of thematically central for the genre (there are outlier cases, but those tend to be intentionally deconstructing the genre).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T18:49:22-07:00","id":630525,"title":"","content":"There's a cool similar in theme called Schism (by Jared Sorenson, using the Ron Edwards Sorcerer RPG). You play people with powers - you begin character creation by defining how you're going to die. I always went for &quot;sticking it to the man&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T18:50:36-07:00","id":630526,"title":"","content":"There's also a neat book series (2 books) by John Ridley called &quot;Those Who Walk in Darkness.&quot; There are people with low-level powers, but it's illegal to be one since one blew up San Francisco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T21:47:48-07:00","id":630680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=630373#post630373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you mean it's about otherwise human characters with weird abilities, then yes I think you're right. But I don't think it's narratively &quot;superhero stories&quot; in the sense of &quot;fighting supercriminals to protect law and order&quot; which is kind of thematically central for the genre (there are outlier cases, but those tend to be intentionally deconstructing the genre).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That being said, I suspect nothing stops you from playing a deviant who plays vigilante (some hunters do it), but in tone it would probably be more Kick Ass with acidic spit and protective skin tumors than Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:03:04-07:00","id":630950,"title":"","content":"If you mean superhero that fights bank robbers then it wouldn't be any better than all the others. If you are talking about fighting super villains then Deviants would surpass Hunters as superheroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:52:49-07:00","id":631688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=627006#post627006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're called Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; Deviant chapter would be really interesting - in large part because it would have to cover the Non-Deviant Hunters who &quot;Hunt&quot; the Deviant-Creating Conspiracies, as well as the overlap with Deviants via the Hunters of orgs like the Cheiron Group who hunt down their escapees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:50:12-07:00","id":631743,"title":"","content":"I always thought Tetsuo was more of what it's like to be a Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T22:14:20-07:00","id":631910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=626845#post626845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned, powerful, slightly-to-seriously disturbed psionics, like the Scanners and victims of Project Akira. A shapeshifter who's combination of Mystique with a Hulk/Guyver hybrid -- the perfect infiltrator, until someone messes them up and the biotech turns the Deviant into a barely-human killing machine. Invisible Agents stalking the shadows, from those who want their molecules back to the conspirators plotting to <i>Take Over the World!</i> because the change left them freakin' nuts. Low-grade supermen and women who are stronger, faster and smarter than baselines, waging a secret war to decide whether they rejoin humanity or replace it. A faux-angel hiding from the monstrous sorcerous conspiracy that made the perfect escape artist, then didn't expect an escape (and the techno-Demons who think said angel is hunting <i>them)</i>. A faux-devil created to be the ultimate horror, but who decides to be a fierce hero instead. Groups of Deviants protecting a world that hates and fears them, from a darker world that thinks they're hilarious -- or just <i>delicious.</i><br /> <br /> Have I mentioned that I <i>really </i>want this game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Invisible Agents&quot; . . . You know, with <b>Deviant</b>, I think we'll finally have all the official rules we need to play a campaign replicating the early seasons of <b>Buffy the Vampire Slayer. </b>The jock who turned himself into Mr. Hyde to impress a girl. The geek who creates a Promethean out of his brother's corpse. The unpopular girl who was ignored for so long, she actually became invisible (and started killing people in retaliation) . . . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T11:41:51-07:00","id":633631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=630373#post630373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean it's about otherwise human characters with weird abilities, then yes I think you're right. But I don't think it's narratively &quot;superhero stories&quot; in the sense of &quot;fighting supercriminals to protect law and order&quot; which is kind of thematically central for the genre (there are outlier cases, but those tend to be intentionally deconstructing the genre).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you *could* do a darker Justice League or Avengers with Deviant, but that's not the genre.<br /> <br /> X-Men, protecting a world that hates and fears them (while rescuing their own from killer robots, racist conspiracies, and fellow mutants who experiment on their own). Doom Patrol, freaks united to turn their curses into the strength to make a difference. Inhumans, largely fighting to live their own lives while avoiding the humans who would exploit them (they were secret for most of human history) and dealing with their own when the transformed go mad. There's a rich vein of &quot;outsider heroes&quot; in superheroic lore given how many comic fans are weirdos ourselves. Frack, DC has a team <i>called</i> the Outsiders. Until legal crap turned the franchise into a mess, X-Men was *the* superhero juggernaut for over 20 years. And that's just Big Two US comics. I'm not even going to <i>try</i> tapping the potential manga/anime vein here. There are, hopefully obviously, a <i>lot</i> of other things that gamers can do with Deviant, but this is a superhero subgenre that's just begging to be exploited by folks who want to light a candle rather than curse the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:48:38-07:00","id":634069,"title":"","content":"So, systems\u2026 do you think we're likely to see things like power stat and Integrity substitute, or will Deviants be more akin to third-tier Hunters, differentiated from ordinary mortals primarily by a set of powers and frailties representing the experiments they were subjected to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T00:25:32-07:00","id":634334,"title":"","content":"Maybe both, most splats have a minor template, deviants might include those who were slightly altered (x ray vision, or invisibility) w/o power trait and integrity, and those who were majorly changed ala being remade into a claymore, scanner like psychic, or terminator who do get a power trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:48:43-07:00","id":634634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=634069#post634069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, systems\u2026 do you think we're likely to see things like power stat and Integrity substitute, or will Deviants be more akin to third-tier Hunters, differentiated from ordinary mortals primarily by a set of powers and frailties representing the experiments they were subjected to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess is it will be Integrity, but with more mechanical weight to it, as it may relate to control over their powers/mutation/evolution/whatever, and like Mages some abilities may have &quot;cut loose!&quot; options that are also Integrity breaking-points.<br /> <br /> That's just an idea off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:08:10-07:00","id":634993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=634069#post634069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, systems\u2026 do you think we're likely to see things like power stat and Integrity substitute, or will Deviants be more akin to third-tier Hunters, differentiated from ordinary mortals primarily by a set of powers and frailties representing the experiments they were subjected to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's probably how it'll work, but I'm hoping that the strength of Deviant powers/talents/thingies are solely determined by the traits of said powers themselves, and that instead of a power stat, you have a <i>control</i> stat. Maybe even merge it with the Integrity expy. You don't spend points to fuel your powers, you spend them to <i>rein powers in.</i> You run out? Hulk Smash, Tetsuo blobs out, Scanners melt buildings and explode heads, cyberpsychosis kicks in, you get the picture.<br /> <br /> Y'know, I kind of hope Deviants keep Integrity as their...um, Integrity stat. Emphasize their remaining humanity, show that they're still people. To use a comment from the rpg.net discussion, The Man decided a person was a resource, and did terrible things to that person. Those terrible things cause lingering pain and suffering, but the person inside is stronger for it, and is <i>still human.</i> IMO, keeping Integrity reinforces this basic thesis for Deviant in important ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:30:26-07:00","id":635029,"title":"","content":"Maybe they'll have some sort of overload or burnout measure, similar to Cthulhutech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:19:19-07:00","id":635067,"title":"","content":"It sounds to me like people want <i>Minor Template: The Major Template Gameline</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:02:32-07:00","id":635086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=635067#post635067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds to me like people want <i>Minor Template: The Major Template Gameline</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I wouldn't be saying no to seeing the Purified becoming their own gameline while staying like a Minor Template. I'd rather see Deviant go full on Major Template though, just a low powered one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:00:56-07:00","id":635116,"title":"","content":"Well, there are indications that they might be doing <i>something</i> weird with the template, what with the \u201cnot stable\u201d comment. Who knows what that might be, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T19:02:10-07:00","id":635317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=634069#post634069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, systems\u2026 do you think we're likely to see things like power stat and Integrity substitute, or will Deviants be more akin to third-tier Hunters, differentiated from ordinary mortals primarily by a set of powers and frailties representing the experiments they were subjected to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping for something more aligned with the other games and less aligned with Hunter. It'll save on the hacks I'll have to write.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T05:40:22-07:00","id":637938,"title":"","content":"I read this book once, don't remember the title, but I thought it had an interesting premise- A man learns a martial art, and begins developing past human limits, but the martial art starts mutating him into something inhuman.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian ki powers, basically.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if that sort of thing will work in Deviant. Teaching someone a language of magic, but learning it alters the mind or even the body, mathematical equations that break the mind but unlock psychic powers, biofeedback techniques that mutate the body in monstrous ways, etc. <br /> <br /> Makes the deviants a bit more complicit in their own alteration, but no one said they were told what the results would be, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T08:51:57-07:00","id":638059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=637938#post637938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I read this book once, don't remember the title, but I thought it had an interesting premise- A man learns a martial art, and begins developing past human limits, but the martial art starts mutating him into something inhuman.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian ki powers, basically.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if that sort of thing will work in Deviant. Teaching someone a language of magic, but learning it alters the mind or even the body, mathematical equations that break the mind but unlock psychic powers, biofeedback techniques that mutate the body in monstrous ways, etc.<br /> <br /> Makes the deviants a bit more complicit in their own alteration, but no one said they were told what the results would be, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.comicsforge.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/11/herculesmethod.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I love that as an origin, I certainly hope it's a possibility. If you remember the name please share, there was something like it in Mage's Intruders book. Luther Strode does something like it, pic related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-24-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:00:09-07:00","id":638063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=637938#post637938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I read this book once, don't remember the title, but I thought it had an interesting premise- A man learns a martial art, and begins developing past human limits, but the martial art starts mutating him into something inhuman.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian ki powers, basically.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if that sort of thing will work in Deviant. Teaching someone a language of magic, but learning it alters the mind or even the body, mathematical equations that break the mind but unlock psychic powers, biofeedback techniques that mutate the body in monstrous ways, etc. <br /> <br /> Makes the deviants a bit more complicit in their own alteration, but no one said they were told what the results would be, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a boss background. Dave has said some Deviants are the product of their own work, so I'm sure it should be doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T22:59:17-07:00","id":646368,"title":"","content":"Oh something I've been wondering about, so I thought I'd mention it-<br /> <br /> Psychics were included in the list of inspirations for Deviant, so one has to assume that psychic deviants are a thing.<br /> <br /> Are you folks hoping that they can buy supernatural merits and dial them up to 11 somehow, sort of like some of the ordo dracul can, or are you hoping for an unrelated system ala Vanguard hunters or the psychic lense for mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T23:29:21-07:00","id":646373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646368#post646368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh something I've been wondering about, so I thought I'd mention it-<br /> <br /> Psychics were included in the list of inspirations for Deviant, so one has to assume that psychic deviants are a thing.<br /> <br /> Are you folks hoping that they can buy supernatural merits and dial them up to 11 somehow, sort of like some of the ordo dracul can, or are you hoping for an unrelated system ala Vanguard hunters or the psychic lense for mages?</div> </div> </div> </div> I prefer an unrelated system.<br /> <br /> Also, is it just me, or could a Deviant be a result of direct or indirect exposure to other monsters, not just mortal scientists and cultists? How about very specific combinations of freak occurrences, cosmological weirdness and miscellaneous reality warping phenomena?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I really want to make Deviant versions of Freakazoid, the Tick and similarly strange characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-31-2015, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T01:49:38-07:00","id":646447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646373#post646373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is it just me, or could a Deviant be a result of direct or indirect exposure to other monsters, not just mortal scientists and cultists? How about very specific combinations of freak occurrences, cosmological weirdness and miscellaneous reality warping phenomena?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would make sense if that were the case. Eventually humans would evolve some sort of response to supernatural phenomena. Well, at least they SHOULD evolve one if the idea of survival of the fittest is correct. When you have monsters, you get monster hunters and the like.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T03:22:14-07:00","id":646468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646373#post646373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I prefer an unrelated system.<br /> <br /> Also, is it just me, or could a Deviant be a result of direct or indirect exposure to other monsters, <b>not just mortal scientists and cultists</b>? How about very specific combinations of freak occurrences, cosmological weirdness and miscellaneous reality warping phenomena?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I really want to make Deviant versions of Freakazoid, the Tick and similarly strange characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. I think part of the theme of Deviant is that they are the result of regular mortal humans messing things up. Not that they can be exceptions to this, but I think the default would be human sourced.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T03:57:24-07:00","id":646505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646447#post646447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would make sense if that were the case. Eventually humans would evolve some sort of response to supernatural phenomena. Well, at least they SHOULD evolve one if the idea of survival of the fittest is correct. When you have monsters, you get monster hunters and the like.....</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this has just gave me an idea. It's similar to the one of the explanations for the development of psychic powers in the second sight supplement, perhaps some deviants are created as a sort of defense against supernatural predators?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:01:14-07:00","id":646621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646373#post646373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I prefer an unrelated system.<br /> <br /> Also, is it just me, or could a Deviant be a result of direct or indirect exposure to other monsters, not just mortal scientists and cultists? How about very specific combinations of freak occurrences, cosmological weirdness and miscellaneous reality warping phenomena?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is, it's a meaningless quirk of origin. Deviants are hunted by mortal organizations trying to either draft them, brainwash them, or vivisect them to see how they tick, even if these organizations have nothing to do with their origin.<br /> <br /> That being the case, a deviant who just happened to evolve solar-like bioluminescent blood to ward off vampires is going to be hard pressed to find time to go vampire hunting when they have an organization out to kidnap and brainwash them that shot their dog, kidnapped their wife, and hacked databases to make them sex offending terrorists as far as the government is concerned.<br /> <br /> So it would be &quot;Okay, fine you can be a scentless deviant with silver fingernails and teeth, but that's not going to be particularly helpful in dealing with the Illuminati group that wants to autopsy you, because they aren't werewolves,&quot; which means that I feel a player might feel cheated.<br /> <br /> But I'll bite, what advantages do you think a Deviant could have to either eliminate the major splats' advantages or capitalize on their disadvantages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-31-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:52:25-07:00","id":646665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646621#post646621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it is, it's a meaningless quirk of origin. Deviants are hunted by mortal organizations trying to either draft them, brainwash them, or vivisect them to see how they tick, even if these organizations have nothing to do with their origin.<br /> <br /> That being the case, a deviant who just happened to evolve solar-like bioluminescent blood to ward off vampires is going to be hard pressed to find time to go vampire hunting when they have an organization out to kidnap and brainwash them that shot their dog, kidnapped their wife, and hacked databases to make them sex offending terrorists as far as the government is concerned.<br /> <br /> So it would be &quot;Okay, fine you can be a scentless deviant with silver fingernails and teeth, but that's not going to be particularly helpful in dealing with the Illuminati group that wants to autopsy you, because they aren't werewolves,&quot; which means that I feel a player might feel cheated.<br /> <br /> But I'll bite, what advantages do you think a Deviant could have to either eliminate the major splats' advantages or capitalize on their disadvantages?</div> </div> </div> </div> To be frank, I am not sure. They're not supposed to much more powerful than Hunters with some Endowments, the so called &quot;burnout&quot; option notwithstanding. At most, their bizarre anatomies and physiology could give them significant bonuses when rolling Stamina to resist powers like Vinculum, a werewolf's scent tracking, a Mage's Life Arcanum and so forth. Not immune, mind you, just very resistant. Kinda like how Deadpool's relative balance between cancer and healing factor makes it hard to use psychic powers on him, or how the Hulk's anger is so intense that reading his thoughts and controlling him is only possible for masters of sorcery like Loki or Doctor Strange. You could have a Merit for Deviants that also applies this extra resistance when rolling Resolve against supernatural powers. Their resistance against mundane and supernatural control of emotions would probably stay the same, though.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:02:16-07:00","id":646713,"title":"","content":"It would be a quirk of origin, but I don't think it would be meaningless. Someone who developed mutations after being fed on by a weird vampire or suddenly gained psychic powers after a run in with a Promethean seems like a perfect target for Chiron. And someone given strange powers by random phenomena and then hunted by a shadowy organization who wants to experiment on them is fittingly X-Files-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 08-31-2015, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:14:21-07:00","id":646754,"title":"","content":"As far as evolving in response to Supernaturals, the adaptations wouldn't have to be so specific as to be useless except when facing that specific monster. One could develop psychic powers to defend against vampires' mental disciplines or develop superior speed or camouflage to help escape Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:36:21-07:00","id":647776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646665#post646665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be frank, I am not sure. They're not supposed to much more powerful than Hunters with some Endowments, the so called &quot;burnout&quot; option notwithstanding. At most, their bizarre anatomies and physiology could give them significant bonuses when rolling Stamina to resist powers like Vinculum, a werewolf's scent tracking, a Mage's Life Arcanum and so forth. Not immune, mind you, just very resistant. Kinda like how Deadpool's relative balance between cancer and healing factor makes it hard to use psychic powers on him, or how the Hulk's anger is so intense that reading his thoughts and controlling him is only possible for masters of sorcery like Loki or Doctor Strange. You could have a Merit for Deviants that also applies this extra resistance when rolling Resolve against supernatural powers. Their resistance against mundane and supernatural control of emotions would probably stay the same, though.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that would seem a little redundant to me, if Deviants have a power stat. Which, honestly, I suspect they will, but it's not like I've got either precognition or have the OP writers' computers bugged, so I might very well be wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So I was thinking more along the lines of specific mutations.<br /> <br /> So for example, werewolves are pack hunters, scent hunters, vulnerable to silver. Being scentless makes scent tracking useless, a deviant might have silvered natural weapons or exoskeleton, or liquid flesh that takes no damage from claws and fangs, that sort of thing, so an anti-Werewolf Deviant might be a scentless liquid being over a skeleton of silver, like if Skynet designed the TX while tripping on acid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=646754#post646754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as evolving in response to Supernaturals, the adaptations wouldn't have to be so specific as to be useless except when facing that specific monster. One could develop psychic powers to defend against vampires' mental disciplines or develop superior speed or camouflage to help escape Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div> Who said anything about the mutations being useless against anything over than a specific supernatural? And camouflage would do absolute jack against werewolves, who hunt by scent. <br /> <br /> My point was that deviants are hunted by mortal organizations that either want to recapture them, or just want them in general, that's the buy in for the game. That makes other supernaturals irrelevant to the focus of a deviant game, just like other supernaturals aren't particularly important to a Mummy collecting relics.<br /> <br /> Designing a deviant character concept of &quot;I'm the evolutionary response to werewolf or vampire etc depredation or domination&quot; says that the player wants to fight vampires or whatever, which basically boils down to &quot;I'd rather be playing hunter.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 09-01-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:27:03-07:00","id":647978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=647776#post647776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who said anything about the mutations being useless against anything over than a specific supernatural? And camouflage would do absolute jack against werewolves, who hunt by scent.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> You guys are talking about silver weapons and sunlight blood; that's pretty useless against anything other than werewolves and vampires respectively. Camouflage certainly isn't the best defense against werewolves, yeah, but saying it does &quot;absolutely jack&quot; is a bit much, especially in situations where scent tracking is less reliable (say a rainy city with lots of air pollution) or in combination with the use of either mundane chemicals or Deviant chemical powers.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=647776#post647776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that deviants are hunted by mortal organizations that either want to recapture them, or just want them in general, that's the buy in for the game. That makes other supernaturals irrelevant to the focus of a deviant game, just like other supernaturals aren't particularly important to a Mummy collecting relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may not be relevant to the game's primary focus, but that doesn't mean they couldn't be an interesting wrinkle, even if it's just as part of the organization's motivation or the catalyst for the horrible changes the player character undergoes. I mean, if we're going to see Chiron, then other supernaturals are going to be a factor to some small degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=647776#post647776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Designing a deviant character concept of &quot;I'm the evolutionary response to werewolf or vampire etc depredation or domination&quot; says that the player wants to fight vampires or whatever, which basically boils down to &quot;I'd rather be playing hunter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that assumption is always true. I think it just says the player thinks it's an interesting background. Or it might mean that they'd like vampires or whatever included as a (possibly minor) plot point without necessarily being an antagonist. Maybe the Deviant wants to be looking for other vampires in the hopes that they can undo what was done to them so Umbrella Corp or whoever will stop chasing them, or to try and get the vampires help against the Ilaria Corporation or whatnot, or just to try and figure out what happened. And I think most players understand that their background plot hooks aren't going to be the primary focus of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:35:23-07:00","id":647998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=647978#post647978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that assumption is always true. I think it just says the player thinks it's an interesting background. Or it might mean that they'd like vampires or whatever included as a (possibly minor) plot point without necessarily being an antagonist. Maybe the Deviant wants to be looking for other vampires in the hopes that they can undo what was done to them so Umbrella Corp or whoever will stop chasing them, or to try and get the vampires help against the Ilaria Corporation or whatnot, or just to try and figure out what happened. And <b>I think most players understand that their background plot hooks aren't going to be the primary focus of the game</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to disagree with the bolded part as a general rule. In my games, I try to make sure my players understand that nothing happens if I can't tie it into their background plot hooks somehow. Not necessarily, like, &quot;Your mother who you thought dead was secretly a Mystagogue who was trying to push you towards Awakening,&quot; but &quot;You mentioned vampires in your background, ergo vampires will be featured in a big way.&quot; I understand some people play where background is mostly justification for Merits/Skills, but I don't start creating NPCs until after I see characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:48:31-07:00","id":648025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=647998#post647998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to disagree with the bolded part as a general rule. In my games, I try to make sure my players understand that nothing happens if I can't tie it into their background plot hooks somehow. Not necessarily, like, &amp;quot;Your mother who you thought dead was secretly a Mystagogue who was trying to push you towards Awakening,&amp;quot; but &amp;quot;You mentioned vampires in your background, ergo vampires will be featured in a big way.&amp;quot; I understand some people play where background is mostly justification for Merits/Skills, but I don't start creating NPCs until after I see characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to incorporate background stuff when possible, but I don't generally make it the primary focus of a game, unless the whole party shares similar/related backgrounds. If I've got 4 players and one of them featured vampires in their backstory, vampires will certainly come up, but probably as a side/sub-plot. I'm not going to force my other 3 players to deal with vamps as a major focus. Now, if the other 3 players say &quot;ooo vampires&quot; and want to go down that road, that's different. Just a difference in styles, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:59:10-07:00","id":648034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=648025#post648025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to incorporate background stuff when possible, but I don't generally make it the primary focus of a game, unless the whole party shares similar/related backgrounds. If I've got 4 players and one of them featured vampires in their backstory, vampires will certainly come up, but probably as a side/sub-plot. I'm not going to force my other 3 players to deal with vamps as a major focus. Now, if the other 3 players say &quot;ooo vampires&quot; and want to go down that road, that's different. Just a difference in styles, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. There's a little chicken and egg with my method: I generally outline the premise, genre expectations, and system beforehand and expect the players to come up with something collaboratively and build off of each other's backgrounds. So ideally I get a focused, specific game out of it where everybody knows what to expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:38:25-07:00","id":651833,"title":"","content":"So, campaigns. (Yes, I'm still really excited about D:t?. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) What do folks want to run? I'm leaning towards a fairly standard one based on the concept, with as broad a set of Deviants as I can manage -- I'm hoping for at least one bio (Guyver-ish), one cyber (Robocop-lite), and one psi (Scanner), with maybe a spirit-made Slayer in the mix -- probably created by a God-Machine cult to justify the diversity of concepts. One of the great things about the God-Machine is that investigating/opposing it can lead to all kinds of native nWoD weirdness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe I'll tie in a Seer pylon or Pandoran/Centimani throng, if they're compatible with the broader concepts of Deviant (if any). Maybe the PCs were all made with different &quot;parts&quot; of the same slain Angel -- psuedo-flesh for the bio, &quot;gears&quot; for the cyber, brain bits for the psi, and remnants of the spirit itself for the Slayer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T11:39:42-07:00","id":652853,"title":"","content":"I totally have this idea for deviants being at the fringe of society. Very underground and maybe Blending in with the more social pariahs of the area. Trying desperately to find any link to the groups that made them in an effort to pull them down. For me. I'm thinking whatever creates deviants will be divided between so big &quot;they're too big to fail&quot; to do obscure they leave nearly no trace of themselves on the world at large. I hope the book supports s very forlorn hope feel. <br /> <br /> I'm so exciting for this game. I'm waiting the ks abs saving up for it now. I'd really like to get 5 of the premium ks editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:49:56-07:00","id":653043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=651833#post651833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, campaigns. (Yes, I'm still really excited about D:t?. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) What do folks want to run? I'm leaning towards a fairly standard one based on the concept, with as broad a set of Deviants as I can manage -- I'm hoping for at least one bio (Guyver-ish), one cyber (Robocop-lite), and one psi (Scanner), with maybe a spirit-made Slayer in the mix -- probably created by a God-Machine cult to justify the diversity of concepts. One of the great things about the God-Machine is that investigating/opposing it can lead to all kinds of native nWoD weirdness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe I'll tie in a Seer pylon or Pandoran/Centimani throng, if they're compatible with the broader concepts of Deviant (if any). Maybe the PCs were all made with different &quot;parts&quot; of the same slain Angel -- psuedo-flesh for the bio, &quot;gears&quot; for the cyber, brain bits for the psi, and remnants of the spirit itself for the Slayer?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, personally, I'd like it if there were multiple types of organizations and individuals that can create Deviants. They don't always have to be nefarious Megacorps and ruthless cultists of elder gods. There should be reasons for the creation of Deviants other than &quot;we fucked up the surgery&quot; or &quot;we want bigger profits&quot;. People could make Deviants with neutral or even noble intentions. Perhaps the people that put you on the slab or altar are caught in chases and dramas of their own. I hope the atmosphere of the game has elements of trial and error, bad guys behind normal folks behind urban legends, suspicion, teamwork forged in blood, adapt or die and the like. I'd say the ST would be encouraged to give it all he's got to make cool plot twists, and not just in a &quot;whodunnit&quot; way. You probably won't be traveling to other planes of existence all willy-nilly, or investigating the ruins of mystical empires. However, you can visit the strange basements, mansions, warehouses, sewers, hospitals and temples were Deviants were or will be made. You will be dealing with organized and disorganized criminals, corrupt or uninformed police officers, CEOs with ties to up and coming cults, preachers with secret agendas and sympathy for fringe science, and occasionally some nebulous monsters that may be former Deviants or Deviants gone wrong. I don't mind cyberpunk and grunge aesthetics at all. I don't even mind a bit of overlap with Shadowrun or Don't Rest Your Head. In fact, those two games would be excellent inspirational material, methinks. Oh, and the occasional epic fights between Deviants in burnout mode would be awesome. Imagine pitting a psychic Deviant with Doctor Manhattan-like powers against a Deviant with biological weaponry like Alex Mercer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T01:06:43-07:00","id":653624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=652853#post652853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me. I'm thinking whatever creates deviants will be divided between so big &quot;they're too big to fail&quot; to do obscure they leave nearly no trace of themselves on the world at large. I hope the book supports s very forlorn hope feel.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's already been mentioned that deviants can be created by themselves, so if someone can tinker in their garage or basement and become a deviant, obviously the default assumption isn't going to be that only epic level conspiracies can make deviants. <br /> <br /> I'm sure the option for epic conspiracies will be presented (Cheiron is pretty impressive as far as conspiracies go, a company with global reach and a private army of 1000 enhanced soldiers and who dabble in germ warfare).<br /> <br /> In fact, Deviant seems to be about, from what we've seen spoiled, not only about self defense against the conspiracies after them, but bloody gorey revenge against them, which implies to me that even if Deviants can't destroy their conspiracy down to the last person, they can make the conspiracy regret they ever heard the deviant's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:55:11-07:00","id":654088,"title":"","content":"You know the more I think about it, the more that I really wonderful how viable is it to make a Tenno in Deviant.<br /> <br /> I'd need the ability to party bullets, the standard superhuman jumping mechanics splats can sometimes get, and then assorted powers all with the option to take a living flesh suit of powered armor.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, on thinking on it even more Warframe's Tenno pretty much sound like valid Deviants right down to the Revenge against those that twisted them, except well, they already won...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T01:25:58-07:00","id":654873,"title":"","content":"I really wouldn't worry about it.<br /> <br /> Even if Deviant doesn't have a do it yourself system ala mage rotes or hunter embodiments, Deviant seems to be secret cyberpunk in the world of today anyway, so just use the Plug-In rules from Bleeding Edge to round things out.<br /> <br /> I mean it's not like the conspiracies in Deviant or other parties can't have more advance technology lying around. Antagonists has Imbued, some of whom are undead cyborgs made with the power of SCIENCE! <br /> <br /> Secret super science is hardly unknown in fiction about illuminati types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 09-07-2015, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:22:33-07:00","id":657317,"title":"","content":"I had a thought about a certain video game series that might work as a Deviant chronicle. I'm talking about Splatterhouse. Let's list the similarities:<ul><li>The protagonist, Rick Taylor, &quot;wakes up on an altar&quot;, that is, he is wounded and only the Terror Mask can save him. By changing him into a monster.</li> <li>His powers are not numerous or city-busting: enhanced physical attributes all around, healing factor, blade arms in the remake and a Berserker mode in the third game and the remake. This Berserker mode is reminiscent of the &quot;burnout&quot; mode that has been mentioned as a sort of &quot;Going Loud&quot; for Deviants.</li> <li>The main antagonist, Dr. West, is being investigated by the Rick and his girlfriend due to rumors of grisly experiments on captive subjects inside the doctor's mansion. As he wakes up with the Mask on his face, he must fight his way through hordes of disfigured and monstrous test subjects. The games have a street level feel to them because of this isolation in a horrible place filled with freaks of mad science. Even when you are out in a massive graveyard or forest, there is this constant fear of hostile forces chasing you down, and there is no help coming.</li> <li>Rick's girlfriend is apparently turned into a monster in the first game, forcing him to kill her. This prompts him to seek revenge, and he ends up destroying the mansion. In the ending of the third game, you have a chance of defeating the Terror Mask, as your powers seem to have stuck with you even after the Mask detaches itself.</li> <li>Rick himself doesn't start out as an average Joe, as he is a parapsychology student. I think there is potential in making a Deviant version of Rick who tries to return to a normal life after suffering so much, but can't. Maybe some cultist thinks he can create a new Terror Mask out of Rick's skull, maybe Cheiron is interested in knowing more about Dr. West. Regardless of what new stories you could tell with Deviant Rick, the game would have more of a pulpy, weird fiction feel to it, rather than cyberpunk.</li> </ul>Does this sound like a viable idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T01:44:59-07:00","id":657544,"title":"","content":"Deviant seems to be the splat for making a whole lot of video game protagonists, from Torque to Commander Shepard to Mercer to Delta to the Bloodborne Hunter.<br /> <br /> So not only is it okay, I think it qualifies as using as intended. I'd probably play up the evil magnet qualities the mask supposedly had, so that poor Rick can't have a normal life without living houses trying to eat him or demonic attackers.<br /> <br /> To fit in with deviant though, they aren't very powerful demons....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 09-09-2015, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:29:13-07:00","id":660035,"title":"","content":"Would it be wrong to think that Deviant would be a great way to have Iteration X-like characters in NWOD games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T19:24:15-07:00","id":660224,"title":"","content":"The inspirations for Deviant have always bothered me a bit, especially the government versions. They don't seem to explore the implications of the government sending giant purple robots after its own citizens. So I'd make a character who takes it to the logical conclusion. He doesn't want to get revenge on the shadowy government agency that created him. He wants to overthrow the government in a bloody revolution, and execute the politicians that authorised it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T02:05:52-07:00","id":660524,"title":"","content":"Assuming that any actual politicans authorized anything.<br /> <br /> The idea that individuals who are willing to violate the laws of man, nature, and god will nevertheless run their operations up the flag pole seems like an unlikely premise.<br /> <br /> I mean &quot;Oh Mr President, do you mind if we form a collusion with violent anti-american drug cartels to sell drugs to americans, to raise money to do things that if you were willing to pay for you'd just pay for them?&quot; that's an awkward conversation.<br /> <br /> And if that conversation is awkward, just imagine the one about genetically modifying a zombie virus to make mutant supersoldiers, at the low low price of risking a zombie apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 09-11-2015, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T02:14:01-07:00","id":660528,"title":"","content":"The politicians don't actually have to be responsible, the character just has to think they that are. He could even acknowledge they didn't directly authorise it, but overthrow them anyway for their inability to control their subordinates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:33:27-07:00","id":660731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=660524#post660524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean &quot;Oh Mr President, do you mind if we form a collusion with violent anti-american drug cartels to sell drugs to americans, to raise money to do things that if you were willing to pay for you'd just pay for them?&quot; that's an awkward conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Oliver North? It's not the same thing but it's very close and presumably there have been other attempts, successful or not, for similarly shady deals.<br /> <br /> The sell is less Umbrella Corporation, and more Universal Soldier. Not 'unstoppable biological plague,' as much as, 'We will never lose soldiers on the ground again, we will never have to deal with them going AWOL or causing a public relations fiasco.'<br /> <br /> It doesn't even have to be an aggressive thing, but DARPA is working on all sorts of weird stuff, like implants to help deal with PTSD and biological weapons counters, basically biological 'shields' in the form of bacteria that attack biological weapons. It's easy to imagine something like that going horribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-11-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:10:44-07:00","id":660774,"title":"","content":"Would something like the Moment from Day of the Doctor (or a biological version thereof) be a viable character? Potentially massive power, but that power only has one use, and she does everything in her power to make sure that use never happens. Thinking of the talk of usually low power but potential for &quot;blowouts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T12:55:15-07:00","id":660984,"title":"","content":"That conversation would not be awkward for politicians in the United States. I think there would be politicians that would support something that they knew would create a zombie apocalypse, it would make a great campaign issue during the next election cycle. As for military research, knowing the stupid research they pay for anything is possible. They are willing to pay for research that they know won't go anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T15:21:54-07:00","id":661144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=660984#post660984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That conversation would not be awkward for politicians in the United States. I think there would be politicians that would support something that they knew would create a zombie apocalypse, it would make a great campaign issue during the next election cycle. As for military research, knowing the stupid research they pay for anything is possible. They are willing to pay for research that they know won't go anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could play the Winter Soldier angle, e.g.: the dodgy science happens in secret until it blows up half of DC, takes over the Internet, and makes a lot of career politicians supremely uncomfortable. Then you deal with the fallout. The question for the players is do you work toward containment, or do you burn the house down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T20:31:07-07:00","id":661426,"title":"","content":"here is a character idea I had.<br /> <br /> <i>you wake up tied to a tree at the edge of a clearing. You can see the full moon. Your head feels like someone stuffed it full of cotton. You notice Them they were chanting in a indecipherable language writing strange symbols on a old railway spike. In blood. Your blood you realize. As soon as you grasp this fact the chanting stops and then They drive the nail into your heart. While this happens you feel something</i> else<i> enters you. Your flesh twists, changes and in a moment of clarity you realize that a disaster has happend</i>. <i>To</i> Them, <i>for as confused as your are it is nothing to the fire coursing through your veins. Your body now so much different than before breaks the ropes like they were paper, and as you kill them you know in your heart that this is only the beginning.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T20:39:52-07:00","id":661430,"title":"","content":"In <i>Beware</i>, one of Richard Laymon's books, this psychopath joins a cult. As time goes by he rises through the ranks and gets chosen to partake of some special rite that will make him a weapon for them. He eats a magic bean and turns invisible. Basically. Anyways the cultists never read any sci-fi or fantasy growing up and found out that invisible psychopaths are not big on loyal or obedience. When he isn't terrorizing people he's running from the cult who wants their bean back.<br /> <br /> Good book, I could see him as a Deviant who is more into satisfying his personal desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:16:09-07:00","id":664555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=661144#post661144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could play the Winter Soldier angle, e.g.: the dodgy science happens in secret until it blows up half of DC, takes over the Internet, and makes a lot of career politicians supremely uncomfortable. Then you deal with the fallout. The question for the players is do you work toward containment, or do you burn the house down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap. I can't believe I didn't realize this: CA: Winter Soldier is pretty much a perfect Deviant campaign. You could even have the distant 1941 prologue; a benevolent mad scientist turns you into a superhero, and you fight Nazis. There's an &quot;accident&quot; and you wake up an obscene number of years later into a world you don't understand, but hey, &quot;your country needs you.&quot; You fight a bunch of super-freaks, do your best to help people, and find out that while yes, the Nazis really were that evil, your bosses were never exactly sunshine and roses, and today? Yeah, they're the bad guys. So you defect, join the super-freaks, teach them how the Evil Conspiracy thinks and works, and show your ex-masters they should never have betrayed the dream. &quot;No, <i>you</i> move.&quot; Boo-yah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T13:44:57-07:00","id":683490,"title":"","content":"So onyx path is coming out with a new version aberrant. And deviant was the name of black dog games aberrant. So. What I'm saying is. Id love to see a nod and a wink to a blown up space station in deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:40:57-07:00","id":683950,"title":"","content":"So is it a safe bet to guess that some inspiration will come from the Garth Ennis series &quot;The Boys&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:35:52-07:00","id":684750,"title":"","content":"I can't wait to run a <b>Demon</b>/<b>Deviant</b> crossover based on <i>Orphan Black</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T10:56:36-07:00","id":732637,"title":"","content":"I wonder that with so many possibilities and origins for the deviants if it would be possible to create any organizations or groups that ties them toguether. I believe that we will have something more similar to demons agendas, losely organized groups of people united by an objective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T12:35:38-07:00","id":732826,"title":"","content":"Yes, I imagine the organizations will be more along the lines of who wants to hide, who wants a cure, who wants to massacre the people who did this to them, who wants to go all Magneto on the muggles, and who wants to use their powers for financial gain, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T15:31:01-07:00","id":733215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=732826#post732826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I imagine the organizations will be more along the lines of who wants to hide, who wants a cure, who wants to massacre the people who did this to them, who wants to go all Magneto on the muggles, and who wants to use their powers for financial gain, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Those are good ideas. I can see already the four groups: those who just want to hide and start a new life, those who are looking for a cure, those who want revenge, and those who embrace what they are and want more power.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:44:05-07:00","id":738900,"title":"","content":"Something that I can see happening in the corebook is that they will give example conspiracies/cults/what-have-yous so that ST's and players can have a starting point. Then, they give rules for how to make your own shadowy secret sects for those ST's who feel enterprising. I, myself, would do that if the players did not like the ones as presented in the book. <br /> As far as what Deviants are? I would love to see something low powered. Those games wherein the players can mow through a gang but then run like little kittens when the SWAT team shows up are really fun. The players can flex and go &quot;We are bad asses.&quot; That is something that all players (that have been in groups with me) like (on some level be it large or small) is when they can show off their supernaturally-ness in combat. By the same token, if they get to swagger around, then a game predicated on horror becomes &quot;What shall we kill today?&quot; and then degenerates into not being fun for anyone.<br /> I think that if they were made by some group, I doubt that said group would be easily taken down. On the other hand, the size of the group would be informed by the length of the chronicle. Do you want a long game? Then make the enemy be something uber-huge. Do you want a short game? Then the group that made you was a small cult that existed only in your state or city (See, even a short game can be shortened).<br /> Also, I am unconcerned if it is bioware or cyberware or psychic enhancement since all of it can be re-skinned for your table. Does your game focus less on Demon's sleek and chrome and focus more on the visceral nature of Werewolf and the blood of Vampire? Then you can turn that cyber-eye that lets you see through walls to the eye of a madman who could see beyond what others could.<br /> What I want are the themes of the game explored. Is this going to be about revenge or is this going to be an &quot;I'm on the run&quot; sort of game? Which way will it fall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:55:47-07:00","id":738939,"title":"","content":"And now it's time to wonder if Deviant will still get made, now that White Wolf/Paradox hold the reins!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:02:16-07:00","id":739392,"title":"","content":"Wait...wat?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:02:46-07:00","id":739396,"title":"","content":"No use in spreading fear. I'm sure it will be, there's no reason for the new IP holders to squash the RPG stuff, it's small fish. At most, we just won't see any NWoD video games or merchandise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:29:20-07:00","id":739650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=738939#post738939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it's time to wonder if Deviant will still get made, now that White Wolf/Paradox hold the reins!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?769077-Paradox-buys-White-Wolf&amp;p=19516757#post19516757\" target=\"_blank\">It will.</a><br /> <br /> Atamajakki, remember who and what Paradox, aka <i>king of the customer relations department born from a tabletop publisher</i>, is. Even if that weren't the case, a vaguely competent contract won't care-Deviant is going to be well within the theoretical contract term, and it's simply smart business to renew if things remain profitable. That, and Deviant even sounds like prime video game material from the high concept (&quot;So, you play as victims of evil cultists and megacorporations out for revenge in an urban fantasy world? Tell me, how can we fit a knock-off of Shadow of Mordor's Nemesis System into this?&quot;).<br /> <br /> Besides, the main thread's in Trouble Tickets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:50:29-07:00","id":739706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=738939#post738939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it's time to wonder if Deviant will still get made, now that White Wolf/Paradox hold the reins!</div> </div> </div> </div> Do not even joke about something like that. It's the game I'm more hyped about.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:53:57-07:00","id":739734,"title":"","content":"Regarding the power level of the deviants, I would like it to be related to their philosophy. The best example I can come with is the infamous games. If you embraced your super powered nature above anything else you became more powerful, but your powers caused a lot of collateral damage and were difficult to control. On the other hand if you choose moderation and responsibility, you didn't gain much power, but you became much more adept in their use, gaining precision and control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T16:43:49-07:00","id":740010,"title":"","content":"That'll be a roleplaying decision. <br /> <br /> They've revealed that Deviants will be the weakest splat, barring hunters, but that they're power level is sufficient to deal with their foes, who are muggles.<br /> <br /> If they need more power, they can hulk out, but the writer mentioned likened it to to blowout, implying it's a dangerous technique and hardly under control. <br /> <br /> So a responsible deviant wont hulk out willy nilly, an irresponsible one on the other hand....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T17:37:03-07:00","id":740205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=740010#post740010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That'll be a roleplaying decision.<br /> <br /> They've revealed that Deviants will be the weakest splat, barring hunters, but that they're power level is sufficient to deal with their foes, who are muggles.<br /> <br /> If they need more power, they can hulk out, but the writer mentioned likened it to to blowout, implying it's a dangerous technique and hardly under control.<br /> <br /> So a responsible deviant wont hulk out willy nilly, an irresponsible one on the other hand....</div> </div> </div> </div>That system works for me too. In fact I like it more, it's more in tune with horror movies than comic books, which is perfect for world of darkness. I can't wait to see what sort of deviants we get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T17:40:17-07:00","id":740226,"title":"","content":"You know, taking into account the theme of the game and the power level of the deviants, I believe that the game would work best on its own, without crossover with the other lines. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:41:25-07:00","id":740491,"title":"","content":"Aren't they all built on the basis of &quot;on their own&quot;, with merely the common rule-set and archetype conceits enforcing/enabling crossover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T20:28:06-07:00","id":740732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=738939#post738939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it's time to wonder if Deviant will still get made, now that White Wolf/Paradox hold the reins!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it gets made. I've been saving for a large reward tier since I have heard about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:45:48-07:00","id":740950,"title":"","content":"I doubt there is anything to worry about. Paradox seems to be evaluating licensing agreements, but will keep those that are working. Assuming that includes agreements not related to video games, kickstarters suggest Onyx Path is working just fine.<br /> <br /> It would be nice if OP mentioned the buyout on Monday to address future possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-30-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:22:18-07:00","id":741563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=740491#post740491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't they all built on the basis of &quot;on their own&quot;, with merely the common rule-set and archetype conceits enforcing/enabling crossover?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is something that I do enjoy about the NWoD compared to the CWoD. In the classic world, there was a meta-plot that forced cross overs down your throat even though the rules did not allow it. In the New World, you can have the crossovers if you want them. But each line can, literally, stand on it's own. If your table likes to play a mixed group? GO FOR IT! If your table only wants to explore one line, then that is also fine and dandirific!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:55:18-07:00","id":743131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=740226#post740226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, taking into account the theme of the game and the power level of the deviants, I believe that the game would work best on its own, without crossover with the other lines. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem that, like Mummy, Deviant is going to have a focus that makes crossovers a little harder to fit in thematically.<br /> <br /> That being said, Prometheans, Changelings, and Demons should all be able to sympathize with a Deviant's plight, there might very well be Hunters willing to go all Punisher on the conspiracies/cults/corporations than are pulling these shenanigans, and Beasts will be happy to bring over pizza and beer to hang out with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 10-30-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T19:09:31-07:00","id":743474,"title":"","content":"I do see Prometheans and hunters, even mages, but the other lines not as much. Let's try and see the relations. Prometheans themselves are freaks born out of an experiment, even if they weren't human before, so no problem fitting them in. Hunters is obvious, human beings that raise to hunt these abominations, the people that created them, or to profit from them. Mages can be the creators of these beings or look for them for research. Demons could fit, perhaps the god machine is the ultimate evil behind all these experiments? perhaps he's looking to create humanity 2.0 and demons are trying to stop him with its own creations? it could be a cool idea to explore. Changelings have the most sympathetic approach to deviants, since their situations are so similar. I think that the true fae could be the rivals of the god machine, creating deviants of their own. Vampire and werewolf, I just don't see how you can fit them thematically without changing their stories a lot. Mummy is the same. As for Beast, perhaps some of the original deviants who have trascended humanity and became something else? I'm just throwing ideas out in the air. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:32:28-07:00","id":744611,"title":"","content":"Vampires could be very effective antagonists. They are known for treating people as resources and many empower servants to act in their stead. While established Vampires tend to avoid what they don't understand, Ordo Dracul and certain outliers could take a keen interest in the Deviants. They could even create them. The Ghouls are of particular note since they are parallel to Deviants in many respects but also markedly different. Ghoul-Regnant relationship is far more personal than what most Deviants get and the Vinculum denies Ghouls even their free will - something Deviants would prize over all else. This makes room for sympathy. Still, finding a Vampire and Ghoul in an affectionate or even respectful relationship might defy Deviants expectations, with unpredictable results. Deviants who care enough to help Ghouls free themselves could fail spectacularly, due to not knowing about the Vinculum, rapid aging or Vitae addiction. Deviants who don't care have living reminders of how much more they can lose.<br /> <br /> Deviants could also find themselves supporting fledgling Vampires in freeing themselves from their tyrranical Elders. Regardless of whether it began with pleas for sympathy, blackmail, bribery or mind control, such relationship could turn rotten quickly. How many people would the Vampire throw under the bus to free themselves? More importantly, how many people would the characters? Also, who says freeing a Vampire is a good thing? Characters who would succeed are in for a bitter lesson about the Pyrrhic victories and cycles of victimisation.<br /> <br /> Vampires need not even be the masterminds. Certain Mortal groups could simply use them as servants or resources to create new Deviants (admittedly, it works for many splats). All it takes is a pill that makes one resistant to Vinculum, and the dynamics change entirely, with free-willed Ghouls still needing their fix from somewhere. Also, Kindred and other Organisations suddenly becoming aware of each other will end up disastrous for someone. While the most reasonable thing would be to avoid each other, entires sagas have begun with people being unreasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:36:33-08:00","id":750332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=738939#post738939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now it's time to wonder if Deviant will still get made, now that White Wolf/Paradox hold the reins!</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the worst case scenario that Paradox is going to axe the nWoD to try to unite the customers under one roof I wouldn't be shocked if they dragged Deviant back into the oWoD. The only thing I can think of that the oWoD offered along these lines was the Freak Legion, which was well Freak Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:44:50-08:00","id":750403,"title":"","content":"I think the worst case scenario would be Paradox decides to end the licensing agreement with Onyx Path. That would likely mean Deviant wouldn't be a part of the World of Darkness. I'm not sure about the Storyteller system. I don't know if it is an IP itself. It seems a bit odd that Paradox would scrap everything Onyx Path is doing though. Money is money. Ditching OP would mean losing money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T19:15:18-08:00","id":750431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=743131#post743131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does seem that, like Mummy, Deviant is going to have a focus that makes crossovers a little harder to fit in thematically.<br /> <br /> That being said, Prometheans, Changelings, and Demons should all be able to sympathize with a Deviant's plight, there might very well be Hunters willing to go all Punisher on the conspiracies/cults/corporations than are pulling these shenanigans, and Beasts will be happy to bring over pizza and beer to hang out with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring Hunters, all of them would probably be willing to tears some heads off too. Particularly Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T20:14:21-08:00","id":750552,"title":"","content":"Well it's not like hunters typically let bad guys get a pass just because they are biologically human- They go after cultists, slashers, witches, some hunt regular old common criminals too.<br /> <br /> So a hunter could very easily respond to a deviant's situation with &quot;Just a second, I need to pack my fireax and molotov cocktails.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T20:33:45-08:00","id":750569,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but a Promethean, Changeling, Demon, or Beast is going to have much more visceral response to the news. The former three because of like resembling like, the fourth because you don't fuck with the younger siblings like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:42:33-08:00","id":752290,"title":"","content":"I have no idea if/how Deviant will still be made, but if it does, I am pretty sure Deviants would fall under the Fundamentally Human category of Kin (like Mages and Slashers). Despite the revelation that most of their powers will be physically obvious and probably pretty freaky, I think it is their central motivation that marks them as Fundamentally Human. Also, they start out as humans, unlike Prometheans. Revenge is a very human desire, but it can easily turn us into monsters. That's why they are still Kin, I believe. It's not being a techno-arcane monster that marks you as non-Kin, it's your outlook and attitude about monsterhood. Demons try to pass off as humans, and they HAVE to, for the sake of their Covers. Some Beasts might call that cowardice or denial, but those Beasts probably don't really understand the plight of Demons.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I'm picturing this strange and conflicted scenario where a Deviant has to choose between allying himself with a Brood or a Ring. Beasts might be more genuine, understanding and even compassionate towards Deviants because of their beliefs about Family, but they lack the necessary information and expertise with confronting the distant and impersonal groups that made the Deviant. On the other hand, Demons are skilled spies and have lots of experience with infiltrating, controlling and sabotaging mortal facilities that are part of Infrastructure, but Demons can stab your back at any moment if it suits them. Does this sound like a viable plot hook? The challenge might be to make the character (not the player, gotta keep them separate) understand the full implications of this choice.<br /> <br /> The plight of Deviants makes me think of two quotes that further convince me they are Kin, but Fundamentally Human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>May Parker, Spider-Man 3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncle Ben wouldn't want us living with revenge in our hearts, it's like a poison. It can take you over and turn us into something ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shylock, The Merchant Of Venice</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you prick us, do we not bleed? If you tickle us, do we not laugh? If you poison us, do we not die? And if you wrong us, shall we not revenge?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-09-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:36:54-08:00","id":752376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=752290#post752290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, I'm picturing this strange and conflicted scenario where a Deviant has to choose between allying himself with a Brood or a Ring. Beasts might be more genuine, understanding and even compassionate towards Deviants because of their beliefs about Family, but they lack the necessary information and expertise with confronting the distant and impersonal groups that made the Deviant. On the other hand, Demons are skilled spies and have lots of experience with infiltrating, controlling and sabotaging mortal facilities that are part of Infrastructure, but Demons can stab your back at any moment if it suits them. Does this sound like a viable plot hook? The challenge might be to make the character (not the player, gotta keep them separate) understand the full implications of this choice.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe? So much depends on context, first impressions, who the PCs are. Crossover is fundamentally about personal connections and impressions at the lowest level. And its not like demons are going to come out and tell the Deviants they're demons right away - that kind of thing is a huge risk to their life. There's a lot of variables in play here. So, while its a possible plot hook, its not necessarily going to be a simple one to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:55:57-08:00","id":752952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=752376#post752376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe? So much depends on context, first impressions, who the PCs are. Crossover is fundamentally about personal connections and impressions at the lowest level. And its not like demons are going to come out and tell the Deviants they're demons right away - that kind of thing is a huge risk to their life. There's a lot of variables in play here. So, while its a possible plot hook, its not necessarily going to be a simple one to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right again. Man, I need to ask my questions in better ways.<br /> <br /> Also, I just realized something. Mewtwo is a psychic Deviant. However, in the end of the movie...<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He gives up on revenge.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:19:37-08:00","id":752989,"title":"","content":"Sudden cases of resurrection via crying harder will do a lot to shatter a person's viewpoint on the sanity of reality and how one will deal with it.<br /> <br /> That said, totally playing Mewtwo now. &quot;Cry harder, Cheiron, cry harder.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:37:34-08:00","id":761717,"title":"","content":"I'm having some doubts as to how this Burnout Mode will work for Deviants, and how the developers would try to make it distinct from Going Loud. I am unsure if a Deviant would get additional powers, improved but out of control versions of the powers he already has, or both. As MCN said earlier in this thread, the Invisible Man could be a Deviant. Would he become undetectable to all five senses and very resistant to supernatural detection in Burnout Mode? If he lost control of his powers, would his invisibility start leaking and covering random people and places?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:56:59-08:00","id":761882,"title":"","content":"You see, the problem is that deviants could have such a vast range of powers and abilities that its impossible to encapsulate them or determine what they can and cant do, and that's without pointing out their origins, weird science? magic? curses? accidents? radiation? etc...There has to be some limits, but till we have a sneak peek the only thing we can do is speculate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 11-10-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:50:26-08:00","id":762345,"title":"","content":"A couple of thoughts occur to me. One, I'm not convinced that the &quot;Burnout Mode&quot; needs to be different from Going Loud. One of the beautiful things about New World of Darkness is the ability to take rules and remix them in new combinations. IMO, Deviant will be different enough because the characters won't also be maintaining Covers and hacking the world's system through Embeds and Exploits. It's okay to reprise mechanics from other games if they are thematically appropriate. It's not lazy. (That would be copy-pasted text blobs -- I'm looking at you Beast ephemeral being rules.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2964_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2964\" data-vbnamecard=\"2964\">Firanai</a> : This is a problem for all splats. The answer is that any given rulebook only ever shows us a selection of powers and their origins. Just think about Vampire 2e, there could easily be more ways to do &quot;hedge&quot; magic than just Blood Magic and Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I don't actually see the copy-pasted ephemeral rules in Beast as being lazy, it's more of a missed opportunity. While not as awesome as Demon, Beast is still leaps and bounds better than something like Geist 1.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T14:54:28-08:00","id":772547,"title":"","content":"So, does anyone know of any characters that might be interpreted as more arcane Deviants, instead of technological ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:07:44-08:00","id":772592,"title":"","content":"Yes, technological enhancement does have more of a place in the zeitgeist, but there's Buffy the vampire slayer as probably the most famous example that comes to mind, I'd argue some of the ninja from Naruto would also count, the Claymore, and Chrona from Souleater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-23-2015, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:52:04-08:00","id":772634,"title":"","content":"Hellboy strikes me as a perfect Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:22:19-08:00","id":772657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=772634#post772634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hellboy strikes me as a perfect Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div> Aren't Deviants former humans, though? He strikes me more as a one-of-a-kind Hunter of the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: that being said, a Hellboy-like Deviant sounds cool. Eldritch heritage and a dark artifact replacing a limb sound like possible origins/advantages for Deviants.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spawn_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Spawn</b></a> could also be an arcane Deviant.<br /> <br /> EDIT 3: Kratos too, but I think he should be played in a Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-23-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:34:22-08:00","id":772664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=772592#post772592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, technological enhancement does have more of a place in the zeitgeist, but there's Buffy the vampire slayer as probably the most famous example that comes to mind, I'd argue some of the ninja from Naruto would also count, the Claymore, and Chrona from Souleater.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you are talking about ninjas like Shino and the hosts of the Tailed Beasts, I agree. Orochimaru sounds like he'd love to work for Cheiron, but he'd probably get kicked out for making one Deviant too many.<br /> <br /> Who's Claymore, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-23-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:42:02-08:00","id":772668,"title":"","content":"I had another realization: Ben10 and Generator Rex are totally Deviants. They bought all the powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T19:54:07-08:00","id":772744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=772664#post772664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you are talking about ninjas like Shino and the hosts of the Tailed Beasts, I agree. Orochimaru sounds like he'd love to work for Cheiron, but he'd probably get kicked out for making one Deviant too many.<br /> <br /> Who's Claymore, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>The stars of a manga and anime of the same name, an organization takes girls, cuts them open like fish, and sticks demon guts in them to give them superpowers, if they overuse their powers they will transform into more monsters, but some of them figured out how to cause this transformation at will and come back to their mostly human state, ala Deviant's &quot;blowout&quot; mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=772657#post772657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Aren't Deviants former humans, though? He strikes me more as a one-of-a-kind Hunter of the Lucifuge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Possibly not always, the inspiration list includes such works as Dark Angel, in which the characters were engineered before birth to be the way they were, so while odd there might be room for Deviants who were denied ever having a chance at normalcy. <br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking about Innocent deviant campaigns. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-23-2015, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:21:09-08:00","id":773269,"title":"","content":"Actually as I read through this thread the example that instantly came to mind was Firestarter by Stephen King. The child of two Deviants, the mom had low levels of telepathy the dad had &quot;the push&quot; a form of mind control that actually caused him to injure himself the harder he used it. I could see burn out mode doing a lot of damage to the Deviant. I also could see even &quot;normal&quot; looking Deviants radiating a form of &quot;disquiet&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:01:03-08:00","id":773301,"title":"","content":"Is this still coming out? I don't see it on the Monday list","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:10:00-08:00","id":773306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=773301#post773301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this still coming out? I don't see it on the Monday list</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it's still pre-first draft, so it doesn't and hasn't ever yet appeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:06:57-08:00","id":773411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=773306#post773306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because it's still pre-first draft, so it doesn't and hasn't ever yet appeared.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it still coming out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:23:01-08:00","id":773557,"title":"","content":"Yes. Please finish pre-draft so I can buy it. I could make my own but it would be horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T18:55:28-08:00","id":775158,"title":"","content":"Weirdly enough, reading over the material for Deviant, what 'clicked' as an example of a horror movie Deviant was Jennifer Check from Jennifer's Body.<br /> <br /> Maybe a little too good as blending in to be a Deviant, though... I guess we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:26:19-08:00","id":775403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=761717#post761717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having some doubts as to how this Burnout Mode will work for Deviants, and how the developers would try to make it distinct from Going Loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves the word used was blowout, but burnout implies at least one possible difference (and maybe blowout does too): that it's the end for the Deviant. The blaze of glory - or at least the inferno of chaos and destruction - they can choose to go out in when they run out of other options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=772744#post772744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly not always, the inspiration list includes such works as Dark Angel, in which the characters were engineered before birth to be the way they were, so while odd there might be room for Deviants who were denied ever having a chance at normalcy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orphan Black's another listed inspiration; while the clones seem to be normal humans (barring maybe an increased healing factor), they're still born into their problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> For other arcane options for where Deviants could come from, Prometheans and vampires have both been plothooked as cocked-up attempts to make mummies, and Deviants could be too (as well as cocked-up attempts to make Prometheans and vampires).<br /> <br /> Speaking of Promethean, the Ulgan Lineage is all about the way magical initiations break you up and remake you into something new. As a story hook, that works for Deviants just as well.<br /> <br /> A sorcerer attempting to make a summoning vessel, sacred whore, or homunculus.<br /> <br /> Someone cures a supernatural condition like spirit possession, but the cure has side effects (no one said Deviants can't be made with good intentions).<br /> <br /> Someone tries to cure a supernatural condition like spirit possession, but the subject isn't actually possessed, and the &quot;cure&quot; just fucks them up.<br /> <br /> Despite the usually SF trappings, Mr Hyde and Captain America are basically made with alchemy.<br /> <br /> What <i>are</i> the long-term effects on the Oracle of Delphi, from breathing in all those mysterious vapours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T01:31:33-08:00","id":777618,"title":"","content":"The anime series <b>Deadman Wonderland</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GzBZU1hKIzg\" target=\"_blank\"><u>opening</u></a>) works well in the<b> Deviant</b> framework. The basic premise is that a conspiracy is rounding up Deviants with blood-based powers, and imprisoning them (under bogus charges, if need be) in a corrupt jail. You see, they want the secret to make more such Deviants . . . and turn a tidy profit at the same time. Thus the Deviants (also known as &quot;Deadmen&quot;) are forced to fight each other in illegal pay-per-view death matches . . .with the loser (assuming they survive) having a body part amputated for research.<br /> <br /> &quot;One Reason&quot;, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2pZ-UpjtlXY\" target=\"_blank\">t</a><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2pZ-UpjtlXY\" target=\"_blank\"><u>he opening song</u></a> makes for nice mood music, too<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnimeLyrics.com</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>One Reason</b><br /> <br /> Slit the throat of reason and reality<br /> Cut myself and scream for their insanity<br /> Wake up to this nightmare that will never end<br /> The main attraction of this twisted master plan<br /> <br /> Trust nothing but pain to get me<br /> through the daze<br /> Sleep with one eye open not to be their prey<br /> Fist against my face they bring me to my knees<br /> The pressure's crushing down so hard<br /> I can't break free<br /> <br /> When I can feel my skin crawl<br /> When I'm about to crack<br /> The hunger for revenge<br /> gives me strength to stand<br /> <br /> I will be your deadman<br /> With nothing but this blood on my hands<br /> Stuck in your &quot;wonderland&quot;<br /> I just want to make you bleed like me<br /> <br /> Everyday goes by without a second thought<br /> Living in a perfect and controlled project<br /> A puppet of their sick perversion's appetite<br /> Will I be trapped inside this hell until I die?<br /> <br /> So what if no one cares<br /> Enough to make a change<br /> I give my bleeding heart out for one reason<br /> <br /> I will be your deadman<br /> With nothing but this blood on my hands<br /> Stuck in your &quot;wonderland&quot;<br /> I want to make you bleed just like me<br /> <br /> So make me your deadman<br /> With only poison in my veins<br /> Stuck in your &quot;wonderland&quot;<br /> Stagnated by the passivity<br /> I'm gonna make you bleed like me</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Fair warning, though - <i>Deadman Wonderland </i>is a &quot;torture porn&quot; title masquerading as a tournament fighter. Some of the scenes are pretty brutal, and its not an easy series to finish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 12-01-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T19:06:10-08:00","id":790622,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Excerpt from reddit:<br /> &quot;So, what can you reveal us about Deviant?&quot;<br /> &quot;If you want to run a chronicle in which Sarah Manning and Buffy the Vampire Slayer team up with Robocop to take on the Umbrella Corporation, Deviant will be the game for you.&quot;<br /> This answer made me cry out of pure joy, but it also made me even more curious as to how are they going to create options for deviants with such different backgrounds?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-22-2015, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T19:11:34-08:00","id":790627,"title":"","content":"I wonder if I can downscale the organisations? Like less Umbrella and more &quot;local mad scientist&quot; or &quot;small cult&quot;? I've done it before for Hunter, so it probably won't be too much of a problem.<br /> <br /> Still, I am very much looking forward to Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T19:11:50-08:00","id":790628,"title":"","content":"Every time I see stuff about Deviant, I have a real urge to run a Jessica Jones-esque punk noir game, mixed with a drop or two of Geek Love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T20:23:32-08:00","id":794573,"title":"","content":"If Captain America is a Deviant instead of an epic mortal, what would his Blowout mode be like? I always thought the precision with which his shield ricocheted was surreal, even for the properties of a wondrous alloy. Perhaps Deviant!Cap has latent telekinetic powers? If he's a mortal, this precision could be granted by that Athletics Skill Trick from Mirrors that lets you throw objects with superlative accuracy.<br /> <br /> As a side note: is it just me, or is <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/SkullGirls\" target=\"_blank\">Skullgirls</a></b> a bit Deviant-ish? Most of the characters use some sort of weaponized body horror granted by something that was implanted in them, be it cybernetic implants or a talking parasite. Peacock and Painwheel were upgraded in especially gruesome ways. The titular antagonist is chased down by people who want to harness her powers, and she is motivated by revenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T01:28:19-08:00","id":794680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=794573#post794573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Captain America is a Deviant instead of an epic mortal, what would his Blowout mode be like? I always thought the precision with which his shield ricocheted was surreal, even for the properties of a wondrous alloy. Perhaps Deviant!Cap has latent telekinetic powers? If he's a mortal, this precision could be granted by that Athletics Skill Trick from Mirrors that lets you throw objects with superlative accuracy.<br /> <br /> As a side note: is it just me, or is <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/SkullGirls\" target=\"_blank\">Skullgirls</a></b> a bit Deviant-ish? Most of the characters use some sort of weaponized body horror granted by something that was implanted in them, be it cybernetic implants or a talking parasite. Peacock and Painwheel were upgraded in especially gruesome ways. The titular antagonist is chased down by people who want to harness her powers, and she is motivated by revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more referring to Bucky and the band of miscreants S.H.I.E.L.D./HYDRA had locked in the (not so) proverbial basement. The blowout here was an all-out brawl that put Cap in the hospital, thus a kind of Death Rage, rather than some high-power, telekinetic meltdown.<br /> Buuuut, if we're applying templates to Comic Book Superheroes, Cap's a former Chiron Acquisitions Specialist, with a lot of Teamwork Techniques, Physical Skills and Merits. If you wanted Deviant!Cap, however, Hibernation would be thematically appropriate, seeing that he's more of a Skill and Attribute-monkey than anything too flashy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T20:48:29-08:00","id":795355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=794680#post794680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more referring to Bucky and the band of miscreants S.H.I.E.L.D./HYDRA had locked in the (not so) proverbial basement. The blowout here was an all-out brawl that put Cap in the hospital, thus a kind of Death Rage, rather than some high-power, telekinetic meltdown.<br /> Buuuut, if we're applying templates to Comic Book Superheroes, Cap's a former <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Chiron Acquisitions Specialist</span>, with a lot of Teamwork Techniques, Physical Skills and Merits. If you wanted Deviant!Cap, however, Hibernation would be thematically appropriate, seeing that he's more of a Skill and Attribute-monkey than anything too flashy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree with everything but <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">that</span>, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">TFV</span> would be more appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T06:02:55-08:00","id":796797,"title":"","content":"For me the questions are how Deviant is going to be different than &quot;Mortals with Supernatural Merits&quot; from the CofD core. I get that, for instance, some psychic characters id Deviant are the results of attempting to create Telepaths like those with the Telepathy merit - it is successful but with unforseen side-effects. I also get that it covers that last major splat from gothic gaming - the Invisible Man/Mr. Hyde type character.<br /> <br /> However, I just worry that its something that we could have just done with a CofD supplement rather than a complete new game and that Deviant won't mesh setting-wise well with other merits say, the psychic merits from the CofD core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:38:58-08:00","id":796961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=795355#post795355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI agree with everything but <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">that</span>, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">TFV</span> would be more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keyword here being <i>former. </i>It explains his augmentations better than TFV's supertech, although he might go TFV for his shield and body armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:06:56-08:00","id":797159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=796961#post796961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keyword here being <i>former. </i>It explains his augmentations better than TFV's supertech, although he might go TFV for his shield and body armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would probably stat Project: Rebirth as a joint venture between TFV and The Ascending Ones; the Super Soldier serum is basically a long-term Elixir, developed by/for the U.S. Army.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXA