omethean 2d comes out their own splat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:16:46-08:00","id":798531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=798056#post798056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While it might change in second edition, the AO are not alchemists in first edition, they have zip zero nada ability to make a new elixir, they get them from djinn or actual alchemists and then add poison.<br /> <br /> Which means that unless you think a supersoldier serum that kills most of the people who tries it is a feature and not a bug, they would at best be no help whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Alchemists in the cofd can be found among the vampires, mages, thaumaturges, sorcerers and mummies who've broken their leash, and when promethean 2d comes out their own splat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTrue, but the AO were closet thing to potion-makers among HUNTERS, not supers in general. There have been stories in which it was implied that Dr. Erskine's formula was something of a &quot;Hieronymus Box&quot;, which I suppose would make Erskine a Mage, or maybe a Hedge Wizard?","signa