bcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=800328#post800328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shinma, Aesir Pharmaceuticals, Star Labs, AIM.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bRight, forgot A.I.M., I'll go add them to my list!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:08:19-08:00","id":803467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=799705#post799705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, what kind of evil corporations and organizations from fiction would be perfect for this game? We obviously have the Umbrella corporation, but what other suggestions do you have?</div> </div> </div> </div> As a member of the SCP Foundation wiki, I am eagerly anticipating the chance to one day play a Deviant Chronicle that flips the traditional perspective of said site: you are not an Agent of the Foundation or another Group Of Interest who hunts anomalies, you ARE the anomaly on the run from these ruthless organizations. <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Here's a list of the factions that could be adapted to CofD and Deviant.</b></a> Imagine what it must be like to be taken in by Dr. Wondertainment (TM) and be turned into a trademarked mutant with gimmicks meant to entertain as if you were a living toy, but said Doctor (if they are even a human being) has a very reckless and sometimes downright alien definition of what is fun. Or imagine that you are an orphan living in the streets, but you have a potentially spectacle-worthy talent or supernatural power, and you are approached by Hermann Fuller's Circus Of The Disquieting. The more you define your life and identity around the Circus, the more you find your gift seeping into you and changing you.<br /> <br /> There's a mountain of excellent inspirational material there, but I wish you perseverance to overcome the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ArchivePanic\" target=\"_blank\"><b>archive panic</b></a> you will feel when the extent of the setting becomes apparent. If by any chance you would like to narrow things down, you can use the <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/tag-search\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Tag Search</b></a>, and focus on tags like &quot;humanoid&quot;. If that doesn't help, you can send me a private message and I'll try to help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:27:22-08:00","id":803476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=803158#post803158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, what kind of deviant you would like to be? Is there any character in fiction that you would like to use as your template? In my case, I would love to play a character similar to the one from a movie I love called Darkman, which I think is a great inspiration for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div> I might very well want to play something different after reading the book, but what I look forward to playing right now is something along the lines of a character from bioshock or prototype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:03:26-08:00","id":803718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=803158#post803158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, what kind of deviant you would like to be? Is there any character in fiction that you would like to use as your template? In my case, I would love to play a character similar to the one from a movie I love called Darkman, which I think is a great inspiration for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helena Hyde. (&quot;Helena&quot; referring to the Helena from Orphan Black, and &quot;Hyde&quot; to an experiment along the lines you'd probably expect).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:20:50-08:00","id":803755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=803467#post803467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As a member of the SCP Foundation wiki, I am eagerly anticipating the chance to one day play a Deviant Chronicle that flips the traditional perspective of said site: you are not an Agent of the Foundation or another Group Of Interest who hunts anomalies, you ARE the anomaly on the run from these ruthless organizations. <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Here's a list of the factions that could be adapted to CofD and Deviant.</b></a> Imagine what it must be like to be taken in by Dr. Wondertainment (TM) and be turned into a trademarked mutant with gimmicks meant to entertain as if you were a living toy, but said Doctor (if they are even a human being) has a very reckless and sometimes downright alien definition of what is fun. Or imagine that you are an orphan living in the streets, but you have a potentially spectacle-worthy talent or supernatural power, and you are approached by Hermann Fuller's Circus Of The Disquieting. The more you define your life and identity around the Circus, the more you find your gift seeping into you and changing you.<br /> <br /> There's a mountain of excellent inspirational material there, but I wish you perseverance to overcome the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ArchivePanic\" target=\"_blank\"><b>archive panic</b></a> you will feel when the extent of the setting becomes apparent. If by any chance you would like to narrow things down, you can use the <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/tag-search\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Tag Search</b></a>, and focus on tags like &quot;humanoid&quot;. If that doesn't help, you can send me a private message and I'll try to help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! thank you very much, I will check it out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:57:54-08:00","id":804594,"title":"","content":"After looking through the inspirations, I'm honestly interested in what direction they're going to go with this gameline. The underground secret society seems to be a given. However, the tone and mood have got me a bit confused. I mean, with the noted influences of Fringe and Videodrome, it does seem like there is a global experimentation angle. However, it does note a lot of Cronenberg movies, so does that mean that Deviants have to worry about that sort of thing if their powers get out of control? Or will there be a more psychological horror angle? Maybe a mix of body horror and psychological thriller? Either way, I cannot wait to see what comes of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10600-howlingseas23","name":"HowlingSeas23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T20:07:57-08:00","id":820695,"title":"","content":"I remembered that the Hulk was cited as one of the inspirations for Deviant, so I decided to post <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dyQpEoMFF3w\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the opening for the 1996 Incredible Hulk cartoon.</b></a> It's great for getting into that &quot;I can't catch a break&quot; mindset. I also wanna share <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pXHeuRMc6ak\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the intro for the Men In Black cartoon</b></a>, which has a vibe of impersonal and professional hunting of the abnormal. Also, is it just me, or are the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles pretty much Deviants?<br /> <br /> Another thought that occurred to me was that Deviants might be splat with the most incentive for criminal activity, right alongside Changeling. The level of organization among Deviants is piquing my imagination as well. Do they tend towards extremely tightly knit groups motivated by mutual interest like Changelings, or is it an every-man-for-himself deal? Probably a juxtaposition of the two, which might overlap a bit with Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T20:19:57-08:00","id":820701,"title":"","content":"I'm biased because I love ideology and organizations. It definitely made it (even) harder for me to get into Beast when there weren't any. I hope we at least get modular examples like Hunter or Changeling 2 - which is probably a good comparison since Deviants don't seem to lend themselves to big arching groups like mage or vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T22:41:59-08:00","id":820755,"title":"","content":"I'm a huge sucker for factions and groups, but I'm not sure if Deviants have enough in common in order to band together within anything larger than the coterie/throng/motley equivalent for mutual survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T09:39:11-08:00","id":821048,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm guessing the game will lean towards small groups rather than large societies. Otherwise the outcast concept will probably fizzle. It's probably going to fit comfortably somewhere between Hunter (conspiracies) and Prometheans (honestly optimized for psuedo-solo play).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T09:43:14-08:00","id":821049,"title":"","content":"I think it's going to hedge closer to Promethean and Geist. Having an organised society, even on a city-basis, would stray a little too close to Changeling's mood. They might actually globalise Deviant, Resident Evil style, and have Deviant survivors from all over the world establish some sort of network that allows them to team up temporarily to strike at different organisations. Since the network doesn't actually have a guiding philosophy, it doesn't step on Hunter's toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T09:48:54-08:00","id":821050,"title":"","content":"It's been mentioned that <b>Deviant</b> will contain rules for creating personalized conspiracies for the antagonists, which would be like <b>Mummy</b>'s Cult rules but a little more mechanical and obviously more antagonist oriented.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about a global network of Deviants. <b>Demon </b>or <b>Changeling</b> is a good gauge to me: most are probably street level but with some larger regional support, but the bigger you get the more you attract unwanted attention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T09:52:05-08:00","id":821051,"title":"","content":"Well, I recall someone say that Deviant was going to be about teaming up to take on organisations like Umbrella and the like. I think something that's been unexplored so far is the idea of individuals forming temporary alliances on a global scale, joining not for ideological reasons, but to get something done (maybe Demon might touch on something like this?). I figured it'd fit what we know of Deviant, so I might as well throw my bet on that pot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T10:01:53-08:00","id":821055,"title":"","content":"I imagine their X and Y splats will be a lot looser, in contrast with other supes, so territory and common enemies will probably be the defining ties of Deviant culture, such as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:10:14-08:00","id":821082,"title":"","content":"It's perfectly possible to have large organizations on a global scale without a traditional hierarchical chain of command. A large organization can be sustained by informal means, its leaders are chosen by reputation, and orders are given and obeyed by social influence. Just look at how the ascending ones conspiracy in hunter organizes themselves. It's the best example I can imagine, and the one that makes the most sense with the deviants. There are many other examples: the majority of compacts, and the way demons organize in ideologies. . Another great example is the organization firewall, from the game eclipse phase, take a look at it too. My point is that there are options to make it work and make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:21:50-08:00","id":821399,"title":"","content":"Dave has said that Deviant templates are 'unstable.' This, coupled with the fact that potentially every Deviant could have a separate organization behind their transformation, makes me think that Deviants don't really view each other as kindred. There's so much potential in how one differs from the next that it'd be a bit much to think that, for example, Buffy would team up with Sarah Manning.<br /> <br /> This is sort of one of the problems I have with <b>Changeling the Lost</b>, too, but those characters at least have more in common.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I can't see why some Deviants come together. Like I said, I just can't picture global networks of them. Their numbers aren't high enough and their situations can be too disparate. Sometimes I wonder if this would be a better 'crossover game' than <b>Beast</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:48:11-08:00","id":821417,"title":"","content":"Personally, I feel like that very reason supports a more informal global organisation, rather than an actual society with philosophies and the like. You can have global organisations, as Firanai proposed, but you can also have a global network that merely offers information and facilitates communication, like Geist's Twilight Network. That way, Deviants can team up for short periods of time, so they don't have to agree with each other, and you can keep the &quot;local&quot; play in-between team-ups fairly isolated and Promethean-style.<br /> <br /> Sorta like the Avengers in the movies, if you think of it that way. The chronicles have some stories where it's just the local Deviant group taking care of business in their city or just travelling around, and special stories where they team up with other Deviants from around the world to strike a massive blow at a shady organisation. And then once that's dealt with, everyone goes back to dealing with their local problems. Hell, if your group is up for it (or you play via PbP), you can further refine each local story into a Deviant's solo adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:45:00-08:00","id":821435,"title":"","content":"I like that.<br /> <br /> I would work it by taking the supportive regional groups and saying they have contacts with other regional groups around the world. They're not united by a shared philosophy but yeah sometimes you gotta call in the A-team","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T00:21:27-08:00","id":821471,"title":"","content":"It would also make sense if the game assumes that by default PCs have been changed by the same organisation, and communal building of your Nemesis organisation is part of character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T02:56:36-08:00","id":821518,"title":"","content":"Only if it they were willing to piss players off, or make the whole situation not make sense.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty evident that deviants are a varied bunch, which would mean that all the players are variations on a theme (hampering player options) if they have the same makers, or making the organization hunting them make no sense.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the organizations hunting the deviant is that they are a resource. The stereotype is five players, well if an organization can change five people, why are they worrying about the escaped prototype and his four friends when they can just use what must be a successful process to mass produce their own superminions?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the player characters are the result of the same organization having multiple successful projects, then there is absolutely no reason to believe that the organization doesn't have more successful projects, in which case, again, why are they concerned about the PCs again? <br /> <br /> The other option is to make it a debate everytime a group wants to start a deviant game, an added hassle no other game in cofd requires.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T03:37:45-08:00","id":821528,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if it was bent towards 1 deviant and the rest are mortals or pure solo games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T04:25:57-08:00","id":821535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821518#post821518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only if it they were willing to piss players off, or make the whole situation not make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about cutting the hyperbole?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821518#post821518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems pretty evident that deviants are a varied bunch, which would mean that all the players are variations on a theme (hampering player options) if they have the same makers, or making the organization hunting them make no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a situation where the players create the antagonist faction the choice whether they want one large organisation against them or several smaller, more varied ones would be up to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T04:43:31-08:00","id":821544,"title":"","content":"You don't need five successful projects to get five different Deviants. You can have five escapees/survivors of a project/incident that produces different mutations, or an arcane ritual that aligns each of the sacrificial victims with a different element, or a single &quot;cyborg hit squad&quot; that had each squad member with a different set of implants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T06:19:10-08:00","id":821580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821518#post821518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only if it they were willing to piss players off, or make the whole situation not make sense.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty evident that deviants are a varied bunch, which would mean that all the players are variations on a theme (hampering player options) if they have the same makers, or making the organization hunting them make no sense...The other option is to make it a debate everytime a group wants to start a deviant game, an added hassle no other game in cofd requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a whole lot of negative conjecture to me. It's as simple as looking at <b>Promethean</b> - a game that already has years of history - and saying, &quot;Oh, looks like this won't be the case after all.&quot; Literally absolutely <i>zero</i> of the games require PCs to share a social splat and, as mentioned, <b>Promethean</b> doesn't require you to share origins among PCs so why make the assumption about Deviant?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821528#post821528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be surprised if it was bent towards 1 deviant and the rest are mortals or pure solo games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Deviants are intended to be the lowest power splat (bar <b>Hunter</b>) I <i>would </i>be surprised","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T06:44:40-08:00","id":821591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_contain