etc.<br /> And please. Do not indicate that's all Fae job.<br /> <br /> Who feels like me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:35:22-08:00","id":821638,"title":"","content":"I'd be surprised if there wasn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:45:06-08:00","id":821646,"title":"","content":"That's actually something I loved to do about Technocracy-focused game in old WoD. I gave Numina &quot;Psychic Phenomena&quot; along with derangements to many player characters who just survived meeting with aliens from another dimensions (smells like Cthulhu-Tec <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) And now when I discovered this would be 11-th game itself about it... it must be so.<br /> It makes sense to me when there would be religion organisation like truly-screwed scientologists awaiting for cosmic ship taking them awaaaay. That's how many &quot;random deviants&quot; would remain organisation. Somehow.<br /> That's the general feeling bout that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:12:23-08:00","id":821707,"title":"","content":"Just give me some oWOD Fomori-style character builds and I'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:32:50-08:00","id":821717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821535#post821535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a situation where the players create the antagonist faction the choice whether they want one large organisation against them or several smaller, more varied ones would be up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Deviants are meant to be changed by an organisation at all - self made ones will be possible. Though that doesn't rule out an organisation or organisations being after them, it would just be to study them. (It also provides a reason for it to be one organisation after them all, if that's what the players want).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T14:50:01-08:00","id":821887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821707#post821707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just give me some oWOD Fomori-style character builds and I'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you did there...<br /> <img src=\"http://s23.postimg.org/j5fs9u30b/image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> you sir are truly a deviant!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T15:22:08-08:00","id":821913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821887#post821887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you did there...<br /> <img src=\"http://s23.postimg.org/j5fs9u30b/image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> you sir are truly a deviant!</div> </div> </div> </div>........thank you so much for the mental image Lunar. I didn't need to know that option existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T15:25:57-08:00","id":821916,"title":"","content":"Seriously, how the hell do you organize deviants? With so many different origins and possibilities I just can't come with an effective way. The only thing they share is that they have been changed against their will, that's a very broad term. If the developers want to go with the 5 types, five organizations structure then my suggestion is that their type depends on which organization changed them, and faction on their motivation. Tell me what you think, of course, this is mere speculation done for pure fun, not because I have any idea of what they will do.<br /> Those changed by corporations reflect greed, those changed by governments reflect a desire for dominance, those changed by cults reflect a desire for knowledge, those changed by aliens (both extraterrestrial and extradimensional) reflect alien concepts, and finally, those change by accidents reflect the randomness of the universe.<br /> Then we have ideologies. We have the ones motivated by vengeance, who want to destroy their creators no matter what; there are those obsessed with finding a cure; Those who want to hide and start new lives; those who want to rescue others like them and expose the organizations; and those who embrace their change and seek more power. They are not mutually exclusive; it all depends on which one the deviant chooses to focus on.<br /> I think I discussed this in this forum in the past, but I don\u2019t remember.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T16:04:40-08:00","id":821948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821916#post821916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how the hell do you organize deviants? With so many different origins and possibilities I just can't come with an effective way. The only thing they share is that they have been changed against their will, that's a very broad term. If the developers want to go with the 5 types, five organizations structure then my suggestion is that their type depends on which organization changed them, and faction on their motivation. Tell me what you think, of course, this is mere speculation done for pure fun, not because I have any idea of what they will do.<br /> Those changed by corporations reflect greed, those changed by governments reflect a desire for dominance, those changed by cults reflect a desire for knowledge, those changed by aliens (both extraterrestrial and extradimensional) reflect alien concepts, and finally, those change by accidents reflect the randomness of the universe.<br /> Then we have ideologies. We have the ones motivated by vengeance, who want to destroy their creators no matter what; there are those obsessed with finding a cure; Those who want to hide and start new lives; those who want to rescue others like them and expose the organizations; and those who embrace their change and seek more power. They are not mutually exclusive; it all depends on which one the deviant chooses to focus on.<br /> I think I discussed this in this forum in the past, but I don\u2019t remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that one faction that's members carry signs stating that they will die or turn evil at the midpoint of the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T16:08:04-08:00","id":821949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821887#post821887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you did there...<br /> <img src=\"http://s23.postimg.org/j5fs9u30b/image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> you sir are truly a deviant!</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't knock relentlessly grotesque body horror. and the opening story in Freak Legions is solid gold Deviant material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:53:27-08:00","id":822015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821591#post821591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that make working with mortals easier? Lower variance in power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it'd be easier. I thought you were saying that the game would be presented that way as default, which I didn't think would be the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:15:27-08:00","id":822025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821916#post821916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how the hell do you organize deviants? With so many different origins and possibilities I just can't come with an effective way. The only thing they share is that they have been changed against their will <b>by a human agency</b>, that's a very broad term <b>though one similar enough to each other for empathy...</b> those change by accidents <b>don't exist, because the fundamental humanity of the force that changed them is key to the gameline.</b>.<br /> Then we have ideologies. We have the ones motivated by vengeance, who want to destroy their creators no matter what; there are those obsessed with finding a cure; Those who want to hide and start new lives; those who want to rescue others like them and expose the organizations; and those who embrace their change and seek more power. They are not mutually exclusive; it all depends on which one the deviant chooses to focus on.<br /> I think I discussed this in this forum in the past, but I don\u2019t remember.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You missed something DaveB said. All the people who create Deviants are, well, people; there's a human face involved somewhere, someone who is capable of viewing other people as a resource in need of harvesting and retrieval. True, that face can be the Deviant's own, and there's positive examples of those who volunteered for the process regardless, but the average Deviant is not Captain America, but the Winter Soldier after he starts regaining his free will.<br /> <br /> That's something to band together over right there, while differently origin'd Deviants can and do get along perfectly well, their creators...often mutually despise each other barging in on &quot;their property&quot;.<br /> <br /> Good call on possible social splats, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:33:36-08:00","id":822033,"title":"","content":"The whole deviant thing reminds me of a webm I saw a little while ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/Oi0WpEb\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/Oi0WpEb\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/Oi0WpEb\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/gallery/Oi0WpEb </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (Why OPP hasn't gotten the forum able to accept webm and gifv yet I have no idea)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:45:24-08:00","id":822035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=822015#post822015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it'd be easier. I thought you were saying that the game would be presented that way as default, which I didn't think would be the case</div> </div> </div> </div>I was sorta. I mean, mummy is effectively a solo game and 2e has had a greater focus on weaker characters with things like demon-blooded, ghouls and wolf-bloods and mortals with supernatural merits being more playable. So I really wouldn't be surprised if 1 deviant with multiple mortals was a suggested course of action in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:10:43-08:00","id":822205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821580#post821580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a whole lot of negative conjecture to me. It's as simple as looking at <b>Promethean</b> - a game that already has years of history - and saying, &quot;Oh, looks like this won't be the case after all.&quot; Literally absolutely <i>zero</i> of the games require PCs to share a social splat and, as mentioned, <b>Promethean</b> doesn't require you to share origins among PCs so why make the assumption about Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div> Erm, what part of my saying such a basis for the game would risk pissing off players or making the game not make sense did you see as an endorsement of the idea on my part? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T04:59:55-08:00","id":822276,"title":"","content":"I didn't say you endorsed the idea. I said that your assumption, or concern of possibility, of said basis of game was a jumping to conclusion since every game could theoretically have the issue you were talking about and yet every game did not have the conclusion you were pondering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:27:28-08:00","id":822289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=821916#post821916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how the hell do you organize deviants? With so many different origins and possibilities I just can't come with an effective way. T</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen Fight Club? And did I mention many sects and cults - especially UFO cults, which fascinate me as hell?<br /> <br /> If vampires are societies of damned, as they call themselves, many different guys coined by the fact they are damned - then we can have societies of *Support Groups* by medical failures, religious abbuse, degenerated corpo-workers, UFO-abducted, war invalid and so on. That's how I feel it. The same way vampire cliques are club or gentlement clubs or exclusive bdsm clubs for bored yankees.<br /> <br /> You got some point guys - Deviants would be the only supernaturals made by people (or don't they?). It would mean no Dark Mother, Fae, Atlantis, Demiurges but just organisations. Like Dark Angel Jessica Alba stuff. I see so much Technocratic (and Cheiron Group) material here. Runaway clones, rebel hybrids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:35:45-08:00","id":822292,"title":"","content":"Demiurges are still mortal, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:38:10-08:00","id":822294,"title":"","content":"Also, nothing says that supernaturals/aliens couldn't make Deviant, at least so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:29:10-08:00","id":823877,"title":"","content":"I wonder where the inspiration for deviant came from, I love it, but I believe it fits better in a science setting than a heavy supernatural one like the world of darkness, and what are they going to do next? What creatures are left?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:55:03-08:00","id":823888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=823877#post823877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder where the inspiration for deviant came from, I love it, but I believe it fits better in a science setting than a heavy supernatural one like the world of darkness, and what are they going to do next? What creatures are left?</div> </div> </div> </div> The sort of science that results in Deviants is probably tainted by the supernatural in some small but crucial way, and Hellboy has already been mentioned in this thread as a possible Deviant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:57:39-08:00","id":823891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=823888#post823888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The sort of science that results in Deviants is probably tainted by the supernatural in some small but crucial way, and Hellboy has already been mentioned in this thread as a possible Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comic Abe fits even better, since he was not born that way but rather turned into the creature he is now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:10:05-08:00","id":823903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=823891#post823891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comic Abe fits even better, since he was not born that way but rather turned into the creature he is now</div> </div> </div> </div> So does Comic Liz. The levels of destruction she can and has caused are very similar to this Blowout mode that Deviants will have. Also, take a look at this quote from her page on the Hellboy wiki:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sherman's pyrokinesis appears to be something above and beyond &quot;typical&quot; pyrokinesis; more than once it has been hinted that her powers stem from some sort of entity or presence that dwells inside her, one that isn't necessarily based on fire but rather energy in general. In Seed of Destruction Rasputin referred to Sherman's powers as a living thing, hinting that it might be separate from her in some way. If this is true, then it would seem the &quot;entity&quot; that gives Sherman her pyrokinesis shares a symbiotic relationship with her; removal of her powers has been shown to be extremely damaging and even lethal to her. It is also possible that her powers stem from a portion of her soul instead of a separate being; in Hollow Earth her energy is stolen away, leaving her body an empty husk. Her imprisoned powers are shown to look and act like her, insinuating that they are, in fact, her. In either case, it is clear that Sherman's pyrokinesis is a vital part of her being, necessary for keeping her alive. </div> </div> </div>I bet that removing a Deviant's grafts or equivalent is almost invariably fatal. It adds to the terror and callousness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:37:07-08:00","id":824049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=823877#post823877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder where the inspiration for deviant came from, I love it, but I believe it fits better in a science setting than a heavy supernatural one like the world of darkness, and what are they going to do next? What creatures are left?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant is Sense8, Orphan Black, Fringe, The Fly, Hulk, Guyver, Tetsuo the Iron Man, Akira, Hollow Man, Jekyll, V for Vendetta, Videodrome, Existenz, Scanners, Dark Angel, several versions of Beauty and the Beast, John Doe, Kyle XY...</div> </div> </div> </div>He's mentioned Buffy in the past and more recently, too.<br /> <br /> Part of the blurb we got upon its announcement mentioned how Deviants are made on a ritual altar as much as a lab table, so we'll see how much 'science setting' there is to it. We <i>do</i> have <b>Promethean </b>and <b>Demon</b>, remember. That's to say nothing of Ordo Dracul, Cheiron Group, or Last Dynasty International","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:20:57-08:00","id":824689,"title":"","content":"If changelings are creating organisations (Courts) by the only mutual feel of &quot;being victims&quot; then deviants can do similarly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:44:38-08:00","id":824703,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but they're out for revenge, too, and the last thing they want to do is let everyone's big enemy start teaming up with one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T08:54:45-08:00","id":824954,"title":"","content":"well by that<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Deviant is about people turned into supernatural beings by human actors \u2013 their transformation is \u201cmessy\u201d compared to other beings, and they don\u2019t end up with an entirely stable \u201ctemplate\u201d. Most are the result of human conspiracies, cults, mad science, and other groups. Even those whose change was self-inflicted are sought as assets. PC Deviants are the ones who\u2019ve escaped the clutches of their conspiracy \u2013 for now \u2013 and have a thirst for revenge.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Deviant is Sense8, Orphan Black, Fringe, The Fly, Hulk, Guyver, Tetsuo The Iron Man, Akira, Hollow Man, Jekyll, V for Vendetta, Videodrome, Existenz, Scanners, Dark Angel, several versions of Beauty and the Beast, John Doe, Kyle XY\u2026 One thing I quickly realized after Rose and Rich handed me the blurb you\u2019ve seen in the catalog and asked me to make a game out of it is how much inspirational media there is for it, which we\u2019ve not tapped so far.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Many (but, crucially, not all) powers will be physically obvious. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Counter to the trend to increase \u201cpower level\u201d over recent games, because the bulk of their foes are normal (albeit organized) people, they will trend to being the street level. The potential for Akira or Dr Manhatten-style blowouts will be there, but most Deviants will be the lowest-powered full game protagonists bar Hunters.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid nWoD will be too Marvel-ous (because it surely is now very comic, less noir-modern-gothic one). But using this nomenclature - if there are evil conspiracies creating Jessica Alba Hybrids then X-Men can group up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 02-06-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T09:02:37-08:00","id":824956,"title":"","content":"Yes, there's more than enough reason to believe players can group up, but having entire societies based around the idea is a bit much, especially for what amounts to basically freaks and terrorists.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry about it being too comic booky, at least too superhero comic book-like. That will surely be an option but the thrust of Chronicles of Darkness is mystery, and finding out who did it and 'why me' might be a big thrust of things, rather than using their powers to be heroes. Plus since you are basically both going after and running from an organization that outnumbers you, in infrastructure and population, there's probably going to be a lot more of the thriller, like the inspiration of Scanners, or Jason Bourne.<br /> <br /> That said, traditionally there's a group of survivors or other experimented on who fight back against individual companies, occasionally with the help of a rogue employee who hated what they were doing all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:57:13-08:00","id":825138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=824954#post824954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well by that<br /> <br /> I'm afraid nWoD will be too Marvel-ous (because it surely is now very comic, less noir-modern-gothic one). But using this nomenclature - if there are evil conspiracies creating Jessica Alba Hybrids then X-Men can group up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice that Hulk was the only marvel one mentioned. And that's because it's a guy who has been warped by science into a monster that can gain powers at the cost of his mind and personality turning into a raving beast. So, basically werewolf style horror of not being in control and can flip out at any moment rather than some sort of Comic tones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T16:46:17-08:00","id":825155,"title":"","content":"Also he was constantly hunted and everything bad that happened was blamed on him, though admittedly a lot of it was his own fault. I think the dogged chase is something we'll be likely to see, more than the True Fae who 'might' send someone after you or come to find you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:05:49-08:00","id":825169,"title":"","content":"He's essentially a modern (well, okay, 60s) version of Dr Jekyll, who is himself a very Deviant sort of a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T20:22:28-08:00","id":825228,"title":"","content":"We were talking about movies and this one in particular, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3551400/\" target=\"_blank\">Unnatural</a>. The idea being that animals are genetically modified and it leads to horrific and deadly results, which is a huge trope in horror and sci-fi. So I was wondering if there might be Preclinical Deviants, basically animals that have been tested and either abandoned, released or recruited. So you could be chased by dogs with the same mutations as yourself or hyper-intelligent rats or something similar, which seems like it could be a really interesting thing to play off of. They wouldn't even all have to work for the Organization, some could just be neutral or maddened, or even willing to bond with human Deviants.<br /> <br /> Vestiges of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watchers_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Watchers</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/We3\" target=\"_blank\">We3</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2016, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:17:18-08:00","id":825288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825228#post825228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about movies and this one in particular, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3551400/\" target=\"_blank\">Unnatural</a>. <b>The idea being that animals are genetically modified and it leads to horrific and deadly results, which is a huge trope in horror and sci-fi. So I was wondering if there might be Preclinical Deviants, basically animals that have been tested and either abandoned, released or recruited. So you could be chased by dogs with the same mutations as yourself or hyper-intelligent rats or something similar, which seems like it could be a really interesting thing to play off of</b>. They wouldn't even all have to work for the Organization, some could just be neutral or maddened, or even willing to bond with human Deviants.<br /> <br /> Vestiges of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watchers_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Watchers</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/We3\" target=\"_blank\">We3</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should pitch this for the inevitable Night Horrors book, because it sounds like the premise of a game a wanted to make, Nimh: the Revolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:48:39-08:00","id":825297,"title":"","content":"I imagine if Deviant animal friends became available you would get <i>a lot</i> of use out of the True Friend merit.<br /> <br /> No one's going to want to pull an Old Yeller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:49:09-08:00","id":825368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825138#post825138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice that Hulk was the only marvel one mentioned. And that's because it's a guy who has been warped by science into a monster that can gain powers at the cost of his mind and personality turning into a raving beast. So, basically werewolf style horror of not being in control and can flip out at any moment rather than some sort of Comic tones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Captain America has been mentioned more than a few times too.<br /> <br /> IMO I wouldn't worry to much. Modern goth is pretty much a Vampire thing. It's not a general Chronicles of Darkness thing. There's nothing Gothic about Hunter: the Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:27:48-08:00","id":825441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825368#post825368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Captain America has been mentioned more than a few times too.<br /> <br /> IMO I wouldn't worry to much. Modern goth is pretty much a Vampire thing. It's not a general Chronicles of Darkness thing. <b>There's nothing Gothic about Hunter: the Vigil.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to disagree, and I am pretty sure Bram Stoker, James Cameron, and Ridley Scott, among others, would back me up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:03:00-08:00","id":825476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825441#post825441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to disagree, and I am pretty sure Bram Stoker, James Cameron, and Ridley Scott, among others, would back me up.</div> </div> </div> </div>????<br /> <br /> Not sure what they have to do with it. They didn't write Hunter: the Vigil. Flavor-wise its text has always reminded more of 80s military/survivalist action novels than any of the works by the folks you mentioned. YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:58:15-08:00","id":825507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825476#post825476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ????<br /> <br /> Not sure what they have to do with it. They didn't write Hunter: the Vigil. Flavor-wise its text has always reminded more of 80s military/survivalist action novels than any of the works by the folks you mentioned. YMMV</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula is as much about Van Helsing's cell, and their pursuit of Dracula, as it is about Dracula. The Alien franchise is quite Gothic while again largely being a David and Goliath-style monster hunt.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying, and this probably isn't your read of the material, is that there's more to Gothic Horror than Vampires, Werewolves, and melodramatic preening, and that plenty of those other things can and should show up in Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:39:43-08:00","id":825536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825507#post825507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula is as much about Van Helsing's cell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quincey Morris was a man worthy of the title of Hunter and died as a badass. I will fight anyone that says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T10:48:42-08:00","id":826065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825507#post825507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula is as much about Van Helsing's cell, and their pursuit of Dracula, as it is about Dracula. The Alien franchise is quite Gothic while again largely being a David and Goliath-style monster hunt.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying, and this probably isn't your read of the material, is that there's more to Gothic Horror than Vampires, Werewolves, and melodramatic preening, and that plenty of those other things can and should show up in Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I'm not following. Yes you can use Gothic themed works as an inspiration but nothing about the Hunter: the Vigil text screams Gothic. <br /> <br /> There is no overarching Gothic thematicelement running through the various Chronicles of Darkness gmaelines. Specifically in Hunter's case, that's an element that the story teller has to introduce.<br /> <br /> IMO, there's no requirement that any of the games have a Gothic feel to them. This is not, after all, the grimdark future of Warhammer 40k.<br /> <br /> Also the Alien series is more surreal than Gothic and arguably some adaptations of Stoker are more Baroque (looking at you Coppola) than Gothic.<br /> <br /> At any rate, there's no reason that Deviant need be any of the above. It's enough that it focus on (personal) horror and mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:25:07-08:00","id":826375,"title":"","content":"Clearly, we aren't using the same definitions of gothic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:35:43-08:00","id":826730,"title":"","content":"Here I thought Alien was a slasher story written by Lovecraft by way of Freud","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:55:44-08:00","id":826824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=826730#post826730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here I thought Alien was a slasher story written by Lovecraft by way of Freud</div> </div> </div> </div>The man was not too fond of Freud's sexual analysis. I suspect he was more in line with the esoteric side of Jung and that the stuff that brings up sexual imagery in his work it's definitely there but not part of a conscious choice, as if it slipped in along the way. Even when that's the focus of the horror, it's all pretty muffled, which, then again, it's not a surprise.<br /> <br /> I often find myself giggling at the thought of how he would react to the H.R. Giger's works he inspired<br /> <br /> EDIT: That was a way too serious answer. Sorry, I just took a pause from writing my college thesis and after all these hours I still have the S.T. Joshi's biography impressed in my brain. I'll see myself out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-09-2016, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:52:47-08:00","id":826854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=826375#post826375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, we aren't using the same definitions of gothic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. Of your examples only Stoker really fits as an example of Gothic literature. Alien is always going to be 50% science fiction and many of the key aspects of Gothic literarure (like romance) are completely absent from it so it favors horror more strongly than terror.<br /> <br /> I see were you're trying to invoke &quot;Gothic&quot; as a literary genre but I don't agree that it needs to be the centerpiece genre of a game like Hunter, which IMO has a great deal of survivalism in its DNA. &quot;The monsters are everywhere. And your characters can fight back.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want something more specifically Gothic then you have to go back to Hunter's roots -- the Chronicles of Darkness core game. Games like Vampire and Promethean have more Gothic DNA in them (as they lend themselves to the romance aspect necessary for true Gothic literature) than games like Werewolf and Mage which mix in other themes (like crime drama in the case of Werewolf and urban fantasy in the case of Mage). And really in the final analysis, if all the games were all Gothic, all the time, they'd all be the same game, which makes for a dull experience.<br /> <br /> Final thought, the inspirational material sections of these games is always a good tell of what literary genres and themes the game is going to mix together. In the case of Hunter, I'd expect more Van Helsing (the movie) or Helsing (the anime) than Stoker's Dracula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-09-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:23:59-08:00","id":826878,"title":"","content":"I remembered another Deviant-esque character that's more arcane than technological: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Darkness_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jackie Estacado</b></a>. A criminal who gains strange and horrific powers that people want to rip out from his corpse to use for their own goals? Check. Street-level conflicts? Check. Potential for short bursts of devastating power at great cost (i.e. giving in to the sibilant whispers and demonic snarls of the Darkness)? Check. All too human antagonists trying to lure out the protagonist by threatening and killing those he cares about? Check. The video game adaptations of the comic are really cool, to boot.<br /> <br /> On a more lighthearted note, we have Deviants like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_10\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Ben10</b></a>. He has a lot more powers than a normal Deviant will apparently have, but it still fits.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think the different versions of Kamen Rider have been mentioned in this thread too. I, for one, wouldn't mind playing Ultraman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:45:56-08:00","id":827615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=826878#post826878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered another Deviant-esque character that's more arcane than technological: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Darkness_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jackie Estacado</b></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of the characters from the TopCow-verse would fit. The Witchblade is usually touted as an artefact, but Sarah Pezzini is like a Deviant than the owner of a Relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:14:28-08:00","id":827641,"title":"","content":"They are the result of some sort of occultish paradigm, though. It's been years but I think there was an organization or at least a power behind it, and further powers trying to take advantage of it in more modern times.<br /> <br /> It begs the question, how disassociated can a Deviant be from their Organization? Dave has said that Buffy is a Deviant, and counted her turning against the Watchers, though they weren't originally the ones that 'created' her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:26:44-08:00","id":827652,"title":"","content":"Not all Deviants are made by others; it's been stated that they might be self-created, though I can't remember whether they can come about by accident. But an enemy organisation could just as easily be trying to control or study them as make them, and the Watchers sure did their best to control the Slayers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:41:34-08:00","id":827667,"title":"","content":"Wait, I might be late to the party and someone has probably mentioned it but, now that I think about it. the manga Claymore offers great inspiration about Deviants and the relationship with the creators. I'ts one of the main sources of drama in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:49:29-08:00","id":827672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=827641#post827641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It begs the question, how disassociated can a Deviant be from their Organization? Dave has said that Buffy is a Deviant, and counted her turning against the Watchers, though they weren't originally the ones that 'created' her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they kinda were. Or rather, their ancestors were the ones who created the First Slayer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T11:59:33-08:00","id":827681,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, it's been years. I remembered the First Slayer, I forgot about the Shadow Men, I thought she was a 'natural' supernatural occurrence.<br /> <br /> It seems like it's going to be another very versatile game, I'm really digging it already and I haven't gotten this hyped about a <i>new </i>RPG for years. Though with how the new editions, Blood and Smoke and the Idigam Chronicle have come along and even Fallen World is getting me interested it's a good time to be an Onyx Path fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-10-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T08:24:28-08:00","id":828801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=825368#post825368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Captain America has been mentioned more than a few times too.<br /> <br /> IMO I wouldn't worry to much. Modern goth is pretty much a Vampire thing. It's not a general Chronicles of Darkness thing. There's nothing Gothic about Hunter: the Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cpt. America is slang term of Heroes from BTP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So.. it looks like out protagonists would be hunter by special forces of organisations + Goverment mind-blendered drone-versions of deviants. That's Dark Angel fully.<br /> But still I'm afraid of cartooning influence of comic superheroes. WoD characters are first victims, then supernaturals (at cost).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:24:57-08:00","id":828825,"title":"","content":"Idle thought: Deviant + Dudes Of Legend = <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/GodHand\" target=\"_blank\">God Hand</a></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:23:06-08:00","id":829678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=828801#post828801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cpt. America is slang term of Heroes from BTP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So.. it looks like out protagonists would be hunter by special forces of organisations + Goverment mind-blendered drone-versions of deviants. That's Dark Angel fully.<br /> But still I'm afraid of cartooning influence of comic superheroes. WoD characters are first victims, then supernaturals (at cost).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry about this. I'm skeptical that the text is going to have outright superhero riffs. I'm expecting something more along the lines of The Alligator People or The Fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:17:57-08:00","id":829744,"title":"","content":"Though Alligator People are comical, this is still creepy stuff if you imagine this happens to you.<br /> <br /> Also you know what I'd love to incorporate into the game? If we have room for sci-fi horror stuff, then The Thing is a must for me. Disfigurement and other body horror like a Tzimisce victims. One last time when I could freely go with The Thing stuff, were Pandoran Mockeries :&gt; Not to confuse with purely Lovecraftian creatures from the Abyss etc.<br /> <br /> Well, still waiting for first 5 biological clans and 5 organisations for Deviants <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd love to have prelude of character in remote psychiatric clinic or being kidnapped to ufo medical deck. I wonder about mechanical stuff, for example morality system or energy stuff. It should be something about &quot;unexpected side-effects&quot; that regularly torment our character. Just like build-in flaw which will pop-up in the worst moment (UFO-kidnapped psycher loses his control for a night and doesnt remember it - thanks to the under-skin chip? :s )<br /> <br /> Also I gave a lucky guess: Black Dog parodied every game - also Trinity Universe. Aberrant about Novas (mutated celebrities with powers, sounds familiar?) was renamed as, you can guess, The Deviant :P Maybe it is reincorporation of the theme into nWoD. Or just a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 02-14-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:01:44-08:00","id":829776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=829744#post829744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though Alligator People are comical, this is still creepy stuff if you imagine this happens to you.<br /> <br /> Also you know what I'd love to incorporate into the game? If we have room for sci-fi horror stuff, then The Thing is a must for me. Disfigurement and other body horror like a Tzimisce victims. One last time when I could freely go with The Thing stuff, were Pandoran Mockeries :&gt; Not to confuse with purely Lovecraftian creatures from the Abyss etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might give the movie: <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0052549/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0052549/</a> (from 1959) a gander some time. My guess is that Deviant is a game about these kind of experimental victims.<br /> <br /> Regarding The Thing, you'd really need a proper alien game to do it &quot;right&quot; (whatever that really means anyway). In the interim, if you're not adverse to fansplats you might give Alien: the Stranded a whirl. The Thing can be easily recreated using its rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:26:18-08:00","id":830074,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see where they go with this. I like the fact that they start out as normal people. One of the most enjoyable campaigns I played in the oWoD was where everybody started out as a mortal and then got Awakened/Embraced/Realized they were a Were/What-have-you largely by their own choices and actions. Game lines like Promethean, Mummy, and Demon (as fun as they are) do not allow for this &quot;mortal to supernatural conversion&quot; trope. <br /> <br /> I also like the concept inspirations, although I am disappointed that they seem to be aiming this as a minor template instead of a major template. It is hard to do a &quot;Buffy&quot;-esque Slayer if the Slayer cannot actually stand up to a Vampire. I certainly think it is possible to have a splat with empowered mortals without it becoming four-color superheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T09:47:02-08:00","id":830280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=830074#post830074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to see where they go with this. I like the fact that they start out as normal people. One of the most enjoyable campaigns I played in the oWoD was where everybody started out as a mortal and then got Awakened/Embraced/Realized they were a Were/What-have-you largely by their own choices and actions. Game lines like Promethean, Mummy, and Demon (as fun as they are) do not allow for this &quot;mortal to supernatural conversion&quot; trope.<br /> <br /> I also like the concept inspirations, although I am disappointed that they seem to be aiming this as a minor template instead of a major template. It is hard to do a &quot;Buffy&quot;-esque Slayer if the Slayer cannot actually stand up to a Vampire. I certainly think it is possible to have a splat with empowered mortals without it becoming four-color superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The level of power is one of the things that has me the most curious. We only know two things: First, that deviants are going to be above hunters, but below the rest of supernatural splats, that can mean many things. Just with the core book alone, you can pump a regular human with enough supernatural merits to be a serious threat, the same with hunters and their endowements. Second, that they are going to have sort of a &quot;hulk mode&quot; in which they gain a temporary boost in power, but with a cost, which I think is a cool idea. Your regular deviant is more than a match for a regular human, and if he finds something more serious? rage on and kick his ass! I really hope that we can get some more information soon, just something more to speculate about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T14:12:18-08:00","id":830504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=829678#post829678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't worry about this. I'm skeptical that the text is going to have outright superhero riffs. I'm expecting something more along the lines of The Alligator People or The Fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Netflix Marvel series might do for good inspiration. Luke Cage, Nuke, and Killgrave were all made by experiments, and while Jessica was an accident, it was an accident that might have involved shit from the same experimenters. And they offer some ideas for what Deviants might do with themselves if vengeance is done, or not feasible, or just something they don't want to think about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:28:01-08:00","id":830631,"title":"","content":"That's probably too bad for nWoD, becase people talk about COMICS as inspirations, not classic horror books like it was with Vampires and it's folklore. Deviants aren't folkloric stuff, but still I prefer good reading, urban legends and conspiracy theories, not Marvel superheroes. If not belles-lettres, then still something like medium-literature like S. King. It may be dark and gloom but this is still candy-marvel, and that's not the way of game, which causes people to katharsis and expand mind horizons. If the WoD game can't do this, it is written wrong and with bad sources, inspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 02-15-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:42:42-08:00","id":830639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=830631#post830631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably too bad for nWoD, becase people talk about COMICS as inspirations, not classic horror books like it was with Vampires and it's folklore. Deviants aren't folkloric stuff, but still I prefer good reading, urban legends and conspiracy theories, not Marvel superheroes. If not belles-lettres, then still something like medium-literature like S. King. It may be dark and gloom but this is still candy-marvel, and that's not the way of game, which causes people to katharsis and expand mind horizons. If the WoD game can't do this, it is written wrong and with bad sources, inspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how the show of Jessica Jones is what was being mentioned I think your misunderstanding.... Jessica Jones is dark, focuses on investigation, the characters Aren't heroes, the themes are 100% psychological in nature, the characters in the show are treated as conspiracy theories and urban legends... It is not candy-marvel, it is something that already fits into Chronicles of Darkness, even without Deviant.<br /> <br /> That's why it's fine as an inspiration for deviant. Not because it's superheroes that got their powers through science... Because it's a show about superhuman creatures having to deal with psychological trauma in a world that fears them, without them having a choice in the matter because other people took their oppertunities to be normal away from them. It wasn't fey, a primordial beast, the dark mother, spirits... humans broke them and now they are monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:43:04-08:00","id":831018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=830639#post830639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how the show of Jessica Jones is what was being mentioned I think your misunderstanding.... Jessica Jones is dark, focuses on investigation, the characters Aren't heroes, the themes are 100% psychological in nature, the characters in the show are treated as conspiracy theories and urban legends... It is not candy-marvel, it is something that already fits into Chronicles of Darkness, even without Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expound: Jessica Jones herself spends the whole series recovering, or not-so-recovering, from extreme trauma inflicted at the hands of Killgrave, himself broken by experiments carried out on him as a child. Luke was experimented on in prison, and is mostly trying to put it out of his mind, but there's some kind of organisation that's still interested in him. Nuke (never actually called that in the series) was also experimented on, via a drug regimen, but signs back up with the experimenter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why it's fine as an inspiration for deviant. Not because it's superheroes that got their powers through science... Because it's a show about superhuman creatures having to deal with psychological trauma in a world that fears them, without them having a choice in the matter because other people took their oppertunities to be normal away from them. It wasn't fey, a primordial beast, the dark mother, spirits... humans broke them and now they are monsters. </div> </div> </div>Yep. And in Daredevil, Matt is a man who received both disabilities and powers in the same accident, and is trying to make a life as a lawyer, until he gets embroiled in the struggles against a socially powerful individual who wants to remake a chunk of the city in his own image, and won't let any victims or vigilantes stand in his way. And there are a couple of warring occult societies, one of which wants to use Matt as a champion and/or weapon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:50:19-08:00","id":831024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=830631#post830631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably too bad for nWoD, becase people talk about COMICS as inspirations, not classic horror books like it was with Vampires and it's folklore. Deviants aren't folkloric stuff, but still I prefer good reading, urban legends and conspiracy theories, not Marvel superheroes. If not belles-lettres, then still something like medium-literature like S. King. It may be dark and gloom but this is still candy-marvel, and that's not the way of game, which causes people to katharsis and expand mind horizons. If the WoD game can't do this, it is written wrong and with bad sources, inspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><i>Comics</i></b> were themselves inspired by classic horror books. The Incredible Hulk is just Dr. Jekyll &amp; Mr. Hyde reskinned. Horror comics dominated the comics market all the way through the early '60s. Our (now) traditional notions of superheroes are coming out of a long history of pulp horror and suspense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T08:17:47-08:00","id":831041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=831024#post831024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b><i>Comics</i></b> were themselves inspired by classic horror books. The Incredible Hulk is just Dr. Jekyll &amp; Mr. Hyde reskinned. Horror comics dominated the comics market all the way through the early '60s. Our (now) traditional notions of superheroes are coming out of a long history of pulp horror and suspense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everything old is new again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:56:19-08:00","id":833670,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this was answered, and it probably isn't a priority for the writers of Deviant at all, but I'm still curious:<br /> <br /> Where do Deviants fit in the whole Kinship scheme for Beasts? Descended from the Dark Mother? Fundamentally Human? Does Not Apply?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:53:40-08:00","id":833713,"title":"","content":"If it's anything like the others, I'd guess the Beasts will sense a connection with the Organization, view them as unknowing admirers of the Dark Mother, and Deviants as wayward souls who they feel should embrace their creators to get closer to the Dark Mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-20-2016, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:58:25-08:00","id":833715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=833670#post833670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this was answered, and it probably isn't a priority for the writers of Deviant at all, but I'm still curious:<br /> <br /> Where do Deviants fit in the whole Kinship scheme for Beasts? Descended from the Dark Mother? Fundamentally Human? Does Not Apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the guidelines Beast presents and bearing in mind the utter dearth of available metaphysics and/or template-based complications, I'd guess Fundamentally Human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T22:34:40-08:00","id":833720,"title":"","content":"I think they'd be kin considering changelings and mortals with supernatural merits are kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:30:28-08:00","id":833997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=833713#post833713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's anything like the others, I'd guess the Beasts will sense a connection with the Organization, view them as unknowing admirers of the Dark Mother, and Deviants as wayward souls who they feel should embrace their creators to get closer to the Dark Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to the first, not really to the second. <br /> <br /> Given how Cheiron is one of the Deviant guilds, I would say many Deviant creators are motivated by fear of the supernatural, creating Kin to kill Kin. That's going to leave a sour taste in the mouths of the Begotten, even before one realizes how much pain a Deviant is forced through.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine they'd view Deviants as abused cousins who finally have the capacity to break free of the cycle-they probably encourage Deviants to embrace their mutant nature, that it does make them better than humans in at least some ways. It is, after all, karma on the humans who abandoned their compassion and took away others' humanity-Fear of Justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T20:16:17-08:00","id":836195,"title":"","content":"I am so pumped for this game oh god<br /> <br /> I've even started coming up with seeds for homebrew ideas based on what little we know. I had the idea for a sort of Deviant power amplifier that works by allowing the Deviant to enter a sort of controlled Blowout state- in terms of power, it's between their normal state and Blowout-level power, with a cost, but one that's less than the risks of a full Blowout. <br /> <br /> This &quot;Stabilizer&quot; can take many forms based on the Deviant. It can be a suit of armor, an implant, a drug, or even a meditation regimen. Stabilizers can fail, however, catapulting the user into a full Blowout state. <br /> <br /> I figure this setup has precedent in various deviant-inspirational works, and has a lot of potential for drama and plot seeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:41:27-08:00","id":838420,"title":"","content":"I wonder how bizarre you can get with Deviant. Can you go full <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PRli1rRMoSQ\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Earthworm Jim</b></a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T07:07:19-08:00","id":846060,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting that I\u2019ve seen multiple threads on possible new ChroD games mention the Gill-Man and the Invisible Man as the only \u201cClassic Universal Monsters\u201d that don\u2019t have a ChroD line yet due to being too specific <br /> And now we have Beast and Deviant, both designed as umbrella games to essentially cover multiple subtypes of monsters too specific for their own game\u2026and each of the two lines is a perfect fit for one of those two","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:44:41-08:00","id":846086,"title":"","content":"Deviant not only covers the Invisible Man, but also Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde, yet another classical universal monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:30:58-08:00","id":846219,"title":"","content":"I wonder how they'll represent the instability of Deviant powers. In most cases, if you spend your Fuelstat and get the minimal Successes for the situation, you perform as intended without further complications. But what if your powers weren't so predictable? It's likely that emotional triggers will be common, like in the case of the Hulk and Stephen King's Carrie. Another possibility is that Deviants get their powers from serving dark gods. When they disobey the commands of their masters, their powers might lash out at them. When these Deviants enter the Blowout mode, they might be essentially turning into an avatar of their god, making people freeze in terror and bow without knowing why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:14:57-08:00","id":846469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=846219#post846219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility is that Deviants get their powers from serving dark gods. When they disobey the commands of their masters, their powers might lash out at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an antagonist in deviant, since your meant to be fighting against your creators, not serving them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:40:15-07:00","id":846630,"title":"","content":"I hope we get sufficiently non-scientific options for Deviants. While the evil experiments and mutagenic whatevers so quickly come to mind, I'd much rather play the survivor of a cult sacrifice or what have you.<br /> <br /> Do we have any word on Deviant being crossover-friendly? Weren't specific Hunter groups mentioned in the past?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-13-2016, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:19:23-07:00","id":846671,"title":"","content":"I'm reasonably sure Dave Brookshaw has said that there will be occult and non-science oriented Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:24:40-07:00","id":846676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=846671#post846671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably sure Dave Brookshaw has said that there will be occult and non-science oriented Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps Outsider: the Calling can find new life as a Deviant reskin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:41:15-07:00","id":846681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=846676#post846676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then perhaps Outsider: the Calling can find new life as a Deviant reskin.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMGOMGOMG<br /> <br /> I hadn't even thought of that possibility. This game is going to be awesome!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T23:10:57-07:00","id":846954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=846630#post846630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope we get sufficiently non-scientific options for Deviants. While the evil experiments and mutagenic whatevers so quickly come to mind, I'd much rather play the survivor of a cult sacrifice or what have you.<br /> <br /> Do we have any word on Deviant being crossover-friendly? Weren't specific Hunter groups mentioned in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The listed inspirations for Deviant include a guy who reached enlightenment from a near death experience, a teenage girl possessed by a demonic spirit, and a guy who turned into metal because he pissed of a ghost, I'd say the only reason that scientific deviants get more attention is because scientific supersoldiers et al get more attention in pop culture.<br /> <br /> As for hunter groups, it was mentioned that they were hoping to include Cheiron as one of the usual suspects for deviant creation in the book, but it might not happen, they only have so much space to work with after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:13:30-07:00","id":847086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=846671#post846671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably sure Dave Brookshaw has said that there will be occult and non-science oriented Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's been definitively stated. &quot;Altars&quot; were cited as one of the tools with which Deviants might be made.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:47:59-07:00","id":851903,"title":"","content":"The bits of info we've got so far make it seem like Deviant creation is super flexible, and I really hope that's the case. With the wide range of origins they've mentioned, and how it seems they can be established canon groups (Cheiron) or originals (new orgs that the book will mention, cults, &quot;my character accidentally became the brundlefly while trying to cure cancer in his garage&quot;), I'm guessing that character creation isn't so much splat/mechanics based as coming up with your backstory and origin and using a more toolbox-y set of mechanics to represent it. <br /> <br /> So I could see there being X-Splats that represent archetypes, but with multiple possible origins. So there's a &quot;cyborg&quot; splat, but that could the the result of mad science, God-Machine cultists, etc. <br /> <br /> With the flexibility it looks like we'll have, I can't wait to tinker with it and come up with Deviants created by existing splats and organizations (like how Promethean had Vamp/Werewolf/Mage-made prometheans, and how fans have made more for other splats). So far, I have:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Ordo Dracul-developed &quot;superghoul&quot;. Heavy on gothic pseudoscience. <br /> Mage: Honestly, each individual Path has multiple ways they'd go about this. Maybe it just started as an experiment in creating sleepwalkers or trying to isolate a &quot;paradox witness&quot; gene?<br /> Hunter: Came up earlier in the thread- essentially, a hunter becomes a deviant when they go a little overboard with their endowment. Or, as someone put it, &quot;when thaumatech implants take a little too well&quot;.<br /> Promethean: Most Prometheans try to deal with the curses of their condition by becoming more like humans. What happens when one decides to see if he can make humans more like Prometheans?<br /> Changeling: Blurs the lines a bit, since changelings and deviants are already quite alike. I could see changelings trying to create their own changelings, and getting a deviant out of it. Or, some sort of cold-iron Fae-hunter cyborg. <br /> Demon: &quot;make humans more like demons&quot; is already listed as a possible goal for a demon, soooo...<br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T12:06:43-07:00","id":851914,"title":"","content":"The Circle of the Crone could use the Blood of the Crone from the Mother's Army section in Danse Macabre to create new Igigi. The Edimmu were basically vampire Deviants to begin with, a vampire chosen and placed in a pit, eyes removed while the Nanaja summoned spirits from across the void and bound them to his Beast. And, naturally, while it served its original purpose and killed En Isiratuu, after that they reproduced wildly and almost wiped out all vampires.<br /> .<br /> The Ivory Claws could have failed genetic experiments in an attempt to recreate Father Wolf or other Firstborn. Shartha could have something similar, with their progenitors. The Book of the Beasts relied heavily on the concept of a messiah, it's not inconceivable that they might try to jump start it. Fire-Touched might try to create fully half-spirit beings to supplant mankind. Hunters in the Darkness might have rites to turn people into sentinels or shartha-traps. The Ghost Wolves could do anything.<br /> <br /> I imagine most of it won't lean on the other splats in the way Beast did, but who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:09:54-07:00","id":851950,"title":"","content":"One could imagine that Osirans are the result of crudely imitating the Rite of Return on a corpse, but could a Deviant result from someone still living? You come to on an altar, surrounding by chanting cultists gripping knives, their faces hidden by masks of the sacred animals, and use the fraction of s god's strength that rests wherenyour heart once was to escape...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:24:43-07:00","id":852052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=851950#post851950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could imagine that Osirans are the result of crudely imitating the Rite of Return on a corpse, but could a Deviant result from someone still living? You come to on an altar, surrounding by chanting cultists gripping knives, their faces hidden by masks of the sacred animals, and use the fraction of s god's strength that rests wherenyour heart once was to escape...</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that the judges are very much against mummies doing much magical experimentation, especially of that kind...meaning that when a mummy turns against them, they're quite likely to attempt it, because of the &quot;what don't they want me to know?&quot; factor. I'd imagine plenty of them REALLY wish they knew more about how the Rite actually worked, after all, and what better way to study it then trying to replicate it?<br /> <br /> Minor templates were also mentioned earlier, and you could get a lot of deviant ideas from &quot;what happens when you make a minor template major&quot;. For example, a skinchanger frustrated with their limited shapeshifting who goes in search of ancient rituals that would allow them to become a true shapeshifter, or to turn into any animal, or so on. Or a mortal psychic abducted and experimented on, given cybernetic implants in an attempt to make them even more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 03-23-2016, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T23:03:58-07:00","id":852256,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with other splats making deviants is that they have to be able to fight their makers without getting stomped into the ground and with deviants being the weakest splat makes that a problem <br /> <br /> I did think of a deviant made by a mummy's cult too. Except in mine the Mummy was going to become a twice arisen but the high priest botched it intentionally/ was manipulated, so that when the Arisen entered the body they found its original soul there refusing to give up and die. The mummy's Sekem couldn't be contained in a vessel that was already filled. There was enough Sekem to revive the deviant but most of it left their body in a great stream swallowed by an object held in the high preist's hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:15:50-07:00","id":852532,"title":"","content":"I don't really think that's an insurmountable problem. After all, devs have said that Deviants are stronger than Hunters, and Hunters are expected to be able to take on the other splats via tactics, preparation, and exploitation of weaknesses. If you think you can only have a good Deviant story if the Deviant could beat up whoever created them in a one on one arena match, well, that's a bit limiting. Besides, &quot;weakest splat&quot; is relative. The Astounding Human Flamethrower, for example, would probably do pretty well against a lot of vampires in a direct fight. <br /> <br /> That reminds me, anyone have any Dark Era ideas? Maybe something in the earlier half of the twentieth century? Modern Deviant has a biopunk/splatterpunk vibe, but the core concept lends itself very well to retro &quot;universal horror&quot;, pulp scifi, and silver age comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:01:27-07:00","id":852553,"title":"","content":"And if a Deviant is based on a supernatural, it's likely to have powers relating to the supernatural. The Edimmu, for instance, could instill a hunger to commit diablerie in its targets. Committing diablerie on an edimmu killed the diablerist and effectively allowed the edimmu to breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:31:55-07:00","id":852568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, anyone have any Dark Era ideas? Maybe something in the earlier half of the twentieth century? Modern Deviant has a biopunk/splatterpunk vibe, but the core concept lends itself very well to retro &quot;universal horror&quot;, pulp scifi, and silver age comics.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm leaning towards Victorian London. The era just speaks to a sort of &quot;Gothic Mad Science&quot; that I feel would possibly be conductive to what little we know of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:03:57-07:00","id":852584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=852532#post852532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, anyone have any Dark Era ideas? Maybe something in the earlier half of the twentieth century? Modern Deviant has a biopunk/splatterpunk vibe, but the core concept lends itself very well to retro &quot;universal horror&quot;, pulp scifi, and silver age comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will, as always, suggest Meiji Restoration Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:58:02-07:00","id":852619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=852584#post852584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will, as always, suggest Meiji Restoration Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meiji Japan has to be Werewolf. I won't let any other game have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:32:32-07:00","id":852653,"title":"","content":"Any number of mythic and heroic eras could be interesting. &quot;Heroes&quot; such as Heracles or Cu Chulainn could easily be Deviants.<br /> <br /> Or turn of the century Lovecraft Country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:10:23-07:00","id":852685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=852653#post852653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any number of mythic and heroic eras could be interesting. &quot;Heroes&quot; such as Heracles or Cu Chulainn could easily be Deviants.<br /> <br /> Or turn of the century Lovecraft Country.</div> </div> </div> </div> My go-to video games for Lovecraftian imagery, body horror and Gothic Mad Science would be Splatterhouse and Bloodborne. I'd like to see Sumerian, Nordic and Mongolian Deviants that were seen as demigods. Alternatively, monstrous affronts to the nature of world created by consorting with monsters or stealing artifacts from gods. Speaking of C\u00fa Chulainn, take a look at the description of his warp-spasm from the Wikipedia article:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first warp-spasm seized C\u00fachulainn, and made him into a monstrous thing, hideous and shapeless, unheard of. His shanks and his joints, every knuckle and angle and organ from head to foot, shook like a tree in the flood or a reed in the stream. His body made a furious twist inside his skin, so that his feet and shins switched to the rear and his heels and calves switched to the front... On his head the temple-sinews stretched to the nape of his neck, each mighty, immense, measureless knob as big as the head of a month-old child... he sucked one eye so deep into his head that a wild crane couldn't probe it onto his cheek out of the depths of his skull; the other eye fell out along his cheek. His mouth weirdly distorted: his cheek peeled back from his jaws until the gullet appeared, his lungs and his liver flapped in his mouth and throat, his lower jaw struck the upper a lion-killing blow, and fiery flakes large as a ram's fleece reached his mouth from his throat... The hair of his head twisted like the tangle of a red thornbush stuck in a gap; if a royal apple tree with all its kingly fruit were shaken above him, scarce an apple would reach the ground but each would be spiked on a bristle of his hair as it stood up on his scalp with rage. </div> </div> </div>If that isn't a Blowout Mode, I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-24-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T00:24:31-07:00","id":853371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=852532#post852532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think that's an insurmountable problem. After all, devs have said that Deviants are stronger than Hunters, and Hunters are expected to be able to take on the other splats via tactics, preparation, and exploitation of weaknesses. If you think you can only have a good Deviant story if the Deviant could beat up whoever created them in a one on one arena match, well, that's a bit limiting. Besides, &quot;weakest splat&quot; is relative. The Astounding Human Flamethrower, for example, would probably do pretty well against a lot of vampires in a direct fight.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is no fair comparison to Hunter here, in this scenario the deviants are the prey. <br /> <br /> Hunters go on offensive, that's where their power lies- outnumbering their prey, attacking when they are weak, using their weaknesses against them, etc.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what the vampires, or mages, etc, etc, etc, would be doing to the Deviant they would be hunting down.<br /> <br /> Mr Flamethrower's powers won't mean jack when a vampire dominates his waitress to slip sedatives in his coffee, use obfuscate to frame him for a cop killing, or you know just send a dozen thralls with fire extinguishers to take away the deviant's one advantage, or any of the other billion things an organization of supernaturals could do here. <br /> <br /> From the description, it seems pretty plain that deviants are supposed to pit their superior abilities against the resources and manpower of inferior opponents. <br /> <br /> Giving the enemy that already has superior manpower and resources superior powers as well leaves the deviant screwed six ways to Sunday, especially since any organization of supernaturals can probably leverage their supernatural powers into superior resources and manpower too. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:58:02-07:00","id":853473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=852568#post852568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm leaning towards Victorian London. The era just speaks to a sort of &quot;Gothic Mad Science&quot; that I feel would possibly be conductive to what little we know of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. Though if they appear in two eras, the other must be pre-industrial and to take account of the game's occult potential. Maybe Warring States China, with attempts at Taoist alchemy and Wuxia martial arts going badly wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:23:55-07:00","id":853553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=853371#post853371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no fair comparison to Hunter here, in this scenario the deviants are the prey. <br /> <br /> Hunters go on offensive, that's where their power lies- outnumbering their prey, attacking when they are weak, using their weaknesses against them, etc.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what the vampires, or mages, etc, etc, etc, would be doing to the Deviant they would be hunting down.<br /> <br /> Mr Flamethrower's powers won't mean jack when a vampire dominates his waitress to slip sedatives in his coffee, use obfuscate to frame him for a cop killing, or you know just send a dozen thralls with fire extinguishers to take away the deviant's one advantage, or any of the other billion things an organization of supernaturals could do here. <br /> <br /> From the description, it seems pretty plain that deviants are supposed to pit their superior abilities against the resources and manpower of inferior opponents. <br /> <br /> Giving the enemy that already has superior manpower and resources superior powers as well leaves the deviant screwed six ways to Sunday, especially since any organization of supernaturals can probably leverage their supernatural powers into superior resources and manpower too. </div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I guess that's one way to think about it? See, it's ultimately a ST/player issue. If the players and the ST agree that they want to run a chronicle where the PCs are connected to a supernatural organization, there are certainly ways to run that so it works out well. A good ST would be able to work with it, not go &quot;fuck you, you can't win&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:03:57-07:00","id":853607,"title":"","content":"Damn my current internet situation!<br /> <br /> Let see, mad science eras. Victorian London is a classic. 15th-16th century Germany or Switzerland. 19th century Italy and USA (electricity experiments on the bodies and obviously Nickola Tesla). World War 1 (introduction to chemical warfare), Word War 2 (Apemen experiments, UFO tech, the Philadelphia experiment, infrasound). Cold War (drug tests, psychic research, memory implantation).<br /> <br /> Probably old news. Types of Deviants: Jekylls (self experimentation. Dr. Jekyll/Mr. Hyde, the Invisible Man), Virals/Mutants/Mutos/Mutates (genentically modified. Prototype, BioShock Splicers), Cybers/Borgs (cybernetically enhanced. Virus, Terminator), Chems (chemical exposure. Return of the Living Dead (ironically), Re-Animator), Rads (classic Atomic Age catch all: The Incredible Melting Mad, Godzilla).<br /> <br /> For the Subtitle: Tormented, Experminted, Reviled, Exposed, Maltreated, Subjugated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:33:25-07:00","id":853680,"title":"","content":"Cold War has to make it in there somewhere. I'm a sucker for all sorts of shadowy government conspiracies and the actual history there is rife with opportunities for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:51:15-07:00","id":853743,"title":"","content":"I think deviant would make an awesome tv series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:35:08-07:00","id":853790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=853743#post853743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think deviant would make an awesome tv series.</div> </div> </div> </div>It already has. At least, if you take the various inspirational materials that Deviant is modelling as examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:05:55-07:00","id":854311,"title":"","content":"I would like to add Bioshock/System Shock, Metal Gear, Deus Ex and Eclipse Phase to the list of inspirational material, if they haven't been mentioned already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:52:48-07:00","id":854329,"title":"","content":"You know what? Instead of trying to remember all the Deviant-like stories I've seen, I'll point to the TV Tropes articles on <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Transhuman\" target=\"_blank\">transhumanism</a></b> and <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CyberPunk\" target=\"_blank\">cyberpunk.</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-27-2016, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T07:20:10-07:00","id":854462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/608073-deviant-the-subtitle-discussion?p=853607#post853607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably old news. Types of Deviants: Jekylls (self experimentation. Dr. Jekyll/Mr. Hyde, the Invisible Man), Virals/Mutants/Mutos/Mutates (genentically modified. Prototype, BioShock Splicers), Cybers/Borgs (cybernetically enhanced. Virus, Terminator), Chems (chemical exposure. Return of the Living Dead (ironically), Re-Animator), Rads (classic Atomic Age catch all: The Incredible Melting Mad, Godzilla).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the splats, if they have them, will be about the why not the how. Experiment in the see what happens sense, experiment in the try to produce this effect sense, accident, infection, things like that. I think the how will show up in their abilities,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the Subtitle: Tormented, Experminted, Reviled, Exposed, Maltreated, Subjugated. </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping for Marked. Represents the alteration, the fact that most of their abilities are &quot;physically obvious,&quot; and how they're hunted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count"